https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/57c9a44ee2a35e11e77a938c6de4654ef5294b1b","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDU3YzlhNDRlZTJhMzVlMTFlNzdhOTM4YzZkZTQ2NTRlZjUyOTRiMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/2bd2de47c30fe3d77c27cf29d3cf7f01b66cab4d","sha":"2bd2de47c30fe3d77c27cf29d3cf7f01b66cab4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/2bd2de47c30fe3d77c27cf29d3cf7f01b66cab4d"}],"sha":"57c9a44ee2a35e11e77a938c6de4654ef5294b1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/57c9a44ee2a35e11e77a938c6de4654ef5294b1b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/2bd2de47c30fe3d77c27cf29d3cf7f01b66cab4d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T16:36:14Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T16:36:14Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"message":"Drop LRPS 584729320 from link tracking\n\nIt was never a Training Course link. LRPS''s own LTI id_token names it\nresource_link.title \"Test 1\" with target_link_uri \"https://skillproof.training\"\n-- the bare site root, with no ?course= binding. So it resolves to no Course and\nno Skill; it drops the launcher wherever their own account already has standing,\nwhich is why it read as an instructor link (an instructor account was the only\none that got through) and why nothing could ever name it.\n\nIts id is lower than all four PROD links (584731391/462/527/569) and Mike\nHassett already had it on 25 AUG 2026, ten days before that batch was\nprovisioned -- consistent with it being the first provisioning attempt for PROD,\nwhich LRPS itself recorded as \"Test 1\".\n\nMike''s note at the time, \"it doesn''t seem to fully provision\", was correct. JFT\ntested it and reported it working, which was also true and answered a different\nquestion: it authenticates and launches, it just points nowhere in particular.\nAn incomplete provisioning record is not something this list should publish as\na Skill, so it goes. Fixing it properly is a WGU D&D ticket (add the course\nbinding), not a JFT one.\n\n49 -> 48 rows. PROD keeps its four real links, all measured Up.\n\nRemoving the corresponding Docs row is UI work: sh_write.py has no delete\noperation in any mode, by design.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"395308e983e42f0eeacc5d250cf56e0f2ec95202","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/395308e983e42f0eeacc5d250cf56e0f2ec95202"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/2bd2de47c30fe3d77c27cf29d3cf7f01b66cab4d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/2bd2de47c30fe3d77c27cf29d3cf7f01b66cab4d","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDJiZDJkZTQ3YzMwZmUzZDc3YzI3Y2YyOWQzY2Y3ZjAxYjY2Y2FiNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/118fff240c7a837c1334745ecb77ba7aa7216082","sha":"118fff240c7a837c1334745ecb77ba7aa7216082","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/118fff240c7a837c1334745ecb77ba7aa7216082"}],"sha":"2bd2de47c30fe3d77c27cf29d3cf7f01b66cab4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/2bd2de47c30fe3d77c27cf29d3cf7f01b66cab4d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/118fff240c7a837c1334745ecb77ba7aa7216082/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:59:42Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:59:42Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"message":"Use the platform''s own Skill names, not hand-shortened labels\n\nThe labels were Brady''s abbreviations, and they had stopped doing the one job a\nlabel has: \"Python\", \"Calc\", \"E010\", \"Applied UX\", \"Professionalism\" and\n\"Teaching Engineering\" name nothing you can find in SkillProof, and searching\n\"Python\" in the platform returns everything.\n\n32 of 49 rows renamed to the name the platform itself reports, with the course\ncode kept in front where one exists:\n\n  Python                 -> Introduction to Python\n  Calc                   -> Introduction to Calculus\n  E010                   -> E010 · Foundations of Programming (Python)\n  Applied UX             -> Applied UX Research for Real-World Practice\n  Professionalism        -> Foundations of Professionalism in Technology Environments\n  Teaching Engineering   -> Teaching Engineering Concepts to Engineering Students\n  D522-08 File Metadata  -> D522-08 · Python Basics for IT Automation: File Metadata & Copying Files\n\nWhere the names came from. The LRPS provisioning id cannot be resolved to a\nSkill name through any admin route reachable here:\n/tenant-admin/dashboard?tenantId= answers 403 \"You are not associated with any\ntenant\" even for a Super Admin, which contradicts Access Control v1.3 §3.1\n(\"Super Admins ... see everything\") and is a defect, filed separately. But a\nstudent launch ENROLLS the account in the Skill, and /users/me returns\nenrollments[].course with {id, name, slug, description, topics}. Enrollments\naccumulate, so one account names every Skill it has launched, and the slug in\neach link''s ?course= joins name to link exactly -- no positional guessing.\nEvery one of the 32 was measured from a live authenticated launch.\n\nWhy the course code stays in front. The platform names are long and 13 of them\nshare their first 31 characters, so in the Docs table -- which sorts by Status,\nnot course order -- twelve of fourteen rows were indistinguishable before the\ntext wrapped. Measured at the real 52-character column width: the prefix costs\n8 characters on average and zero extra lines, and it is the only form where a\nrow identifies itself on its first line. The label is still a superstring of\nthe platform name, so a search for either the name or the code finds it.\n\nNot renamed, deliberately: the 9 staff portal rows and 4 demo walkthroughs are\nnot Skills; DEV''s 4 rows cannot be enumerated (hosts down, LTI registrations\nstale) and a STAGE name must not be assumed to hold in a separate database;\nand PROD \"Training Course\" is an instructor link carrying no ?course= slug, so\nan instructor session has no enrollment to read it from.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7423d1ad7b85a67461116defd10dc7f9d85e809a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/7423d1ad7b85a67461116defd10dc7f9d85e809a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/118fff240c7a837c1334745ecb77ba7aa7216082","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/118fff240c7a837c1334745ecb77ba7aa7216082","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDExOGZmZjI0MGM3YTgzN2MxMzM0NzQ1ZWNiNzdiYTdhYTcyMTYwODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/999c3080a510cf684093a066472ef438f8b5b59d","sha":"999c3080a510cf684093a066472ef438f8b5b59d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/999c3080a510cf684093a066472ef438f8b5b59d"}],"sha":"118fff240c7a837c1334745ecb77ba7aa7216082","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/118fff240c7a837c1334745ecb77ba7aa7216082"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/999c3080a510cf684093a066472ef438f8b5b59d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:21:40Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T15:21:40Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"message":"Add the two R002 STAGE Skills to the published link list\n\nBoth went live on SkillProof STAGE with LRPS provisioning links and JFT\ndirect-launch URLs, and appeared on neither published surface.\n\n  589890481  R002 - Syntactic Awareness and Grammar\n  589890634  R002 - Writing Measurable Learning Objectives\n\n47 -> 49 rows. Names are the platform''s OWN course names, read from\n/users/me enrollments[].course.name on an authenticated student launch, not\nhand-shortened labels -- both Skills live in School of Education Demo. The\nplatform spells them with a hyphen, not the em dash the other course-level\nrows use, so they are recorded verbatim rather than normalised.\n\nBoth measured Up, reproduced. 589890634 returned FAIL_AUTH at PingFederate on\ntwo attempts and RENDERED_OK on three; every failure was on student account\nindex 1, never on the link, so the account is the fault and is being chased\nseparately. Never trust a first-pass failure here.\n\nbuild_links.py: merge_status() now reads a per-verdict measurement time from\nthe sentry store''s new verdictsAt map, falling back to the scope''s `at` for\nverdicts written before it existed. The scope''s `at` is the last WRITE time,\nand partial sweeps now merge into a scope rather than replacing it, so reading\nit for every verdict would stamp old measurements with today''s timestamp and\npublish them as freshly measured.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e31303eab3da69ed78cdcd71383808bbfe44fd80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/e31303eab3da69ed78cdcd71383808bbfe44fd80"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/999c3080a510cf684093a066472ef438f8b5b59d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/999c3080a510cf684093a066472ef438f8b5b59d","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDk5OWMzMDgwYTUxMGNmNjg0MDkzYTA2NjQ3MmVmNDM4ZjhiNWI1OWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/e432c35992e8e2a9d4ef78b22bc38493fd53447c","sha":"e432c35992e8e2a9d4ef78b22bc38493fd53447c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/e432c35992e8e2a9d4ef78b22bc38493fd53447c"}],"sha":"999c3080a510cf684093a066472ef438f8b5b59d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/999c3080a510cf684093a066472ef438f8b5b59d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/e432c35992e8e2a9d4ef78b22bc38493fd53447c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T20:58:31Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T20:58:31Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"message":"Remove D522-13 from link tracking\n\nIts LRPS record is broken upstream and the row was publishing as red on a\nworld-readable page with no route to a fix from here. Dropped from\nskills.json (48 -> 47 rows), from the rendered index.html, and from the\nprivate overlay''s byId map (44 -> 43).\n\nCorrected two stale README claims while removing the references:\n\n- \"D522-13''s course slug still reads building-small-pro from an earlier\n  renaming test - link works, label is correct, slug is cosmetic-only\"\n  contradicted line 53 of the same file, and was measured false on\n  10 SEP 2026. An authenticated probe failed at\n  lrpsltilaunchservice.wgu.edu/v1/lti_login/577932056, before SkillProof\n  was reached.\n- The landing row said 43 live rows across five section names the page\n  stopped using when it was reorganized by environment. Now 47, with the\n  old names marked historical.\n\nThe rename did not break the SkillProof side. Slugs freeze at creation and\ndo not follow a rename, so the Skill stayed named after paramiko & netmiko\nwhile keeping the building-small-pro slug, and its own ltiConfig\ntargetLinkUri still matched the recorded link exactly. The fault sits in\nWGU''s LRPS provisioning record, which is what LOG-033/034 already said.\n\nThe Skill is still live on STAGE. Archiving is blocked: the control is\naria-disabled with \"Only the skill owner can archive this skill\", and the\nSuper Admin course detail exposes no Archive control at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b0434f4ca0e9919ab825da66c3ae9984273f85a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/b0434f4ca0e9919ab825da66c3ae9984273f85a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/e432c35992e8e2a9d4ef78b22bc38493fd53447c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/e432c35992e8e2a9d4ef78b22bc38493fd53447c","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKGU0MzJjMzU5OTJlOGUyYTlkNGVmNzhiMjJiYzM4NDkzZmQ1MzQ0N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/b1152c567b7eb1711ccef4e21d7663e8c11bfcba","sha":"b1152c567b7eb1711ccef4e21d7663e8c11bfcba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/b1152c567b7eb1711ccef4e21d7663e8c11bfcba"}],"sha":"e432c35992e8e2a9d4ef78b22bc38493fd53447c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/e432c35992e8e2a9d4ef78b22bc38493fd53447c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/b1152c567b7eb1711ccef4e21d7663e8c11bfcba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T19:52:18Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T19:52:18Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"message":"Measure all 44 LRPS links, not one per persona\n\nThe nightly auth suite probed 4 links per environment, so 32 of the 44\npublished statuses were hand-typed on both surfaces. A full sweep now\ndrives from the private overlay''s byId map and probes every published\nlink with a real SSO login, taking measured coverage from 12 to 44.\n\nmerge_status() accepts the per-link store key. The sweep keys verdicts\nas auth::<env>::<persona>::<lrpsId>, because 35 stage student links all\ncarry target=''student'' and collapsed onto one key, losing 34 results and\nhiding whether a link had appeared or been retired. The old three-part\nper-persona key is still read, and is applied only to ids the per-link\nsweep did not measure so one persona-wide verdict cannot stamp itself\nacross 32 rows.\n\nMeasured 10 SEP 2026, and three rows moved from Unknown to Up:\nstage Python, PROD School Admin, PROD Training Course.\n\nPROD Training Course is an INSTRUCTOR link. It had no recorded persona\nand no captured direct-launch URL, so it was probed as a student, failed\nat PingFederate, and sat at Unknown. Forcing each persona showed it\nrenders 2 Courses / 85 Skills as instructor and as School Admin. The\npersona is now recorded.\n\nStill down, both reproduced on a paced re-probe: all four DEV links\nreturn \"Tool not found\" from the LTI service, and stage D522-13 fails at\nthe LRPS launch service.\n\nA first concurrent sweep produced 17 failures. Eleven were HTTP 429 from\nmy own concurrency, not broken links, and would have published as red.\nFailures are now re-probed serially before they count.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e024a2491d2d04801b343bbe8c2aa286f554b67d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/e024a2491d2d04801b343bbe8c2aa286f554b67d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/b1152c567b7eb1711ccef4e21d7663e8c11bfcba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/b1152c567b7eb1711ccef4e21d7663e8c11bfcba","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKGIxMTUyYzU2N2I3ZWIxNzExY2NlZjRlMjFkNzY2M2U4YzExYmZjYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/1513d7dc7ac6fc6406c4e0df387e9dee1efcb6e6","sha":"1513d7dc7ac6fc6406c4e0df387e9dee1efcb6e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/1513d7dc7ac6fc6406c4e0df387e9dee1efcb6e6"}],"sha":"b1152c567b7eb1711ccef4e21d7663e8c11bfcba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/b1152c567b7eb1711ccef4e21d7663e8c11bfcba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/1513d7dc7ac6fc6406c4e0df387e9dee1efcb6e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T18:35:14Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T18:35:14Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"message":"Move the site onto Brady''s design system\n\nFour pages -- the landing page, the One-Slide Pitch, the Status Demo Deck and\na new Full Walkthrough page -- now share assets/brady.css, a token layer built\nfrom the brady-document-style skill''s design-system.md: WGU FY26 brand\nanchors, the BS_ semantic palette, the editorial neutral ramp, Aptos Display,\nand the 4px spacing grid.\n\nThe colour barely moved, and that is the finding rather than a shortfall. The\npages already used #001730, #0070F0, #46B1EF and #EEF6F9 -- the exact FY26\nanchors -- because the vendor copied this design. What actually changed is the\nvocabulary: Paragon token names and component classes are gone, generic greys\n(#E6E6E6..#1A1A1A) became the editorial neutrals, and the Google Material\nIcons webfont is replaced by an inline SVG sprite, so no page makes a remote\nrequest to a third-party design system any more.\n\nThe landing page also gains an editorial masthead: an eyebrow with a BS_TAWNY\nkicker rule, a fluid 44-72px H1 with tighter tracking, and a hairline with\nreal whitespace above the table. A warmer BS_CREAM treatment was mocked up and\nrejected -- side by side, the typography carried nearly all of the gain and\nthe cream was barely perceptible, so it was not worth a hand-derived dark\npalette to maintain.\n\nLight and dark both work on all four pages, with the theme restored in <head>\nrather than at the end of <body>, where it could not prevent the flash.\n\nEvery contrast pairing was measured with a checker that composites alpha over\nthe real backdrop; three earlier ad-hoc checks reported wrong numbers by\nmeasuring against rgba(0,0,0,0). Six real failures were found and fixed, among\nthem the LRPS id at 4.19:1 (design-system.md 1.5 rates BLUE on a blue tint as\nAA for large text only, and that is 12px mono) and the count chip at 3.48:1.\n\nbuild_links.py moved in lockstep, since it emits the divider and copy-button\nmarkup. Its round-trip stayed byte-exact at every step, which is what proves\nthe generator and the page never diverged.\n\nThe walkthrough page replaces a sidebar link that pointed straight at a 41 MB\n.mp4. It has a poster frame captured with Playwright, since ffmpeg is not\ninstalled here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee43df375f36e8ba4e96348d44ef1b14b3368c17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/ee43df375f36e8ba4e96348d44ef1b14b3368c17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/1513d7dc7ac6fc6406c4e0df387e9dee1efcb6e6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/1513d7dc7ac6fc6406c4e0df387e9dee1efcb6e6","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDE1MTNkN2RjN2FjNmZjNjQwNmM0ZTBkZjM4N2U5ZGVlMWVmY2I2ZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/d9576480cf5c1e42c2c44590eb8a0197920e6298","sha":"d9576480cf5c1e42c2c44590eb8a0197920e6298","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/d9576480cf5c1e42c2c44590eb8a0197920e6298"}],"sha":"1513d7dc7ac6fc6406c4e0df387e9dee1efcb6e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/1513d7dc7ac6fc6406c4e0df387e9dee1efcb6e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/d9576480cf5c1e42c2c44590eb8a0197920e6298/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:43:07Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:43:07Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"message":"Make the LINK column copyable without launching a tab\n\nThe row-click handler was bound to the whole <tr>, so every click in the LINK\ncolumn opened a new tab. Copying a URL to paste into a private window -- to\nsign in as a different test account and show someone that experience -- meant\nctrl-dragging carefully through the text and getting an unwanted tab anyway.\n\nThree changes, together:\n\n  - The LINK cell is now a real anchor. Right-click \"Copy link address\",\n    ctrl-click and middle-click all behave the way a link should, which they\n    could not when the cell was plain text under a row handler.\n  - A copy button beside it puts the full URL on the clipboard in one click,\n    with a check-mark confirmation. It stops propagation, so it copies without\n    opening anything.\n  - The row handler now ignores clicks inside the LINK cell entirely, and\n    ignores any click that ends a text selection, so finishing a drag-select\n    anywhere in the row no longer opens a tab.\n\nDetails that matter: an anchor drags as a link by default, which would have\nreplaced one selection problem with another, so the link text keeps\ndrag-to-select. The demo rows store a relative target (\"student/\") which is\nright for navigation and useless pasted into another browser, so the button\ncopies an absolute URL. The async clipboard needs a secure context, so there\nis an execCommand fallback for file:// . The button is a real <button> with an\naria-label and stays visible on focus, not hover only.\n\nVerified by driving it: the clipboard receives the exact URL, the copy click\nopens zero tabs, clicking the name cell still launches, and demo rows copy an\nabsolute address.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"66779f5eeb23204394fba52b4add00bda8b4e808","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/66779f5eeb23204394fba52b4add00bda8b4e808"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/d9576480cf5c1e42c2c44590eb8a0197920e6298","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/d9576480cf5c1e42c2c44590eb8a0197920e6298","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKGQ5NTc2NDgwY2Y1YzFlNDJjMmM0NDU5MGViOGEwMTk3OTIwZTYyOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/55c59b30ce028c075931eea9fd0ec94405b74e39","sha":"55c59b30ce028c075931eea9fd0ec94405b74e39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/55c59b30ce028c075931eea9fd0ec94405b74e39"}],"sha":"d9576480cf5c1e42c2c44590eb8a0197920e6298","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/d9576480cf5c1e42c2c44590eb8a0197920e6298"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/55c59b30ce028c075931eea9fd0ec94405b74e39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:33:40Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:33:40Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"message":"Separate student Skills from staff portals within each environment\n\nEach environment section now carries two audience sub-dividers: staff\nmanagement portals, then the Skills a student launches. Staff lead, because\nthe reader this page is written for is WGU staff.\n\nThe sub-divider is the section-divider idiom at a lighter weight -- no tint,\nno top rule, smaller and dimmer -- so it reads as subordinate to the\nenvironment header rather than competing with it. Three alternatives were\nmocked up and rejected: a coloured left stripe produced a boundary that was\nbarely perceptible, leaned on colour alone, and added a fourth colour beside\nthe status palette; a per-row icon labelled rows instead of grouping them,\nwhich on STAGE is 32 identical icons in a column.\n\nAudience is recorded per row in skills.json, not as a list of ids inside the\nrenderer, and rows are SORTED into group order rather than trusted to arrive\nin it. Adding a Skill stays one entry that declares what it is -- appended\nanywhere in the file, it still renders under the right heading. Verified with\na row added at the end of the file.\n\nThe demo section renders flat on purpose. Its four walkthroughs are one\nclick-through seen through four roles, not a student/staff split, and\ngrouping them would invent a distinction that is not there.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bfdea6ce412d499939c3a9f70f0b2cbbb6c5ae8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/bfdea6ce412d499939c3a9f70f0b2cbbb6c5ae8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/55c59b30ce028c075931eea9fd0ec94405b74e39","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/55c59b30ce028c075931eea9fd0ec94405b74e39","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDU1YzU5YjMwY2UwMjhjMDc1OTMxZWVhOWZkMGVjOTQ0MDViNzRlMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/f6c31bd6a5dce034feebe3b9bbae450b7dac2cb9","sha":"f6c31bd6a5dce034feebe3b9bbae450b7dac2cb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/f6c31bd6a5dce034feebe3b9bbae450b7dac2cb9"}],"sha":"55c59b30ce028c075931eea9fd0ec94405b74e39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/55c59b30ce028c075931eea9fd0ec94405b74e39"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/f6c31bd6a5dce034feebe3b9bbae450b7dac2cb9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:20:43Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:20:43Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"message":"Lead with PROD, and match the developer page''s status vocabulary\n\nSection order was DEV, STAGE, PROD -- pipeline order, which is a builder''s\nconvention. This page is a directory for colleagues, so it now runs PROD,\nSTAGE, DEV, with the no-login walkthroughs last. Four dead DEV links were\ngreeting every reader at the top while the live pilot sat below the fold.\n\nStatus labels and colours now match the Superhuman developer page exactly:\nUp / Unknown / Down, using that page''s select-option colours (#187B34,\n#8B6C1D, #A91E1E). Two vocabularies for one link across two pages made a\nreader work out whether \"Broken\" and \"Down\" meant the same thing.\n\nDown is red, where it was amber. Amber now carries Unknown, which is where\ncaution is the right reading -- a dead link showing caution-yellow understated\nit, and Unverified''s grey said \"no information\" about links we had measured.\n\nThose three hexes are picked for light backgrounds and go muddy on an 8px dot\nin the dark theme, so the dark theme lifts the same hues rather than leaving a\nstatus marker nobody can read. Checked in both.\n\nThe DEV section note said the LTI registrations are gone. True, but not the\nwhole story: measured 10 SEP 2026, the DEV hosts do not answer either --\nwgu-dev-api accepts TCP and never responds on 443 or 80, and wgu-dev serves a\ncertificate for another name. Two separate faults, and the note said one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"034d34c8af5cecafb3e2af8e99502e52bf24b4df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/034d34c8af5cecafb3e2af8e99502e52bf24b4df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/f6c31bd6a5dce034feebe3b9bbae450b7dac2cb9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/f6c31bd6a5dce034feebe3b9bbae450b7dac2cb9","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKGY2YzMxYmQ2YTVkY2UwMzRmZWViZTNiOWJiYWU0NTBiN2RhYzJjYjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/b5b1e3aace58373e539e00ade990eedcb2a296a1","sha":"b5b1e3aace58373e539e00ade990eedcb2a296a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/b5b1e3aace58373e539e00ade990eedcb2a296a1"}],"sha":"f6c31bd6a5dce034feebe3b9bbae450b7dac2cb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/f6c31bd6a5dce034feebe3b9bbae450b7dac2cb9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/b5b1e3aace58373e539e00ade990eedcb2a296a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:15:57Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:15:57Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"message":"Keep the status wording on this page as it was\n\nAn earlier pass in this session started aligning this page''s Status labels to\nthe developer page''s Up/Unknown/Down and adding a verdict strip above the\ntable. Both are reverted.\n\nThis page exists to hand colleagues links to SkillProof resources. Up/Down is\noperational vocabulary for the people running the environments, and a summary\nof what is broken is a monitoring view, not a directory. The developer page\ncarries both; this one does not need them.\n\nThe two surfaces still agree on the thing that matters: the same 44 LRPS\nlinks, same environments, same names, same underlying state. Only the wording\nof the state differs, deliberately.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6cb58ccb6a439fbb52c79bb8564434f2eeb3b002","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/6cb58ccb6a439fbb52c79bb8564434f2eeb3b002"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/b5b1e3aace58373e539e00ade990eedcb2a296a1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/b5b1e3aace58373e539e00ade990eedcb2a296a1","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKGI1YjFlM2FhY2U1ODM3M2U1MzllMDBhZGU5OTBlZWRjYjJhMjk2YTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/b56f20c35f9f7c3940394f6eeaa939967362ba8e","sha":"b56f20c35f9f7c3940394f6eeaa939967362ba8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/b56f20c35f9f7c3940394f6eeaa939967362ba8e"}],"sha":"b5b1e3aace58373e539e00ade990eedcb2a296a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/b5b1e3aace58373e539e00ade990eedcb2a296a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/b56f20c35f9f7c3940394f6eeaa939967362ba8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:06:56Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T17:06:56Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"message":"Sync the developer page by row, never by rebuilding it\n\nbuild_links.py --superhuman --publish used replace-all, which deletes every\ntable and recreates it. That was right exactly once, to convert 93 bullets\ninto tables. Run again it destroys the page: hand-built headings, renamed\ntables, select-list colours and every chart view built on those tables.\nIt is now hard-refused.\n\nsync_superhuman.py is the steady-state path. It changes Status cell VALUES in\nwhatever table already exists and leaves structure alone, so formatting\napplied in the UI survives. Tables are matched by parent page and column\nnames, never by table name, because those get renamed.\n\nFour things it has to get right, each found by getting it wrong first:\n\n  - The tables endpoint caps a page at 100 and this doc holds 259, so an\n    unpaginated read found none of ours and reported \"nothing to update\" --\n    a silent no-op, the worst way for a sync to fail.\n  - maintenance mode refuses payloads over 25 rows. It sends consecutive\n    batches under the cap rather than passing --confirm-large.\n  - Chart views carry the same column names as their base table, and writing\n    a row through a view writes through to the base, so views are excluded or\n    every cell is written twice.\n  - A value that is not one of the Status column''s select options is accepted\n    and rendered UNSTYLED -- success reported, colour silently lost. Any such\n    value is now skipped, naming the missing option.\n\nStatus wording moved to the private overlay (statusLabels) so renaming an\noption is a data edit. The Superhuman doc and page ids moved there too: they\nare internal identifiers and this repo is public.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"efdf6a4d2cd9c44f9acaa8840c964710fd357fb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/efdf6a4d2cd9c44f9acaa8840c964710fd357fb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/b56f20c35f9f7c3940394f6eeaa939967362ba8e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/b56f20c35f9f7c3940394f6eeaa939967362ba8e","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKGI1NmYyMGMzNWY5ZjdjMzk0MDM5NGY2ZWVhYTkzOTk2NzM2MmJhOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/53bc83947b37aa519fe561aed8fbfa482546fdf0","sha":"53bc83947b37aa519fe561aed8fbfa482546fdf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/53bc83947b37aa519fe561aed8fbfa482546fdf0"}],"sha":"b56f20c35f9f7c3940394f6eeaa939967362ba8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/b56f20c35f9f7c3940394f6eeaa939967362ba8e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/53bc83947b37aa519fe561aed8fbfa482546fdf0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:54:23Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:54:23Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn"},"message":"Reorganize the link list by server, and generate it from data\n\nThe 43 rows were grouped by release phase -- Alpha, Beta E010, Beta D522,\nStaff Portals -- labels that stopped describing anything once all three\nservers went live. They are now Dev / Stage / Prod, each holding that\nserver''s own staff portals AND its Skills, with the click-through demo left\nat the bottom as the no-login fallback.\n\nThe five PROD provisioning links appear here for the first time. They were\nalready in nightly use by the sentry runner but had never reached this page.\n\nBoth surfaces now compile from skills.json rather than being hand-edited in\ntwo formats. build_links.py follows build_prototypes.py''s contract: Python,\nrun at dev time, commits static HTML, no CI. It also renders the Superhuman\ndeveloper page, which keeps the Client IDs, OIDC/LTI endpoints and internal\nhostnames that must not appear here -- assert_clean() refuses to emit public\nHTML containing any of them, and the sidebar row count is derived rather\nthan typed.\n\nStatus becomes three-state. Active/Broken cannot express what the runner\nactually distinguishes: a dead registration versus a launch we could not\nverify because the test account was the wrong type. Publishing the second as\n\"Broken\" would mark a working link as failing on a public page, so those\nreport as Unverified instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"84304551dcd8cc29de3ca3ee5926e90004e29ffc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/84304551dcd8cc29de3ca3ee5926e90004e29ffc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/53bc83947b37aa519fe561aed8fbfa482546fdf0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/53bc83947b37aa519fe561aed8fbfa482546fdf0","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDUzYmM4Mzk0N2IzN2FhNTE5ZmU1NjFhZWQ4ZmJmYTQ4MjU0NmZkZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/1c59e1aacf30b68a30e36e2bf0a5142aaebdea95","sha":"1c59e1aacf30b68a30e36e2bf0a5142aaebdea95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/1c59e1aacf30b68a30e36e2bf0a5142aaebdea95"}],"sha":"53bc83947b37aa519fe561aed8fbfa482546fdf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/53bc83947b37aa519fe561aed8fbfa482546fdf0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/1c59e1aacf30b68a30e36e2bf0a5142aaebdea95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T18:26:04Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T18:26:04Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"v4.174 — correct the archive-reachability claim\n\nFound while verifying v4.173: GitHub Pages runs Jekyll, which excludes any\npath beginning with an underscore, so the entire _archive/ tree has ALWAYS\nreturned 404 on the deployed site. /_archive/student/, /_archive/instructor/\nand the rest have never been publicly reachable.\n\nThe README and the v4.167 changelog entry both claimed the archived mockups\nwere \"reachable by direct URL\". That was never true of the live site. Both\nare corrected, and the v4.167 entry carries an explicit note rather than\nbeing silently rewritten.\n\nThis makes v4.173 stronger than described: moving help/ into _archive/ took\nit off the live site entirely rather than merely unlinking it.\n\nNo .nojekyll file was added. Publishing the archived mockups is the exact\nopposite of what archiving them is for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"91d918e62188fbe0ccf6b89d8921f79de68b645b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/91d918e62188fbe0ccf6b89d8921f79de68b645b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/1c59e1aacf30b68a30e36e2bf0a5142aaebdea95","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/1c59e1aacf30b68a30e36e2bf0a5142aaebdea95","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDFjNTllMWFhY2YzMGI2OGEzMGUzNmUyYmYwYTUxNDJhYWViZGVhOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/d938b2443c5fa8df9fbb4db38e5503cbe2c34bc8","sha":"d938b2443c5fa8df9fbb4db38e5503cbe2c34bc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/d938b2443c5fa8df9fbb4db38e5503cbe2c34bc8"}],"sha":"1c59e1aacf30b68a30e36e2bf0a5142aaebdea95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/1c59e1aacf30b68a30e36e2bf0a5142aaebdea95"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/d938b2443c5fa8df9fbb4db38e5503cbe2c34bc8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T18:23:40Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T18:23:40Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"v4.173 — archive the hand-built Help mockup and unlink it\n\nhelp/ was a hand-built mockup, not a real SkillProof surface. It should\nhave moved to _archive/ with the other four mockups in v4.167, when the\npersona portals were replaced by live-app screenshot walkthroughs, and it\nwas missed. Left live it presented a fabricated support desk as part of\nthe product. The live app''s own help screen is captured inside all four\npersona walkthroughs, so nothing is lost.\n\nEvidence this was an oversight and not a decision: capture_screens.py\nstill lists help/index.html alongside student/, instructor/, tenant_admin/\nand super_admin/ at their pre-v4.167 root paths with the old mockup screen\ncounts. That script is already flagged ARCHIVE ONLY and stale; untouched.\n\n- git mv help -> _archive/help so its history follows it. Preserved and\n  reachable by direct URL, unlinked from the site: the same treatment the\n  other four mockups get.\n- Removed the landing page''s topbar Help button, the only live link to it.\n  Clicking into an invented help desk mid-demo is worse than that page not\n  carrying a help affordance, and it is itself a recreation of LRPS.\n- Repointed the archived mockups'' own Help links: all four used\n  ../../help/, which resolved to the root copy that no longer exists. Now\n  ../help/. 29 links across the four _archive pages.\n- Re-rooted the archived page''s own up-paths, since it sits one directory\n  deeper now (back-link, logos, favicons -- 8 references).\n- README: live Surfaces row and file-tree entry removed; overview bullet\n  and detail section relabelled as an archived mockup; _archive/help/\n  added to the archive tree.\n- preflight-live.js now asserts the opposite of what it did: that /help/\n  404s on the deployed site and that no live page links to it. New\n  verify-archived-help.js checks the archived copy still renders at its\n  new depth and that all four inbound Help links resolve.\n\nLocal: ARCHIVED_HELP_PASS. Hero regenerated for the changed topbar.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"06946afd1740d00aa8529aafebf7813340dde65b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/06946afd1740d00aa8529aafebf7813340dde65b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/d938b2443c5fa8df9fbb4db38e5503cbe2c34bc8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/d938b2443c5fa8df9fbb4db38e5503cbe2c34bc8","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKGQ5MzhiMjQ0M2M1ZmE4ZGY5ZmJiNGRiMzhlNTUwM2NiZTJjMzRiYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/26c125311233c2a90900233c56c2f3d8b6134cc1","sha":"26c125311233c2a90900233c56c2f3d8b6134cc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/26c125311233c2a90900233c56c2f3d8b6134cc1"}],"sha":"d938b2443c5fa8df9fbb4db38e5503cbe2c34bc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/d938b2443c5fa8df9fbb4db38e5503cbe2c34bc8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/26c125311233c2a90900233c56c2f3d8b6134cc1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T18:14:27Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T18:14:27Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"v4.172 — Help page icon font (pre-demo pre-flight fix)\n\nhelp/index.html declared .material-icons-outlined and preconnected to\nfonts.googleapis.com but never loaded the stylesheet, so no font ever\narrived and all 23 ligatures rendered as their literal words (\"search\",\n\"expand_more\", \"dark_mode\"). It was the only surface in the site missing\nthe line every other page already had. Verified after: 23/23 glyphs\nresolve, all 8 surfaces clean.\n\nFound by preflight-live.js, added here and mirrored to brady-browser-kit.\nIt checks the DEPLOYED site the way an audience gets it -- real CDN, real\nthird-party font requests from this network -- asserting per page: HTTP\n200, no JS errors, no failed requests, icon ligatures resolving as glyphs\nrather than literal text, Aptos loaded, no horizontal overflow at\n1920/1366/1280, no broken images, and no page still declaring the\nsuperseded wordmark favicon. A local check that only asserts HTTP status\ncannot see this class of bug.\n\nLands after the v4.171 release tag, so the tagged snapshot excludes it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8cb8f9f83079ccbd996065c6e613952e8a3c49e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/8cb8f9f83079ccbd996065c6e613952e8a3c49e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/26c125311233c2a90900233c56c2f3d8b6134cc1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/26c125311233c2a90900233c56c2f3d8b6134cc1","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDI2YzEyNTMxMTIzM2MyYTkwOTAwMjMzYzU2YzJmM2Q4YjYxMzRjYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/cc9ce9f92def5b219e3bf6d8c66322a7bb803621","sha":"cc9ce9f92def5b219e3bf6d8c66322a7bb803621","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/cc9ce9f92def5b219e3bf6d8c66322a7bb803621"}],"sha":"26c125311233c2a90900233c56c2f3d8b6134cc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/26c125311233c2a90900233c56c2f3d8b6134cc1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/cc9ce9f92def5b219e3bf6d8c66322a7bb803621/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:58:19Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:58:19Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"v4.171 — the status demo deck now opens in the browser\n\nThe landing page linked the raw .pptx, so \"view the deck\" meant \"download\n41 MB, wait, open PowerPoint\". No browser renders PowerPoint natively, so\nthe deck is converted to something a browser can paint: a viewer at /deck/.\n\nNot the Microsoft Office Online viewer -- it caps at 10 MB against a 41 MB\ndeck, would not play the embedded video anyway, and would hand a WGU URL\nto a third party to fetch on every page load. All self-hosted instead.\n\n- render_deck.py exports the 7 slides to PNG at 2560x1440 via PowerPoint\n  COM (no LibreOffice or pdftoppm on this machine). 1.6 MB for all 7.\n- build_deck_viewer.py generates deck/index.html: arrow-key/Home/End\n  paging, counter, dot rail, full screen, per-slide deep links (/deck/#4),\n  and the original .pptx one click away on the toolbar.\n- The video is NOT duplicated. Slide 6 is 39.56 of the deck''s 41 MB: one\n  embedded MP4, byte-identical (sha256) to the walkthrough already at\n  assets/video/. A real <video> is overlaid on the slide''s own video\n  region pointed at that existing asset. preload=\"none\" keeps 40 MB from\n  being fetched by anyone who never reaches slide 6, the poster is cropped\n  from the slide''s own render so the region looks identical until play,\n  and the player pauses when you page away.\n- The deck''s hyperlinks survive as real anchors on the exact shape\n  regions. A button authored as three stacked shapes sharing one link\n  merges into one anchor; links on hidden slides leave the tab order.\n- Overlay geometry is read from the slide XML (EMU over slide size, as\n  percentages), never eyeballed -- the same technique the persona\n  walkthrough hotspots use. Measured on the rendered page the video lands\n  at 28.03/0.12/71.90/99.76 against the XML''s 28/0/72/100.\n- Run-level link widths are measured, not trusted. A link on a text RUN\n  reports its whole text box: slide 7''s URL line sits in a 45%-wide box\n  while the text covers ~16%, so the box verbatim leaves a big invisible\n  click target over blank slide. Width now comes from the rendered PNG''s\n  ink, stopping at the first gap wider than 1.5% of the slide -- a first\n  pass took leftmost-to-rightmost ink, swept into the screenshot panel\n  starting at 43%, and produced a 39.8% hotspot. Now 15.8%.\n\nVerified: DECK_PASS, FAVICON_PASS, and the four persona walkthroughs\nunchanged at 32 screens / 39 hotspots / 0 problems. Hero images\nregenerated for the new sidebar label.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5637af98516af0e88f46ed5a9bb3fdf0320d1878","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/5637af98516af0e88f46ed5a9bb3fdf0320d1878"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/cc9ce9f92def5b219e3bf6d8c66322a7bb803621","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/cc9ce9f92def5b219e3bf6d8c66322a7bb803621","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKGNjOWNlOWY5MmRlZjViMjE5ZTNiZjZkOGM2NjMyMmE3YmI4MDM2MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/6b04264c5d4449f109208353de2040f0afaad1c9","sha":"6b04264c5d4449f109208353de2040f0afaad1c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/6b04264c5d4449f109208353de2040f0afaad1c9"}],"sha":"cc9ce9f92def5b219e3bf6d8c66322a7bb803621","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/cc9ce9f92def5b219e3bf6d8c66322a7bb803621"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/6b04264c5d4449f109208353de2040f0afaad1c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:39:36Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:39:36Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"v4.170 — real owl favicon, and the status demo deck on the landing page\n\nFavicon: the old icon was invisible on a dark tab strip because\nassets/wgu-favicon.png was never a favicon -- it was the 2000x910 WGU\nWORDMARK in navy on transparency. Squashed into 16x16 it read as a blob,\nand navy-on-transparent has nothing to sit against once the tab strip\ngoes dark.\n\nReplaced with the owl mark cropped from the official FY26 Full Color\nReverse lockup (owl already white) on an OPAQUE Deep Navy #001730\nsquare, so the icon carries its own background and reads on both light\nand dark chrome. Art is only cropped and scaled, never redrawn.\n\n- new: favicon.ico (16/32/48), assets/wgu-owl-favicon.png (512),\n  assets/apple-touch-icon.png (180), all built by make_favicon.py\n- each .ico frame is rendered at its own size with per-size padding and\n  a small stroke dilation in target pixels; one LANCZOS downscale of a\n  465px outline mark to 16px averaged the hairlines into grey mush.\n  Pillow''s ICO writer downscales every frame from one image, so the\n  container is packed by hand as embedded PNGs to keep that per-size work\n- wired into all 8 live pages, the 4 persona ones via the PAGE template\n  in build_prototypes.py; favicon links are the ONLY change to those\n  files, no screenshots re-captured\n- new filenames on purpose: favicons cache hard. wgu-favicon.png stays\n  on disk because the frozen _archive/ mockups still reference it\n\nDeck: skillproof-status-demo_v1-1_30JUL2026.pptx (7 slides, 41 MB,\nmostly embedded video) added as the third About SkillProof sidebar link,\nbelow Full Walkthrough (2K). Marked `download` since a 41 MB .pptx\ncannot preview in-browser.\n\nAlso regenerated the README hero images so they show the new sidebar.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"22e7de5ddf1e17c8b74375ec4ea97690b05c67a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/22e7de5ddf1e17c8b74375ec4ea97690b05c67a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/6b04264c5d4449f109208353de2040f0afaad1c9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/6b04264c5d4449f109208353de2040f0afaad1c9","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDZiMDQyNjRjNWQ0NDQ5ZjEwOTIwODM1M2RlMjA0MGYwYWZhYWQxYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/20d6bc929edb73213e08a7d261033dd8aaaff5f3","sha":"20d6bc929edb73213e08a7d261033dd8aaaff5f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/20d6bc929edb73213e08a7d261033dd8aaaff5f3"}],"sha":"6b04264c5d4449f109208353de2040f0afaad1c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/6b04264c5d4449f109208353de2040f0afaad1c9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/20d6bc929edb73213e08a7d261033dd8aaaff5f3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:24:25Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:24:25Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"Add the 2K full walkthrough as a landing-page link (v4.169)\n\nLinks the 2K capture from the landing page instead of replacing the pitch-page\nvideo: 2560x2000, 4 min 19 s, 40 MB.\n\n- Landed as assets/video/skillproof-walkthrough-2k.mp4 -- a site-level asset,\n  since it is reached from the landing page rather than being pitch-page media.\n- New sidebar link \"Full Walkthrough (2K)\" immediately under One-Slide Pitch in\n  the About SkillProof section. Points at the file and opens in a new tab so the\n  native player gets the full window and the landing page is not lost; the title\n  attribute carries resolution, duration and size.\n- pitch/index.html is UNCHANGED and keeps its own shorter embedded clip\n  (1280x1000, 38 s), so the pitch slide stays a single tight slide while the\n  long-form walkthrough sits one click away.\n- Landing hero images regenerated, since the sidebar gained a visible row. This\n  is the second time today the hero needed regenerating after a landing change --\n  worth remembering that editing index.html implies re-running\n  capture-landing-hero.js.\n\nVerified in-browser rather than on disk: the link sits directly under One-Slide\nPitch and opens in a new tab, the file serves 200 as video/mp4, the media reports\n2560x2000 and 259 s and actually plays, and a regression check confirms the pitch\npage still uses assets/skillproof-pitch-demo.mp4. The net::ERR_ABORTED on the\nmedia request is a cancelled range request after buffering, not a load failure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"73855612aa56e3ad39693e9d52c321d2a4d8d561","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/73855612aa56e3ad39693e9d52c321d2a4d8d561"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/20d6bc929edb73213e08a7d261033dd8aaaff5f3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/20d6bc929edb73213e08a7d261033dd8aaaff5f3","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDIwZDZiYzkyOWVkYjczMjEzZTA4YTdkMjYxMDMzZGQ4YWFhZmY1ZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/83c871061dea43c480b5ab2e01b947b55756e3ee","sha":"83c871061dea43c480b5ab2e01b947b55756e3ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/83c871061dea43c480b5ab2e01b947b55756e3ee"}],"sha":"20d6bc929edb73213e08a7d261033dd8aaaff5f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/20d6bc929edb73213e08a7d261033dd8aaaff5f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/83c871061dea43c480b5ab2e01b947b55756e3ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:14:26Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:14:26Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"Regenerate the README hero, and correct the landing-page docs it exposed\n\nThe hero images at the top of the README were captured 18 Jun 2026 (v4.162) and\nhad never been regenerated, so the first thing anyone sees was two months and six\nreleases stale. It predated STU101 being added (v4.163), the removal of the\ndecorative filler rows (v4.164) and pagination (v4.165), the 24 E010/D522\nskill-level links (v4.166), the walkthrough relabel (v4.167), and today''s date\nand title changes.\n\nBoth assets/landing/{light,dark}.png re-captured at the existing 1440x900 from\nthe current index.html, via a new capture-landing-hero.js. These are viewport\ncaptures, not fullPage -- the landing page is far taller and the hero shows its\ntop. The script forces the theme the same way the page does (data-theme on <html>\nplus the skillproof-theme localStorage key) rather than assuming a default, waits\nfor webfonts and the table body, and asserts the output is exactly 1440x900.\n\nLooking at the regenerated hero exposed three more documentation errors:\n\n- **Section names were wrong.** The README described the table as three sections\n  (Student Skills / Staff Links / Live-App Walkthroughs). The page actually\n  labels five: Alpha Testing - Various Skills, Beta Testing - E010, Beta Testing\n  - D522, Staff Portals, and Live-App Click-Through Demo. Renamed the README''s\n  own subsection headings to match, and gave per-section counts totalling the 43\n  live rows the page reports.\n- **The filler rows had been removed, but the docs still promised them.** The LRPS\n  surface bullet list advertised \"illustrative filler rows (OEX modules, zyBooks,\n  Pearson, ProctorU...) for realistic LRPS density\" while the same README''s\n  Surfaces table correctly recorded that v4.164 removed all of them. Replaced with\n  what the page really is: 43 real rows, no filler, no pagination, broken links\n  left visible and flagged on purpose.\n- **The landing persona framing was wrong.** It was documented as Sally''s\n  learner-facing entry point; it is really a staff launch hub listing every\n  environment link across all four roles. Also recorded that the page''s user chip\n  still reads \"Alice\" -- cosmetic drift, left alone rather than edited before a\n  demo.\n\nVerified: 34 relative links resolve, no stale claims remaining, hero PNGs\nconfirmed 1440x900 with the current title and all 43 rows present.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"93ab56a34ca6ec5587ef8f7957c42899c99ad06b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/93ab56a34ca6ec5587ef8f7957c42899c99ad06b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/83c871061dea43c480b5ab2e01b947b55756e3ee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/83c871061dea43c480b5ab2e01b947b55756e3ee","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDgzYzg3MTA2MWRlYTQzYzQ4MGI1YWIyZTAxYjk0N2I1NTc1NmUzZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/99bee424459b1705e004fa549178706e3a2c6c6d","sha":"99bee424459b1705e004fa549178706e3a2c6c6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/99bee424459b1705e004fa549178706e3a2c6c6d"}],"sha":"83c871061dea43c480b5ab2e01b947b55756e3ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/83c871061dea43c480b5ab2e01b947b55756e3ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/99bee424459b1705e004fa549178706e3a2c6c6d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:07:45Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T17:07:45Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"Docs: refresh README and CHANGELOG to the current state (v4.168)\n\nThe documentation had drifted a full release behind. It described a Python coding\ncoach when the demo now runs on STU101, told you to regenerate screenshots with a\nscript that only touches the archived mockups, and linked to four per-persona\nREADMEs that were moved into _archive/ back in v4.167.\n\nCorrected, with the reason each mattered:\n\n- **Five broken links.** student/README.md, instructor/README.md,\n  tenant_admin/README.md, super_admin/README.md and the student known-limitations\n  anchor all 404''d; repointed at _archive/. Also repointed the four persona bullets\n  and \"Surface:\" lines, which described the archived mockups while linking to the\n  live demo folders -- so a reader clicking \"student/\" expecting an 18-screen\n  mockup landed on the 8-screen demo instead.\n- **Product framing.** \"WGU''s AI-powered Python coding coach\" now reads as the\n  course-agnostic assessment/coaching engine it is, noting E010 as the first\n  release and STU101 as the demo that shows it works on non-coding content.\n- **Overview banner** replaced: it still announced the 23 Jul change. Now states\n  the three 13 Aug changes and why each was made.\n- **Regenerate instructions** were actively misleading -- the only documented\n  pipeline was capture_screens.py, which regenerates _archive/. Replaced with the\n  real five-step live pipeline (demo-reauth -> demo-seed-diagnostic ->\n  demo-capture -> bump v -> build -> verify), including the diagnostic\n  precondition, the fixed CDP ports, and an explicit note on what the tooling\n  does NOT catch: a hotspot that navigates correctly but sits on the wrong\n  control, since Open Heatmap is targeted by index. capture_screens.py is now\n  labelled ARCHIVE ONLY.\n- **Repo layout** PNG counts were 4/5/4/4; they are 8/8/10/6. Added that the four\n  personas are light-mode only, so those pages ship without a theme toggle.\n- **Design System** palette extensions pointed at student/instructor/tenant_admin\n  index.html, but that CSS now lives only in _archive/ -- the live pages are\n  screenshots plus hotspots and carry no app CSS.\n- **Shared persona & course reference** is now explicitly the archived-mockup\n  canon (E010, Sally, the 13-Topic Python taxonomy), and a new **Live demo canon**\n  table records the real STAGE ids: B002, the STU101 skill and its 4 Topics, the\n  STU101 launch link and why the launch link IS the course selection, the staging\n  Preview skill, and the model + fallback chain.\n- **Version was inconsistent three ways.** The badge read v4.167, the README\n  changelog section claimed \"Latest: v4.160\", and CHANGELOG.md topped out at\n  v4.167. All now agree on v4.168, including index.html''s <title>.\n- **Help surface over-claimed.** Two places said it closes §16.4 #9.15 (video\n  training); help/README.md correctly records that as deferred per WGU direction\n  and removed in v4.81. Corrected both.\n- Recorded observed app drift for JFT: the live New Skill wizard reads \"STEP n OF\n  3\" for steps 1-3 and then \"STEP 4 OF 5\" on review.\n\nCHANGELOG gains a full v4.168 entry covering the STU101 rebuild, the AI loop on\nall three sides, the access grant and staging Skill created to make the capture\npossible, the content-readiness gate, and the cache-buster fix.\n\nVerified: 34 relative links across README/CHANGELOG/help all resolve, no\nmarkdown table row mismatches, versions consistent across badge, title,\nCHANGELOG and the README changelog pointer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ab3d7ab8867f9adcd0ec0a93b4c68da65c0d1311","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/ab3d7ab8867f9adcd0ec0a93b4c68da65c0d1311"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/99bee424459b1705e004fa549178706e3a2c6c6d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/99bee424459b1705e004fa549178706e3a2c6c6d","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDk5YmVlNDI0NDU5YjE3MDVlMDA0ZmE1NDkxNzg3MDZlM2EyYzZjNmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/f53aabd336e422e76c5dd6a3cbd9bfc014221601","sha":"f53aabd336e422e76c5dd6a3cbd9bfc014221601","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/f53aabd336e422e76c5dd6a3cbd9bfc014221601"}],"sha":"99bee424459b1705e004fa549178706e3a2c6c6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/99bee424459b1705e004fa549178706e3a2c6c6d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/f53aabd336e422e76c5dd6a3cbd9bfc014221601/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T16:54:58Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T16:54:58Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"Bump the image cache-buster, and configure the AI prompt screen\n\nSelf-audit after review found two things a visual pass could not surface.\n\nCACHE-BUSTER NOT BUMPED (the important one). Screenshots were re-captured several\ntimes today while `v` stayed put, so the ?v= query on every <img> never changed\nand any browser that had loaded the site was still being served the CACHED\nSKELETON images. The published fix was invisible -- the review may well have been\nlooking at stale files. All four personas bumped to v=7, and the rule is now\nwritten into each flow file and the README: bump v whenever screenshots change.\n\nWIZARD STEP 3 SHOWED AN EMPTY FORM. The one screen whose purpose is to\ndemonstrate AI configuration had all three prompt fields blank, so the COMPILED\nPROMPT PREVIEW rendered empty STUDENT PROFILE / EXAMPLES / OTHER sections and\n\"Download config (.md)\" sat disabled. Now filled with a realistic student profile,\nexample style and tone constraint, so the preview shows a real compiled system\nprompt.\n\nAlso verified in this pass:\n- \"Open Heatmap\" nth=5 still resolves to the Time Management card for BOTH admin\n  personas now that B002 holds seven skill cards (3 live, 3 archived, 1 staging;\n  the staging Skill appends at nth=6). verify-demo.js cannot catch a wrong nth,\n  since the click still navigates -- it just starts from the wrong card.\n- every screen captured as already-light; redaction wrapped 20 dashboard rows,\n  17 heatmap learners and 2 profile fields, with zero unresolved hotspots.\n- Access Control masks ONLY Student rows: staff rows keep names and emails.\n- corrected the stale demo-seed-diagnostic.js filename in flow-student.json and\n  the now-wrong \"6 skill cards\" counts in both nth notes.\n\nRecorded that Super Admin intentionally omits heatmap / per-learner score screens,\nsince School Admin and Instructor already cover those views.\n\n32 screens, 39 hotspots, all clicks landing, widths uniform at 1920.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6bcdd9146aeb439c13888aa77d9da179f90f5974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/6bcdd9146aeb439c13888aa77d9da179f90f5974"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/f53aabd336e422e76c5dd6a3cbd9bfc014221601","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/f53aabd336e422e76c5dd6a3cbd9bfc014221601","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKGY1M2FhYmQzMzZlNDIyZTc2YzVkZDZhM2NiZDliZmMwMTQyMjE2MDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/3e0d3f8d8926737543882f8a914d30c351fe9dff","sha":"3e0d3f8d8926737543882f8a914d30c351fe9dff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/3e0d3f8d8926737543882f8a914d30c351fe9dff"}],"sha":"f53aabd336e422e76c5dd6a3cbd9bfc014221601","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/f53aabd336e422e76c5dd6a3cbd9bfc014221601"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/3e0d3f8d8926737543882f8a914d30c351fe9dff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T16:43:06Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T16:43:06Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"Fix captures that shipped as loading skeletons\n\nStudent screens 2, 4 and 5 published as grey placeholder bars. Every wait in the\nflow reported success, because this app''s skeleton REUSES the real class names:\n.diag__question-title and .diag-result-card both exist while the screen is still\nplaceholders, so waitSelector proved presence and never readiness.\n\ndemo-capture.js now gates on the skeleton being GONE, before hotspot measurement\nand again at the shutter, so a placeholder capture fails the run instead of\nshipping. Two things had to be got right:\n\n- Count loading markers RAW, not filtered by getBoundingClientRect visibility.\n  The first version filtered on size and was therefore useless: a skeleton\n  wrapper measures 0x0 for an instant while its bars are still painting, so the\n  filtered count hit zero and the gate passed immediately. The tell was in the\n  file timestamps -- screen 4 was written two seconds after screen 1, far too\n  fast to have waited for anything.\n- Do NOT treat [role=progressbar] as a spinner. The Super Admin dashboard''s cost\n  bar is div.sa-cost-card__bar-track[role=progressbar]; it is real content and\n  always present, so including it blocked that screen until timeout. The app''s\n  real spinner carries a spinner-* class.\n\nAlso gates on the explicit \"Preparing your first question...\" line the diagnostic\nprints while the model works, and adds per-screen readyTimeout (180s on the\nAI-generated screens, where latency is variable).\n\ndemo-seed-diagnostic.js now finishes any part-finished attempt BEFORE retaking. A\ncapture run leaves the diagnostic mid-attempt and a mid-attempt diagnostic has no\nRetake button, so the seed was continuing the partial attempt and answering only\nthe leftover questions -- earlier weak answers then dominated and the results\nscreen lost its \"Mastered Topics\" group entirely.\n\nVerified: all 32 screens re-captured and audited for rendered-ink density, the two\nflagged low-ink screens confirmed by eye as genuinely loaded (they are 3,018px and\n6,139px sparse analytics tables). All 39 hotspot clicks land on the screen they\nclaim; widths uniform at 1920; frame full-width at 1512/1920/2560.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1ed7d0190d8bfb452d40895804244fb286c6fb9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/1ed7d0190d8bfb452d40895804244fb286c6fb9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/3e0d3f8d8926737543882f8a914d30c351fe9dff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/3e0d3f8d8926737543882f8a914d30c351fe9dff","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDNlMGQzZjhkODkyNjczNzU0Mzg4MmY4YTkxNGQzMGMzNTFmZTlkZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/e7b861068faf14ac5f9c8e75ff707e10267e7adb","sha":"e7b861068faf14ac5f9c8e75ff707e10267e7adb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/e7b861068faf14ac5f9c8e75ff707e10267e7adb"}],"sha":"3e0d3f8d8926737543882f8a914d30c351fe9dff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/3e0d3f8d8926737543882f8a914d30c351fe9dff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/e7b861068faf14ac5f9c8e75ff707e10267e7adb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T15:59:50Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T15:59:50Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"Add the Instructor Skill Preview AI loop\n\nCreated a staging Skill in B002 so the preview flow has something to show:\nSchool Admin > New Skill wizard > Deploy to Staging -> \"Weekly Planning Basics\"\n(STU101-PREV), skill 57769bc8-befa-403c-aa5a-a7463543f76d, 1 topic / 2 learning\nobjectives / gpt-4o-mini. Staging is deliberate -- students cannot launch a\nstaging Skill, and only staging Skills appear in the instructor Preview list.\n\nInstructor is now 8 screens: + Staging Skills list, + Skill Preview AI-generated\nquestion, + Skill Preview AI evaluation. The evaluation grades against exactly\nthe two Learning Objectives typed into wizard step 2 (scored 0.0 and 1.0 with\nper-objective feedback), which shows the authoring config actually reaching the\nmodel. The screen also carries \"Preview only -- no data is saved\".\n\nThis completes the AI loop on all three sides: student assessment, student\ncoaching, and staff-side authoring preview. The 11 Aug site map had recorded this\ngrading step as unverified because the Claude-browser permission classifier\nblocked the submit.\n\nScreens 6-7 navigate straight to the preview URL instead of clicking through.\nResolving the click by the text \"Preview\" never reached the screen -- the page\nheading is also \"Preview skills before they go live\" and there are three\nidentical Preview buttons -- while direct navigation renders in ~3s and\nregenerates the question, since the preview persists nothing. Screen 5''s hotspot\nstill points at the real Preview button, so the click-through story is intact.\n\nRe-verified that \"Open Heatmap\" nth=5 is still the STU101 card: the new staging\nSkill appends at nth=6, so adding it did not shift the existing target.\n\nDemo is now 32 screens / 39 hotspots, every persona on STU101/B002, every capture\n1920 wide, all 39 hotspot clicks landing on the screen they claim.\n\nDropped the \"Known gaps\" framing around STAGE test data: this is a beta test\ntenant and the test labels are expected, not a cleanup target.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ea545704fd17966803f07a4f54a371fc4f8c3e75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/ea545704fd17966803f07a4f54a371fc4f8c3e75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/e7b861068faf14ac5f9c8e75ff707e10267e7adb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/e7b861068faf14ac5f9c8e75ff707e10267e7adb","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKGU3Yjg2MTA2OGZhZjE0YWM1ZjljOGU3NWZmNzA3ZTEwMjY3ZTdhZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/761183db1a1fdb30d9f9ced945068cfe4a40d310","sha":"761183db1a1fdb30d9f9ced945068cfe4a40d310","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/761183db1a1fdb30d9f9ced945068cfe4a40d310"}],"sha":"e7b861068faf14ac5f9c8e75ff707e10267e7adb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/e7b861068faf14ac5f9c8e75ff707e10267e7adb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/761183db1a1fdb30d9f9ced945068cfe4a40d310/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T15:34:06Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T15:34:06Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"Put the Instructor persona on STU101 too\n\nGranted Test InstructorUsr1 access to course folder B002 (which holds STU101)\nthrough Super Admin > Access Control > Instructor row > Add Course, as Brady\ndirected: the Super Admin screen owns \"Instructor Course assignments\", so the\naccess gap was mine to fix rather than to report. The grant took effect\nimmediately for the already-open session -- the check is server-side, so no LTI\nre-launch was needed.\n\nInstructor is now 5 screens, all on B002/STU101: Dashboard (4 courses, B002\nshowing 26 learners / 0.21 avg / 11 at risk) -> Course Detail -> the STU101 skill\nheatmap with its real 17 learners -> Learner profile -> Help. Replaces the older\n1440-wide A101/E010 captures.\n\nAlso fixed: the dashboard''s 68-learner cross-course table was never redacted. It\nholds real names, so surnames are now wrapped and masked there too, consistent\nwith the other personas.\n\nTwo component classes differ between roles for the same-looking screen: the\ninstructor learner-profile title is h1.ilp__title where School Admin uses\nh1.lps__title, so the School Admin selector timed out here.\n\nDemo is now 29 screens / 35 hotspots, every persona on STU101, every capture\n1920 wide. verify-demo.js passes on all four with zero problems and all 35\nhotspot clicks landing on the screen they claim; verify-frame-width.js passes at\n1512/1920/2560.\n\nStill absent, and noted in the README: the instructor Skill Preview screen. It\nneeds a STAGING skill and B002 has only Production(3) + Archived(3), so adding it\nwould mean deploying a new skill into a shared course.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c85b1f5d1a8d5ac736d371938e12dcdd3ebe5548","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/c85b1f5d1a8d5ac736d371938e12dcdd3ebe5548"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/761183db1a1fdb30d9f9ced945068cfe4a40d310","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/761183db1a1fdb30d9f9ced945068cfe4a40d310","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDc2MTE4M2RiMWExZmRiMzBkOWY5Y2VkOTQ1MDY4Y2ZlNGE0MGQzMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/20320d5667cdf20d86ecfd60f50f32db64f55c30","sha":"20320d5667cdf20d86ecfd60f50f32db64f55c30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/20320d5667cdf20d86ecfd60f50f32db64f55c30"}],"sha":"761183db1a1fdb30d9f9ced945068cfe4a40d310","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/761183db1a1fdb30d9f9ced945068cfe4a40d310"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/20320d5667cdf20d86ecfd60f50f32db64f55c30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T15:10:27Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T15:10:27Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"Rebuild the demo on STU101 and add the AI interaction screens\n\nThe demo was missing the thing the platform exists for: no LLM interaction on\neither the assessment or the coaching side. The July 2026 storyboard HAD those\ntwo screens (\"Diagnostic question 1/4\", \"AI feedback\"); the 12 AUG rebuild\ndropped them and also silently moved the student flow off STU101 onto\nIntroduction to Python.\n\nStudent (4 -> 8 screens), all on STU101:\n- AI diagnostic question: \"AI-GENERATED ASSESSMENT\" prompt, answer box, 1/4\n- AI evaluation: feedback narrative + per-objective score table + next focus\n- AI coaching prompt, and AI coaching feedback with its evaluation table\n- plus diagnostic results, Progress Map (4 topics), landing, help\n\nThe student course is fixed by the LTI launch -- the JWT carries activeCourseId\nand the app ignores ?course= entirely -- so the launch link IS the course\nselection. Re-auth now uses provision/576572714 (STU101), not 568442570\n(Python).\n\nSchool Admin (8 -> 10), on B002/STU101: course detail, the STU101 heatmap with\nits real 17 learners, learner profile, and New Skill wizard steps 1-3 including\nstep 3''s model choice, fallback chain and COMPILED PROMPT PREVIEW. Review &\nDeploy is never clicked, so no skill is created.\n\nSuper Admin (6): now includes B002 course detail. The super-admin course route\ntakes the folder id; the skill id renders \"Course folder not found\".\n\nHarness changes:\n- captures at 1920 wide (was 1440), so screens are 1:1 on a 1080p share instead\n  of upscaled by the full-bleed frame\n- `order` lets capture order differ from display order. Diagnostic Results needs\n  a COMPLETED diagnostic and the question screen needs one IN PROGRESS, so the\n  results screen is captured first and the retake that destroys it runs last\n- optional per-step `timeout`, because a 30s default is too thin for a step that\n  waits on an LLM\n- a `select` step: locator.fill() cannot drive the wizard''s required Course\n  dropdown\n- verify-demo.js derives expected width per persona instead of hardcoding 1440,\n  and launches its own browser rather than borrowing an SSO-authenticated profile\n\nFixed a real hotspot bug: resolving the dashboard''s B002 target by text matched\nDIV.tap__course-grid -- the whole 16-course grid at 60.8% width -- so clicking\nanywhere in it navigated. Nothing in that ancestor chain is a real control, so\nthe card is now targeted by selector.\n\nVerified: 31 screens, 38 hotspots, every hotspot click lands on the screen it\nclaims, widths uniform per persona, redaction confirmed visually (student\nsurnames masked, first and staff names visible).\n\nInstructor is unchanged and still NOT on STU101: that account has no access to\ncourse folder B002 (\"You do not have access to this course folder\"). Recorded\nunder Known gaps in the README.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a9e43088e762dbdf49b38a70aedc14280c17b99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/6a9e43088e762dbdf49b38a70aedc14280c17b99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/20320d5667cdf20d86ecfd60f50f32db64f55c30","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/20320d5667cdf20d86ecfd60f50f32db64f55c30","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDIwMzIwZDU2NjdjZGYyMGQ4NmVjZmQ2MGY1MGYzMmRiNjRmNTVjMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/cbff406c862ca8c1fc9aad8e933f9bdc4b66518d","sha":"cbff406c862ca8c1fc9aad8e933f9bdc4b66518d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/cbff406c862ca8c1fc9aad8e933f9bdc4b66518d"}],"sha":"20320d5667cdf20d86ecfd60f50f32db64f55c30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/20320d5667cdf20d86ecfd60f50f32db64f55c30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/cbff406c862ca8c1fc9aad8e933f9bdc4b66518d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:32:38Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T14:32:38Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"Make the demo frame full browser width with internal scroll\n\nThe 12 AUG 2026 build pinned .shot at min(1440px, 100%) with a max height of\n900px, centred in a grey backdrop. That renders as a floating screenshot card,\nnot an app window, which is not what was asked for: full browser width, scroll\nto the bottom inside the frame.\n\n- .shot is now width:100% / height:calc(100vh - bar), edge-to-edge, no card\n  border-radius or shadow, so the capture fills the window like the live app.\n- .stage is block instead of flex. A flex row let a second .active screen\n  flex-shrink both children, which produced phantom width readings when\n  measuring.\n- flow.json''s `frame` width is now documented as the CAPTURE width only, still\n  asserted against every PNG. It is not a display cap -- hotspots are\n  percentage-based so they track the image at any render scale.\n\nVerified with _verify-frame-width.js at 1512/1920/2560 wide: frame width equals\nviewport width, the image renders full width, the frame reaches the bottom of\nevery capture, and the page itself never scrolls. FRAME_FAIL=0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e9dc54ef97053626e6ae8ae788e52523f762cd16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/e9dc54ef97053626e6ae8ae788e52523f762cd16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/cbff406c862ca8c1fc9aad8e933f9bdc4b66518d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/cbff406c862ca8c1fc9aad8e933f9bdc4b66518d","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKGNiZmY0MDZjODYyY2E4YzFmYzlhYWQ4ZTkzM2Y5YmRjNGI2NjUxOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/33ae7c851fb0d4f4cb174421503829e75fc887ee","sha":"33ae7c851fb0d4f4cb174421503829e75fc887ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/33ae7c851fb0d4f4cb174421503829e75fc887ee"}],"sha":"cbff406c862ca8c1fc9aad8e933f9bdc4b66518d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/cbff406c862ca8c1fc9aad8e933f9bdc4b66518d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/33ae7c851fb0d4f4cb174421503829e75fc887ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T21:51:02Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T21:51:02Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"Rebuild the storyboard as a real click-through demo\n\nThe 12 AUG 2026 refresh was unusable as a demo. Two defects, both mine:\n\n  1. Every screen shipped with an empty wire array, so nothing was clickable\n     and the only way to move was the step-button bar. The prior version had\n     working CTA hotspots; that was a regression.\n  2. Screenshots came out at three widths (745/1329/1440) with heights from\n     849px to 6139px, so every click jumped to a different page shape. Cause:\n     the preflight script resized Chrome to 800x520 for window tiling, Chrome\n     persists window size per profile, and the capture used viewport:null,\n     which inherits it. The width spread was noticed mid-run and written into\n     flow.json as per-screen docW values instead of being fixed at the source.\n\nNow:\n\n  - skillproof-qa-tools/demo-capture.js drives every capture from a declarative\n    flow file: one forced viewport for all screens, and each output PNG''s width\n    asserted from its IHDR header, so a mismatched file fails the run.\n  - Hotspots are measured off the live DOM (getBoundingClientRect + scroll\n    offset, normalised to the captured document) rather than hand-authored, so\n    a hotspot cannot drift from the screenshot under it. 31 hotspots across 25\n    screens.\n  - Every screen renders in an identical 1440x900 app window that scrolls\n    INTERNALLY. Tall pages keep all their content without leaking their height\n    into the page shape.\n  - The meta-bar switches roles, so all four personas are reachable from any\n    screen. This is the actual goal: one link instead of signing into four\n    accounts to show the product working.\n  - verify-demo.js clicks all 31 hotspots and asserts each lands on the screen\n    it claims, that no hotspot is container-sized, and that the frame is\n    uniform. Passing on all 4 personas.\n\nRedaction now fails loudly instead of silently. wrapSurnames and mask\nselectors that match 0 elements abort the screen, which caught two screens\nwhere a page-heading wait let capture run before the learner table loaded --\nthose would have published unmasked student names. Student surnames are\ncovered; staff names (instructor, school admin, super admin) stay visible.\n\nScreens: Student 4, Instructor 7, School Admin 8, Super Admin 6.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"de9b1cae37f9b109b05c3156d494eca26b8e030c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/trees/de9b1cae37f9b109b05c3156d494eca26b8e030c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/commits/33ae7c851fb0d4f4cb174421503829e75fc887ee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/33ae7c851fb0d4f4cb174421503829e75fc887ee","node_id":"C_kwDOR2RjXNoAKDMzYWU3Yzg1MWZiMGQ0ZjRjYjE3NDQyMTUwMzgyOWU3NWZjODg3ZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commit/46be39ed0e6ad72fc32a945f0b49c75b78be12cc","sha":"46be39ed0e6ad72fc32a945f0b49c75b78be12cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/46be39ed0e6ad72fc32a945f0b49c75b78be12cc"}],"sha":"33ae7c851fb0d4f4cb174421503829e75fc887ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/33ae7c851fb0d4f4cb174421503829e75fc887ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266849667?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/brady-wgu","id":266849667,"login":"brady-wgu","node_id":"U_kgDOD-fNgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/46be39ed0e6ad72fc32a945f0b49c75b78be12cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T21:19:38Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T21:19:38Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"Refresh storyboard screenshots to current live app (12 Aug 2026)\n\nScreenshots were ~3 weeks stale relative to the live app and covered far\nless than the site map now catalogs. Expanded from 17 to 29 screens across\nthe 4 personas: Student 4, Instructor 7, School Admin 11, Super Admin 7.\n\nAdded coverage for flows that didn''t exist in the storyboard before: the\n3-step New/Edit Skill wizard, Instructor''s Skill Preview and Staging Skills\nlist, School Admin''s Learner Profile and Tenant Settings, Super Admin''s\nPer-School Logo Settings, and Export menus.\n\nStudent data is redacted (first name shown, surname/email/avatar masked)\nper privacy review during capture; staff names (Instructor/School\nAdmin/Super Admin) are shown as-is since this is a beta/test environment,\nnot production data.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"407a17b88f49880e93ee192a0d9fbb1e27a26b5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/git/tr