ub.com/users/brady-wgu/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brady-wgu","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/brady-wgu/SkillProof/commits/9427fe7db6ed7e144a0b88e9747528a6a8018540/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T17:24:16Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T17:24:16Z","email":"brady.redfearn@wgu.edu","name":"Brady Redfearn, PhD"},"message":"v4.160: unify export — one \"Export\" dropdown on every filtered table, format by data nature\n\nThe per-section export buttons were hand-built and inconsistent (drifted placement/\nalignment, a stray margin, all four formats everywhere). Replaced with one shared,\nmodule-injected control.\n\n- table-controls.js injects a consistent \"Export\" dropdown into every filtered table''s\n  control bar (+ heatmaps). Removed all 20 hand-built standalone export rows\n  (TA 8 / SA 9 / instructor 3) via a verified script.\n- Now on every filtered table (rosters, dashboards, School Management, analytics, logs),\n  not just the analytics / drill screens.\n- Format by audience: PDF+CSV for human-read (default); MD+JSON for machine-ingested\n  (logs / audit / webhooks) via data-export=\"machine\". Heatmap -> PDF/CSV; server log -> MD/JSON.\n- \"Reports & exports\" per-row downloads trimmed to PDF+CSV; the table marked data-no-export.\n- SA Logs export via a data-export-here hook on its bespoke filter row.\n\nVerified: SA 14 dropdowns (11 human / 3 machine), TA 7 (6/1), Instructor 3 (all human),\n0 legacy rows, single confirmation toast, no console errors, light + dark. Shared assets -> ?v=13.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"07dc65586fd9b23e85259e595d1880bcd8897b1a","url":"htt