DE0YjJhZDk1NDA1YjIwMzZmNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mtdkjarvis/jarvis-mission-control/commit/14f34d1cb24263c92c4bbc6708181b51a4d4d3c0","sha":"14f34d1cb24263c92c4bbc6708181b51a4d4d3c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mtdkjarvis/jarvis-mission-control/commits/14f34d1cb24263c92c4bbc6708181b51a4d4d3c0"}],"sha":"5604758a6577a148e145014b2ad95405b2036f77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mtdkjarvis/jarvis-mission-control/commits/5604758a6577a148e145014b2ad95405b2036f77"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93952610?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0xNyk","id":93952610,"login":"0xNyk","node_id":"U_kgDOBZmaYg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mtdkjarvis/jarvis-mission-control/commits/14f34d1cb24263c92c4bbc6708181b51a4d4d3c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-24T18:03:17Z","email":"93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-24T18:03:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: agent runtime installer in onboarding and settings (#499)\n\n* feat: agent runtime installer in onboarding + settings\n\nAdd guided installation for OpenClaw and Hermes Agent runtimes,\naccessible both from the onboarding wizard (new \"Runtimes\" step)\nand from the Settings panel (\"Agent Runtimes\" section).\n\nNew files:\n- src/lib/agent-runtimes.ts: detection, background install jobs,\n  Docker sidecar compose templates\n- src/app/api/agent-runtimes/route.ts: install, detect, job-status,\n  docker-compose actions\n- src/components/onboarding/step-agent-runtimes.tsx: wizard step with\n  runtime cards showing install/detect status\n- src/components/settings/agent-runtimes-section.tsx: settings panel\n  section for managing runtimes post-onboarding\n\nLocal mode: runs installer commands in background (OpenClaw via\ncurl installer, Hermes via pipx/npm). Docker mode: generates\nsidecar docker-compose service definitions.\n\nAlso fixes:\n- Security scan no longer penalizes score for missing OpenClaw in\n  standalone mode (severity lowered from medium to low)\n- Export clearHermesDetectionCache() for post-install re-detection\n- Add isDocker to capabilities endpoint\n\n* fix: show Install button in Docker mode alongside sidecar YAML option\n\n* feat: add Claude Code and Codex CLI to runtime installer\n\nExtend the agent runtime installer with two additional runtimes:\n- Claude Code (npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code)\n- Codex CLI (npm install -g @openai/codex)\n\nBoth require post-install authentication:\n- Claude: \"claude login\"\n- Codex: \"codex auth\"\n\nThe UI shows auth status (authenticated/needs auth) for runtimes\nthat require it, with the auth command as a hint.\n\n* fix: Docker-safe installs with proper HOME/npm prefix\n\n- Set HOME and npm_config_prefix to .data/ when running in Docker\n  (HOME=/nonexistent causes EACCES for npm global installs)\n- Run ''openclaw onboard --non-interactive'' after OpenClaw install\n- Try pip as fallback for Hermes (after pipx and npm)\n- Shared runInstallCmd helper with Docker-safe env for all runtimes\n\n* fix: use official Hermes curl installer instead of pip/npm\n\n* docs(openapi): add /api/agent-runtimes contract entries\n\n* fix(ci): sync onboarding e2e expectations and openapi parity","tree":{"sha":"5d995e4c8da95201742937ecc32a282782a2d061","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mtdkjarvis/jarvis-mission-control/git/trees/5d995e4c8da95201742937ecc32a282782a2d061"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mtdkjarvis/jarvis-mission-control/git/commits/14f34d1cb24263c92c4bbc6708181b51a4d4d3c0","verification":{"payload":"tree 5d995e4c8da95201742937ecc32a282782a2d061\nparent dd15409a6bd4fb0d7eee84a4ac0d29f896b37158\nauthor nyk <93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com> 1774375397 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774375397 +0700\n\nfeat: agent runtime installer in onboarding and settings (#499)\n\n* feat: agent runtime installer in onboarding + settings\n\nAdd guided installation for OpenClaw and Hermes Agent runtimes,\naccessible both from the onboarding wizard (new \"Runtimes\" step)\nand from the Settings panel (\"Agent Runtimes\" section).\n\nNew files:\n- src/lib/agent-runtimes.ts: detection, background install jobs,\n  Docker sidecar compose templates\n- src/app/api/agent-runtimes/route.ts: install, detect, job-status,\n  docker-compose actions\n- src/components/onboarding/step-agent-runtimes.tsx: wizard step with\n  runtime cards showing install/detect status\n- src/components/settings/agent-runtimes-section.tsx: settings panel\n  section for managing runtimes post-onboarding\n\nLocal mode: runs installer commands in background (OpenClaw via\ncurl installer, Hermes via pipx/npm). Docker mode: generates\nsidecar docker-compose service definitions.\n\nAlso fixes:\n- Security scan no longer penalizes score for missing OpenClaw in\n  standalone mode (severity lowered from medium to low)\n- Export clearHermesDetectionCache() for post-install re-detection\n- Add isDocker to capabilities endpoint\n\n* fix: show Install button in Docker mode alongside sidecar YAML option\n\n* feat: add Claude Code and Codex CLI to runtime installer\n\nExtend the agent runtime installer with two additional runtimes:\n- Claude Code (npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code)\n- Codex CLI (npm install -g @openai/codex)\n\nBoth require post-install authentication:\n- Claude: \"claude login\"\n- Codex: \"codex auth\"\n\nThe UI shows auth status (authenticated/needs auth) for runtimes\nthat require it, with the auth command as a hint.\n\n* fix: Docker-safe installs with proper HOME/npm prefix\n\n- Set HOME and npm_config_prefix to .data/ when running in Docker\n  (HOME=/nonexistent causes EACCES for npm global installs)\n- Run ''openclaw onboard --non-interactive'' after OpenClaw install\n- Try pip as fallback for Hermes (after pipx and npm)\n- Shared runInstallCmd helper with Docker-safe env for all runtimes\n\n* fix: use official Hermes curl installer instead of pip/npm\n\n* docs(openapi): add /api/agent-runtimes contract entries\n\n* fix(ci): sync onboarding e2e expectations and openapi parity","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpwtHlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMGUQAHiXldF2AzftAGLAvnmqzesO\nt+5EeQgIZs6CGub11PrUuOE0Q3LOpWDdCH1oAep3moPeKCVucFRKdFpwLdQ4t6Af\nUN2Orxrv3a9kbWhFqSuvF7f3MlOaSYVkVz2zd9EQOUFyMOLC4EqP9NQNyL675kf/\n2NKCeFazF7PPVfxL3/lC73kkkgCuUh6GP2YMMa+VdVbs8HoqNButBfFy84/n6raN\nWuFHGxoaL+DPJG9GnBPizO2zliH+dcQC0kbaRnfHs0tDeIDi2zQ4SvD+SJiJnrSj\n1L/Slz9BgUk/378uWZy7zdMbgiSbXTRx8ow07kIOeU5/+I7ygSPdZ6ToVc95XigK\n/her8v2YNhx8XIfbDpAY6DhpY4F8FreUx43qhDBXIybCend5TvHzPGV1ed3/viox\nptsfetpufjmLGyoSB888wnHx9g2KB4kaqNprhURajISKPF0xVPGBpdHBS0r5+QsK\ngRv8vJf4KJoLqzjlgooCgb502J7Gp/+kn0m+s+vzmkGaYvK1nxaqPSdQ+tg4SIId\niAqvOcVcQCU19EUXHqJLrxTF25QhcNCYXoOZvveDKCBEAjQ74jXjQpnRdPUOHlql\nIUln8TG1AdDQKUURRFludbvLeA/1UAqF8OBkpNkVL7+40P6PcUf22IsnOQdtRMF4\nXUVM0eSWVFGsS+kgMcrq\n=JMtU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-01T02:56:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mtdkjarvis/jarvis-mission-control/commit/14f34d1cb24263c92c4bbc6708181b51a4d4d3c0","node_id":"C_kwDOR2esztoAKDE0ZjM0ZDFjYjI0MjYzYzkyYzRiYmM2NzA4MTgxYjUxYTRkNGQzYzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mtdkjarvis/jarvis-mission-control/commit/dd15409a6bd4fb0d7eee84a4ac0d29f896b37158","sha":"dd15409a6bd4fb0d7eee84a4ac0d29f896b37158","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mtdkjarvis/jarvis-mission-control/commits/dd15409a6bd4fb0d7eee84a4ac0d29f896b37158"}],"sha":"14f34d1cb24263c92c4bbc6708181b51a4d4d3c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mtdkjarvis/jarvis-mission-control/commits/14f34d1cb24263c92c4bbc6708181b51a4d4d3c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93952610?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/0xNyk","id":93952610,"login":"0xNyk","node_id":"U_kgDOBZmaYg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/0xNyk","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mtdkjarvis/jarvis-mission-control/commits/dd15409a6bd4fb0d7eee84a4ac0d29f896b37158/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-24T17:56:39Z","email":"93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com","name":"nyk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-24T17:56:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix/memory system audit (#502)\n\n* fix: memory system security, integrity, and performance improvements\n\n- Extract shared path safety helpers to src/lib/memory-path.ts (DRY)\n- Fix path traversal in /api/memory/links using resolveSafeMemoryPath()\n- Add isPathAllowed() prefix check to /api/memory/links route\n- Enforce MEMORY_ALLOWED_PREFIXES in /api/memory/context route\n- Add migration 047 for working_memory column (removes runtime ALTER TABLE)\n- Fix workspace/DB dual-write staleness: compare mtime vs updated_at\n- Add 512KB MAX_WORKING_MEMORY_SIZE guard on PUT (returns 413)\n- Eliminate double directory scan in buildLinkGraph/health/context\n- Extract getAgentByIdOrName() helper to reduce duplication\n\n* feat: FTS5 full-text search for memory + MCP knowledge tools\n\n- Add SQLite FTS5 virtual table for memory filesystem search\n- Replace brute-force substring search with BM25-ranked results\n- Support FTS5 query syntax: AND, OR, NOT, NEAR, \"phrase\", prefix*\n- Auto-build index on first search, incremental updates on save/delete\n- Add /api/memory/search route (GET search, POST rebuild index)\n- Add migration 048_memory_fts for FTS5 table creation\n- Add snippet extraction with <mark> highlighting\n- Porter stemming + unicode tokenization for better recall\n\nMCP tools added (5 new):\n- mc_search_knowledge: full-text search with FTS5\n- mc_read_knowledge_file: read file content + wiki-links\n- mc_write_knowledge_file: create/update knowledge files\n- mc_knowledge_health: run health diagnostics\n- mc_rebuild_search_index: rebuild FTS index\n\n* feat: enhanced consolidation pipeline with gap detection and graph analysis\n\nAdd two new knowledge maintenance passes inspired by LACP:\n\ngap-detect: severity-scored knowledge gap detection\n  - Broken wiki-links (severity 0.8)\n  - Orphan files with no connections (severity 0.5)\n  - Stale files scored by age (age/90 days, capped at 1.0)\n  - Knowledge gaps: terms referenced 2+ times without a file\n\nconsolidate: graph structure analysis\n  - Hub detection: files with disproportionately many connections\n  - Bridge detection: nodes whose removal would fragment the graph\n  - Cluster detection: connected components with density scoring\n  - Weak edge detection: links between unrelated neighborhoods\n\nNew API actions: POST /api/memory/process { action: \"gap-detect\" | \"consolidate\" }\nNew MCP tools: mc_knowledge_gaps, mc_knowledge_consolidate\n\n* docs(openapi): add /api/memory/search contract entries","tree":{"sha":"d35e2348eafdd6f57257e2b9bb3c95fcc8fcddd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mtdkjarvis/jarvis-mission-control/git/trees/d35e2348eafdd6f57257e2b9bb3c95fcc8fcddd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mtdkjarvis/jarvis-mission-control/git/commits/dd15409a6bd4fb0d7eee84a4ac0d29f896b37158","verification":{"payload":"tree d35e2348eafdd6f57257e2b9bb3c95fcc8fcddd6\nparent 0f70fd51541fdd4188e52aca39b841e6dd221af6\nauthor nyk <93952610+0xNyk@users.noreply.github.com> 1774374999 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774374999 +0700\n\nFix/memory system audit (#502)\n\n* fix: memory system security, integrity, and performance improvements\n\n- Extract shared path safety helpers to src/lib/memory-path.ts (DRY)\n- Fix path traversal in /api/memory/links using resolveSafeMemoryPath()\n- Add isPathAllowed() prefix check to /api/memory/links route\n- Enforce MEMORY_ALLOWED_PREFIXES in /api/memory/context route\n- Add migration 047 for working_memory column (removes runtime ALTER TABLE)\n- Fix workspace/DB dual-write staleness: compare mtime vs updated_at\n- Add 512KB MAX_WORKING_MEMORY_SIZE guard on PUT (returns 413)\n- Eliminate double directory scan in buildLinkGraph/health/context\n- Extract getAgentByIdOrName() helper to reduce duplication\n\n* feat: FTS5 full-text search for memory + MCP knowledge tools\n\n- Add SQLite FTS5 virtual table for memory filesystem search\n- Replace brute-force substring search with BM25-ranked results\n- Support FTS5 query syntax: AND, OR, NOT, NEAR, \"phrase\", prefix*\n- Auto-build index on first search, incremental updates on save/delete\n- Add /api/memory/search route (GET search, POST rebuild index)\n- Add migration 048_memory_fts for FTS5 table creation\n- Add snippet extraction with <mark> highlighting\n- Porter stemming + unicode tokenization for better recall\n\nMCP tools added (5 new):\n- mc_search_knowledge: full-text search with FTS5\n- mc_read_knowledge_file: read file content + wiki-links\n- mc_write_knowledge_file: create/update knowledge files\n- mc_knowledge_health: run health diagnostics\n- mc_rebuild_search_index: rebuild FTS index\n\n* feat: enhanced consolidation pipeline with gap detection and graph analysis\n\nAdd two new knowledge maintenance passes inspired by LACP:\n\ngap-detect: severity-scored knowledge gap detection\n  - Broken wiki-links (severity 0.8)\n  - Orphan files with no connections (severity 0.5)\n  - Stale files scored by age (age/90 days, capped at 1.0)\n  - Knowledge gaps: terms referenced 2+ times without a file\n\nconsolidate: graph structure analysis\n  - Hub detection: files with disproportionately many connections\n  - Bridge detection: nodes whose removal would fragment the graph\n  - Cluster detection: connected components with density scoring\n  - Weak edge detection: links between unrelated neighborhoods\n\nNew API actions: POST /api/memory/process { action: \"gap-detect\" | \"consolidate\" }\nNew MCP tools: mc_knowledge_gaps, mc_knowledge_consolidate\n\n* docs(openapi): add /api/memory/search contract entries","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpwtBYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABgoQAGN7W/CmdT1IGjB6msU6km3c\n10E0XmHmbmBmk1/+U7G+6bvXDLttqDNZ/pkHO1NrQZD/ucvR+JGNSHIsFTIAdV+Z\naMRVFan2UWZ7pQPkiqUoyawvatlaSD2raB69xbWGQjQ7WibfXlfD25hMjRB/5fk6\n/MtaCJ6OzNFOdcjgL4NJuDeV7trJdl10Fr8TKWIZsOHOi2bPL5MK8xDNomUMRQ8k\ndqCvquOzAFoKsey+BF+ozE79QKB1Ty+7U1VKI1CqH7xJ9F5EZJ/ITPk0t/oPEbIl\nbD9Im0KPQfV9HM97AuGCTkKSiIh0uEYeuG9amy1C4U3RJkLvFCSGw+Xha0i29dAm\nYw4kgEMRCu290aiX6T0BKp3r9NHFiHduK/jAVQlHEehWbJ0zHvynzeMdOjpY4qR6\nphK+sKJDIsiuWhVZc6OC0keyKC4AV3eJ9Yjb41JJjDJqyOcdlJd7w27hA/yoF1Jz\nSmyavnpSOM3khq2LGXRTd/gwccRMWNlRVLcGuffe0W6SK/l9K0oB7bXLtbWD7g5S\nLlraHx1OxSuf4gjcJAJ7hzR+2CsdI6/W6kgI2hZ5/adZF+H+SrSgy736BJGzt5mi\nx8iX3LWrLQzIhTgMoLNHnRrCLOQCX8kNC2LoJ8+aKo/MVFbjG/Tk7Gs0m+Xggsrp\nJ24a7YovjIydvqixd4JH\n=/ZP+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-01T02:56:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","