a":"f7f8ea74ca4e1ee141c7aade99c18ac3a802a442","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/f7f8ea74ca4e1ee141c7aade99c18ac3a802a442"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/54b2276e87b100eec15692be5127f6e0c7ff0567/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:32:19Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:32:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(runtime): base64 a non-UTF8 response body, or it never arrives intact (#231)\n\nThe producer half. The consumer (api-platform moduleinvoke) must be DEPLOYED\nfirst: it accepts isBase64Encoded and decodes, and until it is serving, a\nbase64 body would be relayed to a browser as base64 text.\n\nA Go string cannot carry arbitrary bytes through encoding/json, which is how\nthis envelope travels. The marshaller substitutes U+FFFD for every invalid\nUTF-8 sequence, silently, so `Body: rec.Body.String()` corrupted every binary\na module has ever served.\n\nMeasured in production 2026-09-16: video-core''s 16-byte AES playback key\narrived as 28 bytes — six invalid bytes, each replaced by the three-byte\nreplacement rune — and hls.js decrypted every segment to noise, reporting\nfragParsingError. It took three days to find because nothing was wrong at any\none layer: the module wrote 16 correct bytes, the platform relayed what it was\ngiven, the CDN served what it was asked for, and every log was green.\n\nThe test is the bytes, not the Content-Type: a module may serve binary under\nany type, and a text/* body holding invalid UTF-8 is equally corruptible.\nValid UTF-8 still travels as a plain string, so every consumer sees\nbyte-identical traffic for everything it already handles.\n\nBoth tests carry their control — binary through a plain string body must come\nback CHANGED, so simplifying lambdaBody back to string(raw) fails them.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019LLaQQeGtSbECUttDeGKam\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cb62568dba131e2167477af61cffaaada9ee4005","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/cb62568dba131e2167477af61cffaaada9ee4005"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/54b2276e87b100eec15692be5127f6e0c7ff0567","verification":{"payload":"tree cb62568dba131e2167477af61cffaaada9ee4005\nparent c45bdaa7a6a5de7f94b57856ef6d55ffaeb66205\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1789569139 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789569139 +0800\n\nfix(runtime): base64 a non-UTF8 response body, or it never arrives intact (#231)\n\nThe producer half. The consumer (api-platform moduleinvoke) must be DEPLOYED\nfirst: it accepts isBase64Encoded and decodes, and until it is serving, a\nbase64 body would be relayed to a browser as base64 text.\n\nA Go string cannot carry arbitrary bytes through encoding/json, which is how\nthis envelope travels. The marshaller substitutes U+FFFD for every invalid\nUTF-8 sequence, silently, so `Body: rec.Body.String()` corrupted every binary\na module has ever served.\n\nMeasured in production 2026-09-16: video-core''s 16-byte AES playback key\narrived as 28 bytes — six invalid bytes, each replaced by the three-byte\nreplacement rune — and hls.js decrypted every segment to noise, reporting\nfragParsingError. It took three days to find because nothing was wrong at any\none layer: the module wrote 16 correct bytes, the platform relayed what it was\ngiven, the CDN served what it was asked for, and every log was green.\n\nThe test is the bytes, not the Content-Type: a module may serve binary under\nany type, and a text/* body holding invalid UTF-8 is equally corruptible.\nValid UTF-8 still travels as a plain string, so every consumer sees\nbyte-identical traffic for everything it already handles.\n\nBoth tests carry their control — binary through a plain string body must come\nback CHANGED, so simplifying lambdaBody back to string(raw) fails them.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019LLaQQeGtSbECUttDeGKam\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqqhzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALakQAJvhDPfiuJYmpcMaiDK+GdV4\nclvp8JXuJPeOQrhz5Hk545f70fHwDM1r37YBa8YomtxrvmLlQdsDm+x/qbbdM0/I\ncsIYR1+28qSd9jgbXfbEv2y1PWPvtTdJvWSsQfbqlETNFTWTTmzhwBYNmVWiiM+R\nSfORI81PJ7wmxfQuJg4+T/EyQ8Dq07NLexeLheiW8rTP5rrjjmROLvvB+X5zTs64\newrpnnfzIqcqQO1g/GzIliQARdeMBqGSNu/gu1UFe60brpLIIe7+YKls3ChQtbF2\ndL+NvRo3ZpDja3Z2j/zLvHKUZKHS2FssA8LjyxIUmHTp59u5wKGy/ilF1IlLeeyE\nLa1OF4Suz8QJxtkF6fFBRitblP04hLeKH2ZBRjL4Jema9SO4HbXpN+0XFitMSiYx\nSwzTjzsddtk/9QcJtsmZFpu6sMqLHL3Xr57Tt6t1C7izOmP5lNiv3ALhbqW19Cnl\nxY4hbHaCMMPWXfL48/iLJM4bMvVb0wy1/9pLx1yFDvkL3aC+rvO+PUqrf/KVXSzR\nFBa6sq74m9qZMaGg1QzbHiUfAffO1wI3BzEgpjZt