riptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/f839850c09dee3e8f77c0984e4c95bb90f23fcee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:11:49Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:11:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(db): a pooled connection must dial with the CURRENT token (#216)\n\nA module''s pool outlived the token that built it, so any container that\nstayed warm past ~15 minutes lost its database permanently.\n\nThe static path — which is the ordinary invocation path — built its pool\nwith no credential provider, freezing the first envelope''s token into\nConnConfig.Password. The cache key excludes the token on purpose (rotation\nmust not churn pools) and refcache returns a hit without ever running the\nfactory, so a rotated token had nowhere to land. Meanwhile MinConns 0,\nMaxConnIdleTime 5m and MaxConnLifetime 30m mean connections are re-dialled\ncontinuously — every one of them with a token that expired long ago.\n\nThe renewal machinery already existed and was correct; nothing on this path\nreached it. internal/runtime/inject.go installs a static db.Credential from\nResources.DB, so resolvePoolFor finds no provider and falls to PoolCache.Get.\nOnly the task-worker path installed a provider.\n\nThe fix does not add a fetch. Every invocation already carries a freshly\nminted token, so the pool only has to stop pinning the first one: Get now\nwires an envelope-backed CredentialProvider and refreshes it on every call,\nhit or miss. BeforeConnect then hands each new connection the token current\nat dial time, and the existing scope guard still refuses a credential that\nwould move the connection to another host, database or user.\n\nMeasured in production 2026-09-09. user-core answered\n`failed to acquire connection: ... PAM authentication failed (SQLSTATE\n28000)` continuously from 09:29Z. It was the only one of five deployed\nmodules affected and the only one with a 60-second cron holding a single\ncontainer warm: every 28000 came from ONE log stream, while a healthy\nmodule''s traffic in the same window spanned five. The others went cold and\nrebuilt their pools with fresh tokens, which is what made a platform-wide\ndefect look like one module''s broken database grant — and sent three\nseparate \"repairs\" (re-install, forward move, db-bootstrap) at a role whose\ngrant was never missing. 28000 is PAM refusing a TOKEN; a missing rds_iam\nmembership is 28P01.\n\nThree tests, each mutation-checked. Two assert the hook at the config layer,\nwhere the existing renewal tests live and no PostgreSQL is needed. The third\nasserts the WIRING, which is where the defect actually was: that Get passes a\nprovider at all, and that a cache hit refreshes it. My first two tests passed\nwith both fixes reverted — they exercised a hook nothing reached.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7175276b17efe9b8966a32b8224f949b3ad36bad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/7175276b17efe9b8966a32b8224f949b3ad36bad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/f839850c09dee3e8f77c0984e4c95bb90f23fcee","verification":{"payload":"tree 7175276b17efe9b8966a32b8224f949b3ad36bad\nparent 4d874338e675674d2b915d1fc4081cd355698f96\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1788959509 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788959509 +0800\n\nfix(db): a pooled connection must dial with the CURRENT token (#216)\n\nA module''s pool outlived the token that built it, so any container that\nstayed warm past ~15 minutes lost its database permanently.\n\nThe static path — which is the ordinary invocation path — built its pool\nwith no credential provider, freezing the first envelope''s token into\nConnConfig.Password. The cache key excludes the token on purpose (rotation\nmust not churn pools) and refcache returns a hit without ever running the\nfactory, so a rotated token had nowhere to land. Meanwhile MinConns 0,\nMaxConnIdleTime 5m and MaxConnLifetime 30m mean connections are re-dialled\ncontinuously — every one of them with a token that expired long ago.\n\nThe renewal machinery already existed and was correct; nothing on this path\nreached it. internal/runtime/inject.go installs a static db.Credential from\nResources.DB, so resolvePoolFor finds no provider and falls to PoolCache.Get.\nOnly the task-worker path installed a provider.\n\nThe fix does not add a fetch. Every invocation already carries a freshly\nminted token, so the pool only has to stop pinning the first one: Get now\nwires an envelope-backed CredentialProvider and refreshes it on every call,\nhit or miss. BeforeConnect then hands each new connection the token current\nat dial time, and the existing scope guard still refuses a credential that\nwould move the connection to another host, database or user.\n\nMeasured in production 2026-09-09. user-core answered\n`failed to acquire connection: ... PAM authentication failed (SQLSTATE\n28000)` continuously from 09:29Z. It was the only one of five deployed\nmodules affected and the only one with a 60-second cron holding a single\ncontainer warm: every 28000 came from ONE log stream, while a healthy\nmodule''s traffic in the same window spanned five. The others went cold and\nrebuilt their pools with fresh tokens, which is what made a platform-wide\ndefect look like one module''s broken database grant — and sent three\nseparate \"repairs\" (re-install, forward move, db-bootstrap) at a role whose\ngrant was never missing. 28000 is PAM refusing a TOKEN; a missing rds_iam\nmembership is 28P01.\n\nThree tests, each mutation-checked. Two assert the hook at the config layer,\nwhere the existing renewal tests live and no PostgreSQL is needed. The third\nasserts the WIRING, which is where the defect actually was: that Get passes a\nprovider at all, and that a cache hit refreshes it. My first two tests passed\nwith both fixes reverted — they exercised a hook nothing reached.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoVsVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2WsQAIbYhEnzXU/lBg40hIl0PcPz\nZRvYfuKKIRj+mtRzfTiFFz7r8rJR2uOBAASr5pl2I332BwusDK7mZwaEBjniOkSA\n9YsohoJdNMAXtNkLzaZ39HMFvxCGLNTy8Be335JGTOX2ru3pBj9vmSPysm8x01Gn\njf3CTWhexd/Rg0VcX/h7c67D47H7+ifdE5BaX8tShMb8BjOkBgrSHslqiTSG0QhM\nel/6yaWxTCyVxEZLftOMJrOJjia0EW94E8uivR/7v2jmQrzJ5428rAwT3SiQSrm5\n6JvL79NjrjBNSUMqsAYffvSNk6TWjtEW4BEV6gZPyhG8Ed7vcy41pHvPF9doGk64\na3sqi1viQAGi8Qa617jMqaLy153A5WiMEqHtSKbWdSbyT3RDPgWhyRgDv7UzFVxN\nrODLdForut9XGQkFh4ObVjR5YzAkKm8x3Q5Y46r7BwuESrsii5MUqLQJZWXzMsnJ\nOBiPsG3CBf9djew+0DZwa9CwRGikGGIi6a0bbkSlLgELwa3Z1r22y+I7PVLfNoOV\n9xtOgOZcHfGOdojykkDQbnohuWsQ3A/w/wIu9kisLIU05G3llqqtHzSRUBMh/LDk\nlpqkMmua9bPiFS+6DsaRUjJReZlKZz8AxT6Wlve1wjP9sGBP3rrDoSP958Qcg+Of\nmHtIK7XaJa3OMELzwnwz\n=BYTC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T13:11:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/f839850c09dee3e8f77c0984e4c95bb90f23fcee","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKGY4Mzk4NTBjMDlkZWUzZThmNzdjMDk4NGU0Yzk1YmI5MGYyM2ZjZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/4d874338e675674d2b915d1fc4081cd355698f96","sha":"4d874338e675674d2b915d1fc4081cd355698f96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/4d874338e675674d2b915d1fc4081cd355698f96"}],"sha":"f839850c09dee3e8f77c0984e4c95bb90f23fcee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/f839850c09dee3e8f77c0984e4c95bb90f23fcee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/4d874338e675674d2b915d1fc4081cd355698f96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T05:01:28Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T05:01:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(db): pin the lifecycle DB-location seam the deployed plane silently failed on (#215)\n\nA deployed module''s install/upgrade calls have never worked. The lifecycle\nbody carries only username+token by design; the LOCATION comes from the\nmodule''s own environment through EnvBaseCredential, whose production half\nwas never written — its comment still reads \"Production (deployed runtime)\nwill replace this with a managed-secret fetch when that infra lands\". So it\nfell through to defaultDevURL and every lifecycle call against a deployed\nmodule died with:\n\n  dial tcp 127.0.0.1:5433: connect: connection refused\n\nNo deployed module''s app-scope migrations had ever run, which is why every\nmodule on the affected app answered 42P01 \"relation does not exist\".\n\napi-platform#756 supplies DATABASE_URL to every provisioned module. Nothing\non THIS side of the seam asserted that the SDK consumes it. The writer and\nthe reader live in different repos, so a URL shape the writer considers\nobvious and the reader rejects would reproduce the same outage wearing a\ndifferent error string — and this repo has been bitten by exactly that\nbefore, with the module URL contract''s receiver-side validator.\n\nThree tests, one seam:\n\n- the SDK accepts the EXACT string api-platform emits, and resolves\n  host/port/database from it. The rendered URL carries a placeholder user\n  (pgx given no user falls back to os/user.Current(), which needs $USER or\n  cgo and can fail inside Lambda); this asserts that placeholder does NOT\n  survive into Username/Token, since the lifecycle handler is supposed to\n  fill both from the request and a base that carried identity through would\n  mask a platform that forgot to send one.\n\n- a NEGATIVE CONTROL: with no DATABASE_URL the fallback is still\n  localhost:5433. Without it the first test would pass for a build that\n  ignores the environment entirely — the same vacuity that let the original\n  bug ship — and it also pins the fingerprint the production diagnosis was\n  keyed on.\n\n- MS_LOCAL_DB_URL still wins over DATABASE_URL, so a developer running a\n  module locally with both set is not silently redirected at a deployed\n  endpoint.\n\nThe literal URL is duplicated rather than imported: a cross-repo seam\nasserted against a value taken from one side only proves that side agrees\nwith itself.\n\nMutation-tested — removing the DATABASE_URL rung reproduces the production\nsymptom exactly (localhost/5433) and fails the first test.\n\nTest-only. No runtime change, no version bump.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d00f734d181403aefe45c6f6770a87bcd98f5371","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/d00f734d181403aefe45c6f6770a87bcd98f5371"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/4d874338e675674d2b915d1fc4081cd355698f96","verification":{"payload":"tree d00f734d181403aefe45c6f6770a87bcd98f5371\nparent 78121716de06c857bb10978493a231dc97b7708f\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1788930088 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788930088 +0800\n\ntest(db): pin the lifecycle DB-location seam the deployed plane silently failed on (#215)\n\nA deployed module''s install/upgrade calls have never worked. The lifecycle\nbody carries only username+token by design; the LOCATION comes from the\nmodule''s own environment through EnvBaseCredential, whose production half\nwas never written — its comment still reads \"Production (deployed runtime)\nwill replace this with a managed-secret fetch when that infra lands\". So it\nfell through to defaultDevURL and every lifecycle call against a deployed\nmodule died with:\n\n  dial tcp 127.0.0.1:5433: connect: connection refused\n\nNo deployed module''s app-scope migrations had ever run, which is why every\nmodule on the affected app answered 42P01 \"relation does not exist\".\n\napi-platform#756 supplies DATABASE_URL to every provisioned module. Nothing\non THIS side of the seam asserted that the SDK consumes it. The writer and\nthe reader live in different repos, so a URL shape the writer considers\nobvious and the reader rejects would reproduce the same outage wearing a\ndifferent error string — and this repo has been bitten by exactly that\nbefore, with the module URL contract''s receiver-side validator.\n\nThree tests, one seam:\n\n- the SDK accepts the EXACT string api-platform emits, and resolves\n  host/port/database from it. The rendered URL carries a placeholder user\n  (pgx given no user falls back to os/user.Current(), which needs $USER or\n  cgo and can fail inside Lambda); this asserts that placeholder does NOT\n  survive into Username/Token, since the lifecycle handler is supposed to\n  fill both from the request and a base that carried identity through would\n  mask a platform that forgot to send one.\n\n- a NEGATIVE CONTROL: with no DATABASE_URL the fallback is still\n  localhost:5433. Without it the first test would pass for a build that\n  ignores the environment entirely — the same vacuity that let the original\n  bug ship — and it also pins the fingerprint the production diagnosis was\n  keyed on.\n\n- MS_LOCAL_DB_URL still wins over DATABASE_URL, so a developer running a\n  module locally with both set is not silently redirected at a deployed\n  endpoint.\n\nThe literal URL is duplicated rather than imported: a cross-repo seam\nasserted against a value taken from one side only proves that side agrees\nwith itself.\n\nMutation-tested — removing the DATABASE_URL rung reproduces the production\nsymptom exactly (localhost/5433) and fails the first test.\n\nTest-only. No runtime change, no version bump.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoOgoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAjoQAH4fPXRv0lRFkRBPpniYW3ph\nPgRP1suJxtwl8tti6zOdSz1yKbN5g+lP2yansPx7Lm4L9MGKtbTUuU3GBROl4aYa\nuZdpRhsi3PvU5oCv0+KafiIx2HEmciFBTcB1nmoSIGsZzKnA2Eqfff51qufD+3yS\ngZ2AYDmjuvgIkpBRaSAbvogW9yXWjmmLfLdyP9wEau846yi6b9BdL0XSlRv9hWgG\nj3A160ri9oxUJZRl0aRbXL9SPBBvAfVQMgRD+O/2FYuQi/M45uDLFoZZPV1QHy6V\nZfnX4tNL79AFK3lpnM7MiEy5AZmXBe6v7uLUPSiAgdo6LDBSmSmVuP0JM9yAYMHR\nSkUHMNhm42aA+74wnsQplYiLHSor8peMLuezMC+FgNJUiEKVY7CK3gJQrTEAX9Ws\nMEClf/zDR7I0lOukuFyt7El/refqdrILafpD/Y0oUUw0A29TF0DCskL9uVMO1fhi\nWMh15yv7d2zHtdzf7+uL5wCAsKLSFLFVqB4ac2n7xsUtNAE4nn28QUQ/j2t3HZJa\naDy8/Tm8VmLXJaRRjnA177E5AQKqrHAbE30ca0+pY3YPcW2HYE4ruWMMX6i84QMR\nwAzxS9bDO5oy1MepGLC3sp4DEWUL3etA7kSDTqAUFUdg+sZkK8lWrHv6bHoEk4zw\nF+Oz6Y0A5AXFCngDa4XW\n=W67u\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T05:01:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/