githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/e69e09d096b1341463b6f1e914cb28dfdeb2985f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T07:15:20Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T07:15:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: module URL cut-over — module-keyed ms.Call and scope-before-module canonical routes (v0.4.14) (#210)\n\n* feat(call): route module hops through the module-keyed dispatch edge\n\nms.Call / CallGet / CallPost now resolve to\n{MS_DISPATCH_URL | dev fallback}/v1/dispatch/apps/module/{targetModuleID}{path}\ninstead of {base}/module/{targetModuleID}{path}. The platform is removing\n/module/{id}/* in a one-wave cut-over and serves the same handler under the\nnew path with the same app-resolution rules (X-MS-App-ID header, else app_id\nquery, else single-install auto-resolve); /internal/* stays open to module\ncallers on this edge.\n\nThis is also a live repair: MS_DISPATCH_URL is the bare API host, where\n/v1/dispatch is path-routed to the dispatch Lambda, so /module/... on that\nhost reached the account Lambda and 404ed.\n\nOnly resolveCallURL changes, as the #146 seam comment reserved. The\nresolveDevDependencyCall comment stops naming /module/{id} for a route it\nnever built (it returns the local module-proxy /_m/{slug} route). The\nactor-delegation tests pin the new path and now fail if the nested call never\nreaches dispatch at all, so the \"no delegation forwarded\" assertion cannot\npass vacuously against a wrong path. Every module must adopt this version\nonce api-platform removes /module/{id}/*; CHANGELOG carries it as the\nv0.5.0 breaking entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: accept the scope-before-module canonical routes (the wave''s blocking half)\n\n🔴 This is what makes the cut-over survivable, and it was missing.\n\ninvocationwire''s canonical-routes check re-derives the routes from App.ID and\nModule.Slug and rejects the envelope when they do not match. It still required\nthe RETIRED shape — /v1/dispatch/apps/{app}/{slug} with \"/public\" and\n\"/platform\" appended — while api-platform''s moduleinvoke.ModuleRoutes now emits\n/v1/apps/app/{app} plus /public/{slug} and /platform/{slug}. Every typed\ninvocation from the new platform would have failed this check, and the module\nwould answer 400 \"invalid invocation context\" on EVERY route, not merely lose\nits module-to-module hops. Measured: user-core''s auth suite against the new\nenvelope on v0.4.13 fails exactly that way.\n\nThe two sides are a transcription of one another, so they now share the\ninvocation_v1.json golden byte for byte (diffed against api-platform''s copy),\nand TestCanonicalRoutesAreScopeBeforeModule pins the rule in the form a reader\nof either repo can compare by eye — with four negative cases, including the\nretired shape, so a validator that stopped running could not pass it.\n\nAlso corrects the CHANGELOG''s \"live repair\" claim. MS_DISPATCH_URL is the bare\nAPI host only for a DEPLOYED module Lambda; a tunnel-served module gets\nhttps://api.mirrorstack.ai/dispatch from docker-compose.yml, WITH the mapping\nkey, so its /module/{id} hops resolve today. No module is deployed, so the 404\nrepairs a path nothing currently takes — the point of the new address is that\nit works under both bases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* release: cut this as v0.4.14, not v0.5.0 — the number is decided against the API\n\nrelease.yml''s own header states the convention: pre-1.0, patch-only bumps even\nfor new SDK surface; a MINOR is for an exported signature change (that is why\nv0.4.0 took one, and why the 54-symbol task-plane wave still took v0.4.1).\n\nMeasured, not assumed. Exported declarations across every non-internal,\nnon-examples package: 506 before, 506 after — 0 added, 0 removed, 0 changed.\nBoth halves of this change live in internal/ (internal/core/call.go,\ninternal/invocationwire/wire.go). So it is a PATCH.\n\nThe behavioural break is total — a module on v0.4.13 answers 400 on every route\nonce the platform emits the new envelope — but the same precedent covers that:\nRunTask losing its synchronous fallback stayed a patch with an [!IMPORTANT]\nCHANGELOG callout rather than an inflated number. This has one, at the top of\nthe entry.\n\nI had pre-pinned v0.5.0 in twelve module go.mod files before deciding the\nnumber. A pin written before the number is decided is a guess; the pins get\ncorrected, not the version.\n\nAlso bumps VERSION and moves [Unreleased] under its heading, so cutting the\nrelease is only the `release` label plus the merge — deliberately NOT labelled\nhere: merging a release-labelled PR IS the release act, and that is the owner''s\ncall.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: keep the release cut in its own PR, per the repo convention\n\nEvery release in this repo''s history is a separate ''chore: release vX.Y.Z'' PR\ntouching only VERSION and CHANGELOG.md and carrying the ''release'' label (#208,\n#203, ...); feature PRs carry no label. I had folded the bump and the CHANGELOG\nheading move into this feature PR, which works mechanically but would title the\nrelease commit after the feature and let a feature merge cut a release — exactly\nwhat the convention avoids.\n\nVERSION goes back to 0.4.13 and the entry back under [Unreleased], stating the\nnumber it should be cut as and why. The release PR follows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"524f4e82e6398fa86d3614b2b4a05f14f561ad99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/524f4e82e6398fa86d3614b2b4a05f14f561ad99"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/e69e09d096b1341463b6f1e914cb28dfdeb2985f","verification":{"payload":"tree 524f4e82e6398fa86d3614b2b4a05f14f561ad99\nparent 8382b979c9b9d97ae9ad7e4197f14559b643970e\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1788592520 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788592520 +0800\n\nfeat: module URL cut-over — module-keyed ms.Call and scope-before-module canonical routes (v0.4.14) (#210)\n\n* feat(call): route module hops through the module-keyed dispatch edge\n\nms.Call / CallGet / CallPost now resolve to\n{MS_DISPATCH_URL | dev fallback}/v1/dispatch/apps/module/{targetModuleID}{path}\ninstead of {base}/module/{targetModuleID}{path}. The platform is removing\n/module/{id}/* in a one-wave cut-over and serves the same handler under the\nnew path with the same app-resolution rules (X-MS-App-ID header, else app_id\nquery, else single-install auto-resolve); /internal/* stays open to module\ncallers on this edge.\n\nThis is also a live repair: MS_DISPATCH_URL is the bare API host, where\n/v1/dispatch is path-routed to the dispatch Lambda, so /module/... on that\nhost reached the account Lambda and 404ed.\n\nOnly resolveCallURL changes, as the #146 seam comment reserved. The\nresolveDevDependencyCall comment stops naming /module/{id} for a route it\nnever built (it returns the local module-proxy /_m/{slug} route). The\nactor-delegation tests pin the new path and now fail if the nested call never\nreaches dispatch at all, so the \"no delegation forwarded\" assertion cannot\npass vacuously against a wrong path. Every module must adopt this version\nonce api-platform removes /module/{id}/*; CHANGELOG carries it as the\nv0.5.0 breaking entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: accept the scope-before-module canonical routes (the wave''s blocking half)\n\n🔴 This is what makes the cut-over survivable, and it was missing.\n\ninvocationwire''s canonical-routes check re-derives the routes from App.ID and\nModule.Slug and rejects the envelope when they do not match. It still required\nthe RETIRED shape — /v1/dispatch/apps/{app}/{slug} with \"/public\" and\n\"/platform\" appended — while api-platform''s moduleinvoke.ModuleRoutes now emits\n/v1/apps/app/{app} plus /public/{slug} and /platform/{slug}. Every typed\ninvocation from the new platform would have failed this check, and the module\nwould answer 400 \"invalid invocation context\" on EVERY route, not merely lose\nits module-to-module hops. Measured: user-core''s auth suite against the new\nenvelope on v0.4.13 fails exactly that way.\n\nThe two sides are a transcription of one another, so they now share the\ninvocation_v1.json golden byte for byte (diffed against api-platform''s copy),\nand TestCanonicalRoutesAreScopeBeforeModule pins the rule in the form a reader\nof either repo can compare by eye — with four negative cases, including the\nretired shape, so a validator that stopped running could not pass it.\n\nAlso corrects the CHANGELOG''s \"live repair\" claim. MS_DISPATCH_URL is the bare\nAPI host only for a DEPLOYED module Lambda; a tunnel-served module gets\nhttps://api.mirrorstack.ai/dispatch from docker-compose.yml, WITH the mapping\nkey, so its /module/{id} hops resolve today. No module is deployed, so the 404\nrepairs a path nothing currently takes — the point of the new address is that\nit works under both bases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* release: cut this as v0.4.14, not v0.5.0 — the number is decided against the API\n\nrelease.yml''s own header states the convention: pre-1.0, patch-only bumps even\nfor new SDK surface; a MINOR is for an exported signature change (that is why\nv0.4.0 took one, and why the 54-symbol task-plane wave still took v0.4.1).\n\nMeasured, not assumed. Exported declarations across every non-internal,\nnon-examples package: 506 before, 506 after — 0 added, 0 removed, 0 changed.\nBoth halves of this change live in internal/ (internal/core/call.go,\ninternal/invocationwire/wire.go). So it is a PATCH.\n\nThe behavioural break is total — a module on v0.4.13 answers 400 on every route\nonce the platform emits the new envelope — but the same precedent covers that:\nRunTask losing its synchronous fallback stayed a patch with an [!IMPORTANT]\nCHANGELOG callout rather than an inflated number. This has one, at the top of\nthe entry.\n\nI had pre-pinned v0.5.0 in twelve module go.mod files before deciding the\nnumber. A pin written before the number is decided is a guess; the pins get\ncorrected, not the version.\n\nAlso bumps VERSION and moves [Unreleased] under its heading, so cutting the\nrelease is only the `release` label plus the merge — deliberately NOT labelled\nhere: merging a release-labelled PR IS the release act, and that is the owner''s\ncall.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: keep the release cut in its own PR, per the repo convention\n\nEvery release in this repo''s history is a separate ''chore: release vX.Y.Z'' PR\ntouching only VERSION and CHANGELOG.md and carrying the ''release'' label (#208,\n#203, ...); feature PRs carry no label. I had folded the bump and the CHANGELOG\nheading move into this feature PR, which works mechanically but would title the\nrelease commit after the feature and let a feature merge cut a release — exactly\nwhat the convention avoids.\n\nVERSION goes back to 0.4.13 and the entry back under [Unreleased], stating the\nnumber it should be cut as and why. The release PR follows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqm8GICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFY8QAHotRVBZQKpGjfVxZwhTfA6i\n2s0sS9n8J7K4OJY4NmpXeACpM+M2oklndqm2o1OROdabdYH0kcUmUZJS675VgzUy\nAGdn+0ZDCM5SS9LZ6S42YzOxKGoIRWDU/iZT583J6FwjMEeTSGrmg2aJUMmfuogr\nRAEDjEiiPJr7SZakW4pxyvi+gWtud8cZlV1GmbwkMNY6o9fAybEM/45O0JBIfu60\noYZqYYYrZwlXkNPKZi4BDAlhAYLzzL+l/etL7A8YQatpKqTTcVkuJeZ+nRNJ2sj2\nozCy3sz2+JWxwOH+JJXup4DkzxZMC/u9IeHe1GEEz7Cdcckh1jc6g/icydSZ0+I3\nphMZ2Lq4ENsOdamfKkW4XJPgTnm/C4L9gVQf45HRNVDgkxcB4TDNMZnzwHE82Dpp\nz38ii8maoLkzKeYT7xk/b1yq9Mu7vbkv9SgPlTlt8RV8fKz6nSsa6c4UY/NVBiB/\nZ6/O66xOg/kGNXl5K1ao7Quc1S3gFwObZG5f0FDJMvKNfKJd+prwKYv/bHDeZ9/m\noci6qge7m3po3ELZnZ0mxnQMc4tJNZfl/bBbgSoErSUiSSzdo8J8YNHggV2pYSH9\nSnWrgSq7RKZNTg3khjgy9hM6yWso8ce6SzV0HLxk+aeFBdFIlFwNBhqSON8H68bO\ndNBn0y0YjTC7+953yeW/\n=OB5l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-05T07:15:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/e69e09d096b1341463b6f1e914cb28dfdeb2985f","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKGU2OWUwOWQwOTZiMTM0MTQ2M2I2ZjFlOTE0Y2IyOGRmZGViMjk4NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/8382b979c9b9d97ae9ad7e4197f14559b643970e","sha":"8382b979c9b9d97ae9ad7e4197f14559b643970e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/8382b979c9b9d97ae9ad7e4197f14559b643970e"}],"sha":"e69e09d096b1341463b6f1e914cb28dfdeb2985f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/e69e09d096b1341463b6f1e914cb28dfdeb2985f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/8382b979c9b9d97ae9ad7e4197f14559b643970e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T02:35:16Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T02:35:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: add timeout-minutes to every job that lacked one (#209)\n\nA job with no timeout-minutes inherits GitHub''s 6-hour default, so a runner\nthat dies mid-job hangs a required check for hours instead of failing fast.\n\nEach value is max(10, ceil(2 x p95)) over the last 20 runs, measured from the\njobs API, with the p95 recorded in a comment beside it. Runner-lease deaths\n(~601s) and short-circuited path-filtered runs are excluded from the\nmeasurement; deploy legs are floored above the slowest run ever observed so a\ncold build is never killed.\n\nWorkflow files only: no runs-on changes, no step logic changes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"afe769fcce32f7ff2af17216f6ee3a6a1899f9d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/afe769fcce32f7ff2af17216f6ee3a6a1899f9d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/8382b979c9b9d97ae9ad7e4197f14559b643970e","verification":{"payload":"tree afe769fcce32f7ff2af17216f6ee3a6a1899f9d7\nparent 08421d0a484c1799c3d42660415c92369de9c543\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1788402916 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788402916 +0800\n\nci: add timeout-minutes to every job that lacked one (#209)\n\nA job with no timeout-minutes inherits GitHub''s 6-hour default, so a runner\nthat dies mid-job hangs a required check for hours instead of failing fast.\n\nEach value is max(10, ceil(2 x p95)) over the last 20 runs, measured from the\njobs API, with the p95 recorded in a comment beside it. Runner-lease deaths\n(~601s) and short-circuited path-filtered runs are excluded from the\nmeasurement; deploy legs are floored above the slowest run ever observed so a\ncold build is never killed.\n\nWorkflow files only: no runs-on changes, no step logic changes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmNzkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAle8QADvJ/3mv6x5Y7Px+oMNvbRrm\ngRcLu2KncIqs9tZkbWYV8iFoAijB+Sz2kGn7x957drblQuLsNPsfpjHpyZOxq3J8\nbKyaspx5bALrypTwebZ4bUJviI1eV1yNu6I/Kkhw6HDOaLkpUcOP/UEAQksqh22X\nmR7nnO4BPLunUSyPv4C7FS61a7UV563e2OOR2qmWWvzt5/sS4ZJoGcYOYrRaXhsg\nduwtloRxvxlg8jx64j45ObgnijgsPAs5M73yjM2X1vMpIFoxe1yKB6LUgW4mEVZS\nFjIo0pQ7P5fv77HsHlPIgMk31NKBBXvdyQ2SN4eExEbCinDj5RLgkFICs8XX9VTE\nIN3anqEP//RfQ9YnDZqo2rLEPxzm5895nmRHlU43WSZ751CoelYkOb7UzXKNSPny\nMmCGyAfCGN49VuyC6arQBhY+5uN5J4YXMGk8xVpUCycUOULRpeTRmGoMZnrYvooa\nUyPUO6Gnljhco+iX5KfKX+ioRwVUfyCcK1irUf2UIFYyjHts26SDkjbONGR8kXTW\nibZ8N8MEnFyLGR5Ff5iSq9MEnZ+w/uYiLbPYkW8s0nOhwqgoECmKk/4GLD5s+B+W\nKjJR+hoSolUc1/1cHSLblGbH349VLKH9M51UEoaaOdyUwBDesCqHAf0Tti0HS4HI\nkD3arBwF3hQBB7XajnNh\n=TvYO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T02:35:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/receiv