://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/c4bdc96c309870ffba735473102dbc5e7157b0ad","verification":{"payload":"tree de5a243fd4e025ac627e341b46a7fe3e1e1f9299\nparent 1c7c02da4ad6b7f0f0615a8a6514e257f2be6413\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1786891709 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786891709 +0800\n\nchore: release v0.4.3 (#182)\n\nAdditive surface only: storage.Client.Get, storage.MaxGetBytes and\nstorage.ErrObjectTooLarge, plus the Get method on the Storer interface. Nothing\nremoved, nothing changed — patch, per the pre-1.0 convention, verified by\ndiffing the exported surface rather than by intent.\n\nvideo-core needs this tag to read HLS playlists over the S3 API instead of\npresigning a client-facing URL and fetching it from inside the module.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgc29CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABhMQACnPXJnenbT2/y7z0fwIit5n\nSAnBRyJSitq+gLcNeEQExq7HO1XMNUWRAmYqD4J+BrXo/Hx+WEuS+Fqx+kW0uuu3\nTYHf7Eqm7YcvhAdt9gh1vqq4PUWrpXiZLZESNaLzUcu7IAhG2zJ1OMWk5XoXtQm7\nGbVDuJCqcRVtlno/3CszKFYmWQ0QjamioL52vUE5W3hneu+1SDqXUYdOTOsfMOE6\n6TLcRu3YRK64yF8gTSZxBn9XCpaZpFO5CYa748jfxS9VHp706Nm2HD7QAkPqtf08\n9iw8K55CFtTK+e+Wmb7EIO9QjwCVwxXTihaA6KXTcPM8GyPaxOlAM6MbARJXj1Wo\nhTo3NbO1VSiuQK8jao7aXOhuY3d8Dj6Ic+DVfGE+mGXEKMO+NRZshI3817MnVM1a\nMHtTOSIdG9hCsHksi3yaj0hynvWYqR8BFdFf3Lt4He62S2zeOyB/I0fFEykx0pxs\nSD8WF9RBAxbyqffM/7penLs0YKRqKhMgAgNWgsKyLIsRFLNLDGOS6hdQy6YKuSBI\nRAOoVt/IROvHp8VgWdbxvaLgtDfvAd77mp/x+5ddwaiCctYgpeXhlPKphcPw9Tqf\nCls0DXsk2WkT/I4Le5t9utSkD29wR8ZdM79x7eoy3HtHW6EyP6Ibd5z4REdfS4be\n6TPEp9Oar7GMsi3ivOzO\n=++uo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-16T14:48:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/c4bdc96c309870ffba735473102dbc5e7157b0ad","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKGM0YmRjOTZjMzA5ODcwZmZiYTczNTQ3MzEwMmRiYzVlNzE1N2IwYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/1c7c02da4ad6b7f0f0615a8a6514e257f2be6413","sha":"1c7c02da4ad6b7f0f0615a8a6514e257f2be6413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/1c7c02da4ad6b7f0f0615a8a6514e257f2be6413"}],"sha":"c4bdc96c309870ffba735473102dbc5e7157b0ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/c4bdc96c309870ffba735473102dbc5e7157b0ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/1c7c02da4ad6b7f0f0615a8a6514e257f2be6413/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T14:37:05Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T14:37:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(storage): read a module''s own object over the S3 API (#181)\n\n* feat(storage): read a module''s own object over the S3 API\n\nThe SDK had no server-side read at all — only PresignGet. A module that needs\nto read its OWN object (video-core parses and rewrites HLS playlists before\nserving them) had to presign a URL and then fetch it over HTTP.\n\nThat is not merely a wasteful extra round trip to your own storage. It is\nwrong: a presigned URL is signed against the CLIENT-facing endpoint, and the\nmodule runs somewhere that address need not resolve. In the dev container it\nresolves to the container itself, so every playlist read failed with\n`dial tcp [::1]:9000: connect: connection refused` — surfacing in the browser\nas a CORS error on master.m3u8, about as far from the cause as an error can\nland.\n\nGet goes over the S3 API with the module''s own credential and the endpoint that\ncredential was minted for, so it is correct from wherever the module runs.\nRule of thumb, stated in the doc comment: bytes YOU need → Get; bytes the\nVIEWER needs → PresignGet or Delivery.\n\nCapped at MaxGetBytes (8 MiB) because this is for small module-owned control\nfiles — playlists, manifests, sidecars — and a mistyped key should not turn a\n4 GB source video into an OOM. The LimitReader is deliberately MaxGetBytes+1 so\nexceeding the cap is DETECTED rather than silently truncated: a truncated\nplaylist is a subtly broken video, which is far worse to debug than a refusal.\n\nAdditive: one method on Storer and one file. No existing behaviour changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(storage): say why Get is on Storer while PrefixDeleter is not\n\ndelete.go keeps DeletePrefix off Storer on purpose, so an interface method\nappearing here reads like an oversight. It is not: ms.Storage hands every module\nthis interface, and reading your own object is as fundamental as writing one.\nRecording the rule so the next capability is placed on purpose either way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"df9224f9906ed94a6508fed5d5750f647557984c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/df9224f9906ed94a6508fed5d5750f647557984c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/1c7c02da4ad6b7f0f0615a8a6514e257f2be6413","verification":{"payload":"tree df9224f9906ed94a6508fed5d5750f647557984c\nparent 334a2b33b543106ab69e82a9be1b8179a0de615e\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1786891025 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786891025 +0800\n\nfeat(storage): read a module''s own object over the S3 API (#181)\n\n* feat(storage): read a module''s own object over the S3 API\n\nThe SDK had no server-side read at all — only PresignGet. A module that needs\nto read its OWN object (video-core parses and rewrites HLS playlists before\nserving them) had to presign a URL and then fetch it over HTTP.\n\nThat is not merely a wasteful extra round trip to your own storage. It is\nwrong: a presigned URL is signed against the CLIENT-facing endpoint, and the\nmodule runs somewhere that address need not resolve. In the dev container it\nresolves to the container itself, so every playlist read failed with\n`dial tcp [::1]:9000: connect: connection refused` — surfacing in the browser\nas a CORS error on master.m3u8, about as far from the cause as an error can\nland.\n\nGet goes over the S3 API with the module''s own credential and the endpoint that\ncredential was minted for, so it is correct from wherever the module runs.\nRule of thumb, stated in the doc comment: bytes YOU need → Get; bytes the\nVIEWER needs → PresignGet or Delivery.\n\nCapped at MaxGetBytes (8 MiB) because this is for small module-owned control\nfiles — playlists, manifests, sidecars — and a mistyped key should not turn a\n4 GB source video into an OOM. The LimitReader is deliberately MaxGetBytes+1 so\nexceeding the cap is DETECTED rather than silently truncated: a truncated\nplaylist is a subtly broken video, which is far worse to debug than a refusal.\n\nAdditive: one method on Storer and one file. No existing behaviour changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(storage): say why Get is on Storer while PrefixDeleter is not\n\ndelete.go keeps DeletePrefix off Storer on purpose, so an interface method\nappearing here reads like an oversight. It is not: ms.Storage hands every module\nthis interface, and reading your own object is as fundamental as writing one.\nRecording the rule so the next capability is placed on purpose either way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgcsRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcVEQAIQQ4nQxeyjNCtQSLi2chLKQ\nwPki7qV0hwSUScmIiIh9Wbo8G5JVWwS0mO5biycbx/gHB67bLenoFQTM88zxQ5eP\nuIm5nker/pcm83Lr8ABaJiSmFSqLzjUA6I7NpdNJYno0IDkWyeU3NYzLBNuiiW8d\nAqeIu9aqkkqm9BZeb48lBjYqcMQ4U4b0