s://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/334a2b33b543106ab69e82a9be1b8179a0de615e","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKDMzNGEyYjMzYjU0MzEwNmFiNjllODJhOWJlMWI4MTc5YTBkZTYxNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/5d4fbe970827b537d94377301481542657b273a8","sha":"5d4fbe970827b537d94377301481542657b273a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/5d4fbe970827b537d94377301481542657b273a8"}],"sha":"334a2b33b543106ab69e82a9be1b8179a0de615e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/334a2b33b543106ab69e82a9be1b8179a0de615e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/5d4fbe970827b537d94377301481542657b273a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:51:28Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T00:51:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(delivery): gated CDN delivery — platform-minted, fail-closed segment URLs (#179)\n\nServing a segment from a presigned S3 URL makes the bytes uncacheable BY\nCONSTRUCTION: a fresh signature per request is a fresh cache key per request, so\nevery viewer pays a full S3 GET plus egress for every object. A delivery token\nrides the QUERY STRING instead, and the CDN''s cache key is the path only — so\none cached object serves every entitled viewer without fragmenting the cache.\n\nAdds the module-facing half of that:\n\n- ms.DeliveryURL(ctx, key, ttl) — CDN url for ONE gated object, credential\n  attached. One mint per call.\n- ms.Delivery(ctx, prefix, ttl) — ONE credential covering a whole prefix,\n  returned as a DeliveryTicket whose URL method builds a url per object. A\n  transcode job is hundreds of segments across four renditions; minting per\n  segment would spend a platform round trip per playlist line.\n- ms.GatedKeyPrefix (\"_gated/\") — the module-relative prefix that opts an object\n  into gating. Objects outside it are served with no credential at all, so this\n  prefix is the whole difference between a public asset and a paywalled one.\n\nWHO OWNS WHAT. The module owns the ENTITLEMENT DECISION (was the credit charged,\nis the role held); the platform owns the DELIVERY CREDENTIAL. The signing key\nnever reaches the module — DeliveryTicket keeps the token in an unexported field\nwith no accessor, so no call site can build an almost-right url. The module id\ninside the token comes from the caller''s own credential, never from anything the\nmodule sends: the mint envelope has no module field and no app field at all.\n\n🔴 THERE IS NO UNSIGNED FALLBACK. Every failure path returns (\"\", err) — mint\nrefused, dispatch unreachable, or a 200 whose token/param/origin is empty. A\nbare CDN url for gated content is a paywall bypass that looks exactly like a\nworking feature, and those urls land in viewers'' playlists where a rollback\ncannot reach them. A 2xx alone is therefore not treated as evidence of a usable\ncredential; the response is screened before a ticket exists.\n\nCaller-supplied bytes go through an allowlist rather than an escape step. The\nplatform''s canonical signing string is LF-delimited and storage.validateKey does\nNOT reject \"\\n\" (only empty, leading ''/'', \"..\" and ''%''), so a newline key is the\ndelimiter-injection shape. The platform re-checks the composed prefix before\nsigning and the edge checks it again after verifying — this copy exists to fail\nin the caller''s own stack frame, not to be the boundary.\n\npostDispatchJSONInto extends the ONE module->dispatch transport to surfaces that\nneed the response body, so a response-reading surface cannot drift from a\nfire-and-forget one. postDispatchJSON is now a thin call into it.\n\nTests are table-driven and every security-relevant one was mutation-checked:\nunsigned fallback on mint failure, trusting a 200''s token, dropping the ticket''s\narmed check, truncating the ttl proposal to \"unset\", substring instead of prefix\ngating, and dropping the key charset — each flips a passing test.\n\nAdditive only: 4 exported symbols added, none removed or changed, so the release\nPR should carry v0.4.2 (PATCH, pre-1.0 convention). No tag cut here.\n\nDeploy order still governs: the CDN edge must validate tokens BEFORE any module\nemits a CDN url. The reverse order makes every gated object public.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"31440774e0f513813240fbe819ec3289f8ff61bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/31440774e0f513813240fbe819ec3289f8ff61bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/5d4fbe970827b537d94377301481542657b273a8","verification":{"payload":"tree 31440774e0f513813240fbe819ec3289f8ff61bb\nparent bef96624370de7423cfad3a4367d837b6a8058af\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1786841488 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786841488 +0800\n\nfeat(delivery): gated CDN delivery — platform-minted, fail-closed segment URLs (#179)\n\nServing a segment from a presigned S3 URL makes the bytes uncacheable BY\nCONSTRUCTION: a fresh signature per request is a fresh cache key per request, so\nevery viewer pays a full S3 GET plus egress for every object. A delivery token\nrides the QUERY STRING instead, and the CDN''s cache key is the path only — so\none cached object serves every entitled viewer without fragmenting the cache.\n\nAdds the module-facing half of that:\n\n- ms.DeliveryURL(ctx, key, ttl) — CDN url for ONE gated object, credential\n  attached. One mint per call.\n- ms.Delivery(ctx, prefix, ttl) — ONE credential covering a whole prefix,\n  returned as a DeliveryTicket whose URL method builds a url per object. A\n  transcode job is hundreds of segments across four renditions; minting per\n  segment would spend a platform round trip per playlist line.\n- ms.GatedKeyPrefix (\"_gated/\") — the module-relative prefix that opts an object\n  into gating. Objects outside it are served with no credential at all, so this\n  prefix is the whole difference between a public asset and a paywalled one.\n\nWHO OWNS WHAT. The module owns the ENTITLEMENT DECISION (was the credit charged,\nis the role held); the platform owns the DELIVERY CREDENTIAL. The signing key\nnever reaches the module — DeliveryTicket keeps the token in an unexported field\nwith no accessor, so no call site can build an almost-right url. The module id\ninside the token comes from the caller''s own credential, never from anything the\nmodule sends: the mint envelope has no module field and no app field at all.\n\n🔴 THERE IS NO UNSIGNED FALLBACK. Every failure path returns (\"\", err) — mint\nrefused, dispatch unreachable, or a 200 whose token/param/origin is empty. A\nbare CDN url for gated content is a paywall bypass that looks exactly like a\nworking feature, and those urls land in viewers'' playlists where a rollback\ncannot reach them. A 2xx alone is therefore not treated as evidence of a usable\ncredential; the response is screened before a ticket exists.\n\nCaller-supplied bytes go through an allowlist rather than an escape step. The\nplatform''s canonical signing string is LF-delimited and storage.validateKey does\nNOT reject \"\\n\" (only empty, leading ''/'', \"..\" and ''%''), so a newline key is the\ndelimiter-injection shape. The platform re-checks the composed prefix before\nsigning and the edge checks it again after verifying — this copy exists to fail\nin the caller''s own stack frame, not to be the boundary.\n\npostDispatchJSONInto extends the ONE module->dispatch transport to surfaces that\nneed the response body, so a response-reading surface cannot drift from a\nfire-and-forget one. postDispatchJSON is now a thin call into it.\n\nTests are table-driven and every security-relevant one was mutation-checked:\nunsigned fallback on mint failure, trusting a 200''s token, dropping the ticket''s\narmed check, truncating the ttl proposal to \"unset\", substring instead of prefix\ngating, and dropping the key charset — each flips a passing test.\n\nAdditive only: 4 exported symbols added, none removed or changed, so the release\nPR should carry v0.4.2 (PATCH, pre-1.0 convention). No tag cut here.\n\nDeploy order still governs: the CDN edge must validate tokens BEFORE any module\nemits a CDN url. The reverse order makes every gated object public.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgQmQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxFoQAFsXf+KG4ZClmNKUIu5EYJ+m\n5x92nC90GxSbvZvs+gkJtw069Arlikhw6TH8RPYYyUo5xhsUCa1vRBEeWypGBY45\nnyIBOYA4bNLCLeouY3jUT7aUSgTl1DQyvgMvZh8MwV5oajh0+5wwYXE7ggoSoeq5\nD2XCyDTEedYP4og9xfZdX2gqP3ni1LhlZEP6hJA1ptvoK+L6cLnC11A2yyqODmF7\nTDSrV4xqEYyTE55epxFN/X6ChvEMFH2UQVJGR/ME+HlyEWGlQKK9MAW62qSMddoi\nD35k4wl7MJQNbmUDx5TStSc0RWVefP6FhUZi98u77zQ5wxkQybzQtXmaODAhjo8C\nbMRtJeBFbU2Zb8zOhFyDEVxg8gyJmjEIxIhdS/VVPLteO5b/8Yowir1dOyIy7Kcm\nZA2LEJ/sWq8C8OJr6o9aJF/N5XxzCYUPGAb+FY1NcjrAfoRVE0EXIpfkKM74bv4n\npjZfF1FQmTHd+NNxMjrox+sKOrdWhkoY86VLuLK9QdOxsf1QOeBKFdsy5yNvTIes\nQmPV8lQV8Bd4Jry0fxKSwD4yKfyABHdrQcGd9dae9kyT/VO0P4subjto5pZRbT/N\n5UbQ3gzPhpkHXeGv8HVg3lL08UmoGd/LLZ3PiVE7XXWt8UWC+d784jefPlSNLmzR\nqBfLMJjCCBrar6yUX7wm\n=xKOl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-16T00:51:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/5d4fbe970827b537d94377301481542657b273a8","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKDVkNGZiZTk3MDgyN2I1MzdkOTQzNzczMDE0ODE1NDI2NTdiMjczYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/bef96624370de7423cfad3a4367d837b6a8058af","sha":"bef96624370de7423cfad3a4367d837b6a8058af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/bef96624370de7423cfad3a4367d837b6a8058af"}],"sha":"5d4fbe970827b537d94377301481542657b273a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/5d4fbe970827b537d94377301481542657b273a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/bef96624370de7423cfad3a4367d837b6a8058af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T18:08:19Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T18:08:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: release v0.4.1 (#177)\n\nPatch, per the pre-1.0 convention in release.yml''s header: \"patch-only bumps\neven for new SDK surface\". Verified against the API rather than assumed — a\nsymbol diff of every non-internal, non-example package between v0.4.0 and main\nshows 54 exported symbols ADDED and none removed or changed. v0.4.0 took a minor\nfor the opposite reason: an exported constructor''s signature changed there.\n\nThe CHANGELOG carries the one thing the small version step understates —\nms.RunTask lost its synchronous fallback, so a deployed module calling it when\nthe task plane is disabled now gets a loud 503 where it previously ran inline.\nNo shipped module is affected: video-transcode is the only caller and it is not\nreleased.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1933744d888dbdbcf58e21bdce077144f4e13d51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/1933744d888dbdbcf58e21bdce077144f4e13d51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/bef96624370de7423cfad3a4367d837b6a8058af","verification":{"payload":"tree 1933744d888dbdbcf58e21bdce077144f4e13d51\nparent 463e2a14c680b20e27405e6db9b871987dfb6a11\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1786817299 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786817299 +0800\n\nchore: release v0.4.1 (#177)\n\nPatch, per the pre-1.0 convention in release.yml''s header: \"patch-only bumps\neven for new SDK surface\". Verified against the API rather than assumed — a\nsymbol diff of every non-internal, non-example package between v0.4.0 and main\nshows 54 exported symbols ADDED and none removed or changed. v0.4.0 took a minor\nfor the opposite reason: an exported constructor''s signature changed there.\n\nThe CHANGELOG carries the one thing the small version step understates —\nms.RunTask lost its synchronous fallback, so a deployed module calling it when\nthe task plane is disabled now gets a loud 503 where it previously ran inline.\nNo shipped module is affected: video-transcode is the only caller and it is not\nreleased.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgKsTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEVEQACPN/x/kSyKX2NCM6Fu9qAtI\nLVmMo+caa6aKnVh3Q5YzNpSAKs4xGfVQco4qnbz7LAFNeSiU7+tFcdMsTSy+XPgR\n66ydNcSikEY1nv3ufaVa9ftRNt4nrQd5vA58Zv0kV27Q7XI390D46AC18/4gc0mj\nWdWhfLK766kCJLuGqPdv7EFJuwMkwyBf8bvZxMMaLGXImwR/k4YabW8P6QVAITA7\n+tNIqedF6hZod4AkkIrsBOzOKXc+d8Lr0F5ZwhUpCL6LNBI2KokwAnz2bWM17H5y\ngFDLIQ5uTPujowmodAFOBLRce8886gWeuJ+wfu5LdPuTIJVG0LoKGcei4Ve43s3e\nBXDkulo8JM0jG01GqBs+qXEcxnklvyRS015tZberf594nmouOvkxhh1SSX0wRHFk\nYMDF6WkcLMr9eHv0oiMfOspLA4xI+yzJ1yLUc1bX/bB/+/FtPC5BdU6foM9Q4RkG\ngbLaaev2fAjZMIJP47055XtrBBpYLgoRuke7zT78l+BSktCH5jBWM/SXhIhx4pMF\nHzBJSzf6RCYUR1xSnZXkdrlEZgNn/WmCVXLuMllK1sfu2B15Tj1avOKEb1lUvqdv\nNMqGYuOzPhGSTHnITuD3/wDV0qTZR3x2ZV0EhxgD2Rro030fnzyMlsK/vn1q3rsE\nQX50oPczOI8qOavxw4hR\n=4No0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-15T18:08:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/bef96624370de7423cfad3a4367d837b6a8058af","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKGJlZjk2NjI0MzcwZGU3NDIzY2ZhZDNhNDM2N2Q4MzdiNmE4MDU4YWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/463e2a14c680b20e27405e6db9b871987dfb6a11","sha":"463e2a14c680b20e27405e6db9b871987dfb6a11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/463e2a14c680b20e27405e6db9b871987dfb6a11"}],"sha":"bef96624370de7423cfad3a4367d837b6a8058af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/bef96624370de7423cfad3a4367d837b6a8058af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/463e2a14c680b20e27405e6db9b871987dfb6a11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-15T07:15:57Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-15T07:15:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(tasks): one-shot task runtime — broker claim, renewable resources, secure module calls (#156)\n\n* feat: declare a task''s compute class in the manifest\n\nTasks execute on the module''s own Lambda, so OnTask has always inherited\nLambda''s 15-minute ceiling and modest vCPU allocation. A four-rendition\nencode of one source hour needs ~90 minutes on 4 vCPU; no API shape makes\nthat fit. The gap is a missing execution tier, not a missing abstraction.\n\nA task may now declare ms.Standard (Lambda, the default), ms.Heavy\n(Fargate) or ms.GPU (ECS on EC2 — Fargate has no GPU support, so it is a\ndifferent runner rather than a flag). The request rides the manifest at\ntasks[].compute so the platform provisions the right runner at deploy from\nthe declaration alone, the same mechanism that already provisions the SQS\nqueue — and so the app owner sees it at install, the same trust root that\nalready governs dependencies and exposed tables.\n\nThe default does not move. A task registered without WithCompute produces\na byte-identical manifest entry, so no module lands on expensive compute\nbecause the SDK grew a field.\n\nSizing is validated at declaration and panics at startup like ExposeTable\n— a resource request that only fails at deploy is the worst of both\nworlds. VCPU on Standard is refused because Lambda derives vCPU from\nmemory and cannot honour it; Heavy is checked against Fargate''s real\nCPU/memory matrix (0.5 vCPU + 512 MB is rejected: 512 MB is legal at\n0.25 vCPU and nowhere else); GPU takes an allowlisted instance and refuses\nVCPU/MemoryMB alongside it, since g4dn.xlarge IS 4 vCPU / 16 GB. The\nmatrix and allowlist are data, and the panic messages render from that\nsame data so the stated rule cannot drift from the enforced one.\n\nAlso re-exports WithTimeout and WithMaxRetries, which existed and were\nadvertised by OnTask''s doc comment but were never reachable from ms.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(tasks): one-shot task runtime — broker claim, renewable resources, secure module calls\n\nReplaces the legacy credential-bearing SQS/HMAC worker with a one-shot process\nthat claims exactly one attempt from the platform task broker and reports one\nterminal outcome.\n\n- internal/runtime/task_broker.go: the authenticated broker client (claim,\n  heartbeat, complete, fail).\n- internal/runtime/task_claim_file.go: the generic runner''s preclaimed handoff,\n  rejecting symlinks, group/world-readable modes, size ambiguity and trailing\n  JSON so a less-protected source cannot be substituted.\n- internal/core/local_task.go: dev mode runs tasks in a process-local idempotent\n  executor, so TaskStatus/CancelTask behave the same locally and deployed.\n- Renewable resource providers for db/cache/storage, so a long task refreshes\n  credentials instead of dying on an expired one mid-job.\n- storage.Delete, and presigned PUTs that carry an exact Content-Length.\n- internal/sqs is deleted: nothing routes through a module-held queue credential\n  any more.\n\nTwo defects the review pass caught, both in the identity/auth path:\n\n- claimIdentityMatches asserted equality on the module SLUG as well as the UUID.\n  The slug is a display label and rename is supported, so every in-flight task\n  of a renamed module failed identity validation — in the branch that also skips\n  the terminal failure callback, so the job hung until the watchdog expired it,\n  once per retry. Identity is the canonical module UUID.\n- isCanonicalCallPath scanned the whole request target for %2f/%2e/%23/%5c,\n  including the query. A query value legitimately carries those, so one of them\n  vetoed classification: ms.Call then silently dropped the actor delegation\n  header and ms.CallDependency hard-rejected the call. It fired on the OAuth\n  authorize-url hop, whose query is an encoded redirect_uri, every time. The\n  scan now covers the path only, matching the platform ingress.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d2508aae233cc6c6e2278d5cc3674cbc902cb7a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/d2508aae233cc6c6e2278d5cc3674cbc902cb7a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/463e2a14c680b20e27405e6db9b871987dfb6a11","verification":{"payload":"tree d2508aae233cc6c6e2278d5cc3674cbc902cb7a4\nparent 78b5912cf68e6e107f0b60ee2608d765b02bb5a1\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1786778157 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786778157 +0800\n\nfeat(tasks): one-shot task runtime — broker claim, renewable resources, secure module calls (#156)\n\n* feat: declare a task''s compute class in the manifest\n\nTasks execute on the module''s own Lambda, so OnTask has always inherited\nLambda''s 15-minute ceiling and modest vCPU allocation. A four-rendition\nencode of one source hour needs ~90 minutes on 4 vCPU; no API shape makes\nthat fit. The gap is a missing execution tier, not a missing abstraction.\n\nA task may now declare ms.Standard (Lambda, the default), ms.Heavy\n(Fargate) or ms.GPU (ECS on EC2 — Fargate has no GPU support, so it is a\ndifferent runner rather than a flag). The request rides the manifest at\ntasks[].compute so the platform provisions the right runner at deploy from\nthe declaration alone, the same mechanism that already provisions the SQS\nqueue — and so the app owner sees it at install, the same trust root that\nalready governs dependencies and exposed tables.\n\nThe default does not move. A task registered without WithCompute produces\na byte-identical manifest entry, so no module lands on expensive compute\nbecause the SDK grew a field.\n\nSizing is validated at declaration and panics at startup like ExposeTable\n— a resource request that only fails at deploy is the worst of both\nworlds. VCPU on Standard is refused because Lambda derives vCPU from\nmemory and cannot honour it; Heavy is checked against Fargate''s real\nCPU/memory matrix (0.5 vCPU + 512 MB is rejected: 512 MB is legal at\n0.25 vCPU and nowhere else); GPU takes an allowlisted instance and refuses\nVCPU/MemoryMB alongside it, since g4dn.xlarge IS 4 vCPU / 16 GB. The\nmatrix and allowlist are data, and the panic messages render from that\nsame data so the stated rule cannot drift from the enforced one.\n\nAlso re-exports WithTimeout and WithMaxRetries, which existed and were\nadvertised by OnTask''s doc comment but were never reachable from ms.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(tasks): one-shot task runtime — broker claim, renewable resources, secure module calls\n\nReplaces the legacy credential-bearing SQS/HMAC worker with a one-shot process\nthat claims exactly one attempt from the platform task broker and reports one\nterminal outcome.\n\n- internal/runtime/task_broker.go: the authenticated broker client (claim,\n  heartbeat, complete, fail).\n- internal/runtime/task_claim_file.go: the generic runner''s preclaimed handoff,\n  rejecting symlinks, group/world-readable modes, size ambiguity and trailing\n  JSON so a less-protected source cannot be substituted.\n- internal/core/local_task.go: dev mode runs tasks in a process-local idempotent\n  executor, so TaskStatus/CancelTask behave the same locally and deployed.\n- Renewable resource providers for db/cache/storage, so a long task refreshes\n  credentials instead of dying on an expired one mid-job.\n- storage.Delete, and presigned PUTs that carry an exact Content-Length.\n- internal/sqs is deleted: nothing routes through a module-held queue credential\n  any more.\n\nTwo defects the review pass caught, both in the identity/auth path:\n\n- claimIdentityMatches asserted equality on the module SLUG as well as the UUID.\n  The slug is a display label and rename is supported, so every in-flight task\n  of a renamed module failed identity validation — in the branch that also skips\n  the terminal failure callback, so the job hung until the watchdog expired it,\n  once per retry. Identity is the canonical module UUID.\n- isCanonicalCallPath scanned the whole request target for %2f/%2e/%23/%5c,\n  including the query. A query value legitimately carries those, so one of them\n  vetoed classification: ms.Call then silently dropped the actor delegation\n  header and ms.CallDependency hard-rejected the call. It fired on the OAuth\n  authorize-url hop, whose query is an encoded redirect_uri, every time. The\n  scan now covers the path only, matching the platform ingress.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgBItCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6hsQACCGXYZeIlKGJO9YWXD20GjM\nrj5pAD6iBaZRmnchMfVBAkkt6wZsUcDZ2dHFlCxN107Jvjuq8kSgB1OajSZqLXSY\nuJqCd86GjJx/Y1bT20JtgKqIvZf9plaraGWZWHVTIi6oY4PTOmGty9n3C/csgito\nSTs83gjzRhhia7C5QTNcJFv+7nVVpBF5p6iMCa80N9MqXn1kkM0rcvSM5PI2Qd0l\nczrkGv8qIoDYsaJ6WUrbWJaD/WGUntHNqByikn3MMkpz25QIUBqMoiEZ08+8Qj/q\nHHAuJ2TKDlzFuPUHE1gGVb7c8X1MRkEBamccWO6GB/eplbTPuZtRj/Ijb9294NFS\nxaQUdOjZtf/kWZZHRcTJduXOjip+MDuYKV/UeSF9roGssDI3EKbd57+hHELZM+ei\n0eZZtToL7eobmkBdjxiEhsV5eRf864b15lr6+z17sPdjRAw6y/zDD/8vSfGP+q1B\n5dWzc2ieixcmPUEm0UpCAfIFzvGM2YKGhcZpcnrKEkNEQhmLAvC+W43BxiHJapQP\nXpMbLRD6XgwbGcO+8a+qvyQoXCvjISsi6cJZto0W4CMqa9+t3PQvGfnTZNuG954O\npc7KyJ2Jb7g8DiPrcogJqui7V5j+CxcRK7hSHPJ1klMhIh3gW/g2Tu134Vkeg1y0\nRUsQ8SuUyyZzVWeR5MpW\n=Hv1Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-15T07:15:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/463e2a14c680b20e27405e6db9b871987dfb6a11","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKDQ2M2UyYTE0YzY4MGIyMGUyNzQwNWU2ZGI5Yjg3MTk4N2RmYjZhMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/78b5912cf68e6e107f0b60ee2608d765b02bb5a1","sha":"78b5912cf68e6e107f0b60ee2608d765b02bb5a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/78b5912cf68e6e107f0b60ee2608d765b02bb5a1"}],"sha":"463e2a14c680b20e27405e6db9b871987dfb6a11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/463e2a14c680b20e27405e6db9b871987dfb6a11"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/78b5912cf68e6e107f0b60ee2608d765b02bb5a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T14:48:31Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T14:48:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(manifest): localize UI page titles and descriptions (#176)\n\nThe module nav rail in web-applications renders\nmanifest.ui.defaultPages[].title, which had no locale channel anywhere in\nthe chain — so a Traditional-Chinese app showed an English nav label even\nthough defaults.nameLabels has carried per-locale module names since #137.\n\nAdd TitleLabels/DescriptionLabels to UIPage, populated from the module''s\nmanifest i18n catalog exactly the way NameLabels/TagLabels already are.\nThe catalog key is the page''s existing (Surface, Route) identity —\nvalidateUI''s own dedup key — spelled ui.pages.<surface>.<route>.title, with\nthe empty main surface written \"main\" and the route used verbatim so there\nis no slug rule to remember and no way for two routes to collide.\n\nBackward compatibility is the whole risk here: both maps are omitempty and\nthe plain Title/Description stay the non-localized fallback, so every\nalready-deployed module keeps serving byte-identical page fields. Empty\nper-locale values are emitted verbatim rather than filtered, because a\ncatalog-parity check is satisfied by adding a key with an empty value while\nthe translation is still pending — consumers must resolve with logical-OR,\nnever ??, or a pending translation renders as a blank nav item.\n\nAlso deep-copy the new maps in cloneUI: DefaultPages was a shallow\nslices.Clone, which would have aliased an author-set map into the registry.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"184f42f1dfd7eaf75be46be457a3982c8070edfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/184f42f1dfd7eaf75be46be457a3982c8070edfc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/78b5912cf68e6e107f0b60ee2608d765b02bb5a1","verification":{"payload":"tree 184f42f1dfd7eaf75be46be457a3982c8070edfc\nparent e49d299510dad9712046d507d0ca8daa1cdd653c\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1786459711 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786459711 +0800\n\nfeat(manifest): localize UI page titles and descriptions (#176)\n\nThe module nav rail in web-applications renders\nmanifest.ui.defaultPages[].title, which had no locale channel anywhere in\nthe chain — so a Traditional-Chinese app showed an English nav label even\nthough defaults.nameLabels has carried per-locale module names since #137.\n\nAdd TitleLabels/DescriptionLabels to UIPage, populated from the module''s\nmanifest i18n catalog exactly the way NameLabels/TagLabels already are.\nThe catalog key is the page''s existing (Surface, Route) identity —\nvalidateUI''s own dedup key — spelled ui.pages.<surface>.<route>.title, with\nthe empty main surface written \"main\" and the route used verbatim so there\nis no slug rule to remember and no way for two routes to collide.\n\nBackward compatibility is the whole risk here: both maps are omitempty and\nthe plain Title/Description stay the non-localized fallback, so every\nalready-deployed module keeps serving byte-identical page fields. Empty\nper-locale values are emitted verbatim rather than filtered, because a\ncatalog-parity check is satisfied by adding a key with an empty value while\nthe translation is still pending — consumers must resolve with logical-OR,\nnever ??, or a pending translation renders as a blank nav item.\n\nAlso deep-copy the new maps in cloneUI: DefaultPages was a shallow\nslices.Clone, which would have aliased an author-set map into the registry.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqezY/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgKIQAEtZcspGD3YX2XZlVeOSiaXQ\nY+lmMqi4iCSJEZq8177wH2kSNt3AeZgevceTa6+7ozHGlM+iX6RhLvUhjvCuO35n\nYgcF+0l3Ma1mOt3OQzzF5fB9enIyGtct2SU2UBgzG4ZXt3CDpjDvhaepQC8LB2oq\nEiqmge4N2EdOzR0COIS0pqgVxsAzq5DQ7YcucFmFBd4HTpkRq2lxHkJXsHMrAiZ1\nyf1pcuzSx9fpqdpDhNG3EwwlGhRZOnCZs8F/fF/69nbADigdlPTfQjIV6rVfCGWC\nXQLuerzr8IvPg+nIFnPsylqgwqw0Zj6Ly1SG7h8OB4ToPTAqX5J6y9PfGg+BUlGe\nuR8VTrPRTLn7mEL3Y5nmiHvhW7qWlDhNgivRUXNo0zeGiDMt2TBNIp7rIhU2GsCY\nzh0J3pYtXp1gs0OMo4jPjbnTq7u+9rXdC+HGxgRpN6GzKgafwLqzv8b8LDJm7Dyb\nGWT9qKBtYMGW8x7odmU/PQPzustj4r9vDntncuNLHfrmRrDgTlfiVPG+LYmDjW8b\nc/x7sbqMBj/CL0mPbYFTcl/R2vsjz0L40ZdIoH1YsrsWKBNUqiPvRbD778at5y/6\nJlDfNiy135upBltlwT9v21ZYd24OvDaKuo8cPQ2DrUfXiHFbm0TzlrDgo+2oHjcG\nZSSvjx/agufanw/POYZU\n=6sr/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T14:58:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/78b5912cf68e6e107f0b60ee2608d765b02bb5a1","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKDc4YjU5MTJjZjY4ZTZlMTA3ZjBiNjBlZTI2MDhkNzY1YjAyYmI1YTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/e49d299510dad9712046d507d0ca8daa1cdd653c","sha":"e49d299510dad9712046d507d0ca8daa1cdd653c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/e49d299510dad9712046d507d0ca8daa1cdd653c"}],"sha":"78b5912cf68e6e107f0b60ee2608d765b02bb5a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/78b5912cf68e6e107f0b60ee2608d765b02bb5a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/e49d299510dad9712046d507d0ca8daa1cdd653c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T22:35:53Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T22:35:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: audit trails as a module principle (#174)\n\n* docs: audit trails as a module principle\n\nTwo modules now record provenance — users-roles for role grants and\nrevocations, oauth-core for session revocations — and they landed on different\nshapes for reasons worth writing down before a third module guesses.\n\nThe failure this documents is not a missing feature. It is a trail that is\nBELIEVED and wrong: incomplete, invented, or attributable to whoever the caller\nsaid they were. Each rule here comes from something that actually went wrong.\n\n- Ledger for repeating events, provenance columns for terminal ones. Columns for\n  a repeating event silently overwrite history, which looks like an audit trail\n  while destroying evidence. users-roles kept granted_by on the current row and\n  revoked with a DELETE, so its trail was being shredded by design.\n- Provenance is (actor, via), never a lone nullable actor, which cannot tell\n  \"the platform did it\" from \"a human did it and we could not identify them\"\n  from \"we forgot to record it\".\n- The actor comes from the request context only, and better still is derived\n  from the row being modified — unforgeable by construction rather than by\n  validation. Validate it against the column type first: a synthetic non-uuid\n  dev identity written to a uuid column failed with 22P02 and rolled back an\n  enclosing transaction. An unidentifiable actor must never refuse the\n  operation, because authorization was already settled and identity is not\n  authorization.\n- Coverage belongs in the mutating statement, not at call sites. Eleven call\n  sites across five paths mutate one table in users-roles, one of them outside\n  internal/. A data-modifying CTE whose RETURNING feeds the audit insert cannot\n  be forgotten, and gets no-phantom-events for free: an ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING\n  grant returns no rows, so a re-grant appends nothing.\n- A bounded read must say it is bounded, or the newest N reads as the whole\n  history.\n- Never backfill, never FK to the described entity, never gate the read on an\n  Internal route — that scope is actorless, so RequirePermission 401s for the\n  identity ms.Call sends, and a host that degrades a failed fetch to \"no audit\n  section\" turns that into \"this subject has no history\".\n\n* docs: correct section 7 — Internal is not a browser boundary on the dev plane\n\nSection 7 claimed \"Internal scope is itself the boundary; the path is not\nbrowser-reachable\" and prescribed gating a Platform-scope read instead. Both\nhalves are false against api-platform today: the dev-tunnel dispatch mount is\nunauthenticated at the HTTP edge, the handler''s only path-shape rejection\ncovers the __mirrorstack namespace so an /internal/ path is forwarded to the\nmodule, and the handler injects a hardcoded admin app-role. A dev-mounted\nmodule''s Internal route is therefore browser-reachable with a fabricated\nprivileged identity; the 5-condition dev gate protects the plane, not the\ncaller.\n\nKeeps the original correct point — an actorless transport cannot be\npermission-gated, so re-adding the gate is not the fix — and states the\nplatform-side gap plainly instead of a boundary that does not exist.\n\nTwo further claims were re-checked against current code and corrected:\n\n- The intro said two modules \"already follow it\". users-roles'' actingUser\n  still returns an error on an absent or malformed operator UUID, which is\n  exactly the refusal section 3 forbids, so they now \"supply the examples\".\n\n- The checklist required a migration to be advertised in ms.Init''s Versions\n  map \"or it never runs\". api-platform has no consumer of the manifest\n  versions map; the upgrade window''s target counter comes from migration_app,\n  which the SDK derives from Config.SQL via migration.LatestVersion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: scope the Internal-edge gap to both planes\n\n* docs: state the Internal-edge gap without the dev-only scoping\n\nThe previous commit corrected the \"Internal is not browser-reachable\" claim\nbut closed section 7 by scoping the gap to the dev plane: \"Production modules\nare not dev-mounted, so the dev-tunnel branch described here does not apply\nthere.\" Only the first half of that survives contact with api-platform.\n\nThe dev-tunnel branch indeed does not serve deployed modules, but the same\nunauthenticated /module edge carries a SECOND branch for a module with a\ndeploy row, and that branch skips the dev conditions (app dev-mode, install\nrow, live tunnel) entirely before invoking the deployed function with the same\nfabricated identity — owner user id, app role \"admin\", plus the platform''s own\ninternal secret. Verified with a throwaway test against\ninternal/dispatch/handler: an anonymous GET /module/{id}/internal/audit/roles\nagainst a module with every dev precondition FALSE returned 200, and the\ninvoke envelope carried path=/internal/audit/roles with appRole=\"admin\". The\ndev-tunnel twin behaves identically. So the gap belongs to the /module browser\nedge, not to dev-mounting, and the old closing paragraph read as a reassurance\nthe code does not support.\n\nSection 7 is also de-duplicated: the scope is now stated once rather than\nasserted \"on the dev plane\" in two paragraphs and contradicted in a third.\n\nTwo smaller corrections in the same section:\n\n- \"its only path-shape rejection covers the __mirrorstack namespace\" conflated\n  two different guards. __mirrorstack is the only NAMESPACE refused; the\n  handler does have other path-shape checks (empty/./.. segments, a raw\n  fragment) — they simply do not cover /internal/.\n\n- The checklist''s \"safe to expose to anyone who can reach the dev edge\" is\n  widened to the /module edge on either plane, matching the above.\n\nThe claims kept from the previous commit were each re-verified rather than\nassumed: ms.Call sends app id + the CALLING module''s service secret and no\nactor (dispatch injects the callee''s internal secret); auth.RequireRoles 401s\nonly when the identity is nil or the role empty, so the 401 is conditional on\nno role being fabricated, which is how the text already puts it; and the\nfive-condition dev gate is named exactly as dispatch documents it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: state the Internal-edge mechanism the code actually has\n\nThe review found this branch reintroducing the defect it exists to remove —\nasserting a mechanism the code does not have. Four corrections, all verified\nagainst api-platform and this SDK:\n\n- audit.md §7 claimed RequirePermission returns 401 for an actorless ms.Call.\n  It cannot. internal/core/module.go:521 compiles RequirePermission to\n  auth.RequireRoles(admin, ...declared), and every /module forward stamps\n  X-MS-App-Role: admin (dev_tunnel.go:734 tunnel, :867 lambda,\n  dev_tunnel_relay.go:113 relay), so the gate ADMITS rather than rejects.\n  The advice stands; the reason is silent admission, not a denial.\n- The production-incident narrative was downstream of that unreachable 401.\n  Re-grounded on failures the edge really produces — not_installed 404,\n  route_local_off / tunnel_offline 503, resolver 500 — all of which ms.Call\n  surfaces as an error (call.go:104).\n- scopes.md still carried the deleted invariant on a page audit.md links:\n  \"the SDK rejects anything else with 401\", \"disjoint auth domains\", \"default\n  to Internal ... you can''t put auth back after leaking\". Corrected on both\n  the English and zh-TW pages, with the auth matrix scoped to what it really\n  describes (SDK middleware, secret configured — not reachability).\n- §7 said the deployed branch skips all five dev conditions. It skips four:\n  transport_resolver.go:103 -> catalog.go:327 resolves the deploy through the\n  app''s own module_install row, so a missing install (or un-bootstrapped\n  schema) still yields no transport.\n\nAlso corrects internal-calls.md, audit.md''s other See-also, which justified\ndropping Internal CORS with \"a browser never originates an Internal call\".\nA browser can; dispatch just writes the Allow-Origin itself on that surface\n(dev_tunnel.go:521 writePerAppCORS), so the conclusion survives the reason.\n\nDocs only.\n\n* docs: land the audit advice, cite the truth suites for the mechanism\n\nThis page was rejected twice for asserting platform auth mechanisms the code\ndoes not have. Rather than iterate on the prose a third time, strip the\nmechanism narration and keep the advice it was there to justify.\n\nRemoved from audit.md §7, all unverified or false against current main:\nthe `/module` edge being unauthenticated at the HTTP layer, a fabricated\n`X-MS-App-Role: admin`, dispatch injecting the target module''s internal\nsecret, the deployed branch consulting none of the dev conditions, and the\nenumerated edge error codes. The same claims are removed from scopes.md\n(both locales) and from internal-calls.md §3.\n\nWhat replaces them is a citation. Two characterization suites merged for\nexactly this purpose and are the executable statement of the trust model:\n`auth_scope_truth_test.go` here, and api-platform''s\n`internal/dispatch/handler/module_edge_truth_test.go` +\n`module_edge_router_wiring_test.go`. Facts about the edge are now named by\ntest rather than paraphrased, so CI contradicts a stale document instead of\na reviewer having to remember.\n\nThe advice is unchanged and is the point of the page: no `RequirePermission`\non an `Internal` read, the audit write inside the mutating statement, record\n`(actor, via)` and never a lone actor, actor from ctx only, and never gate\nthe audit read on an actorless call.\n\nAlso corrected against source:\n- scopes.md''s auth matrix was wrong in both directions. Replaced with a\n  measured table taken from the real `m.Router()`, and dropped the\n  \"disjoint auth domains\" claim — one `X-MS-Internal-Secret` authenticates\n  both `InternalAuth` and `PlatformAuth`.\n- §4''s \"five logical paths\" was not verifiable; the eleven `user_roles` call\n  sites span four files, one outside `internal/`.\n- §3''s 22P02 account now separates the 500 from the `ms.Tx` rollback.\n- internal-calls.md §3 keeps its \"today\" antecedent, with the CORS gate\n  stated as `auth.SecretConfigured()` rather than the stale `MS_INTERNAL_SECRET`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b5dc807281081dab65629a3ba17ef39f77455704","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/b5dc807281081dab65629a3ba17ef39f77455704"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/e49d299510dad9712046d507d0ca8daa1cdd653c","verification":{"payload":"tree b5dc807281081dab65629a3ba17ef39f77455704\nparent b6bbfbb7e7cc59f586653a1484cecaac581d721e\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1786401353 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786401353 +0800\n\ndocs: audit trails as a module principle (#174)\n\n* docs: audit trails as a module principle\n\nTwo modules now record provenance — users-roles for role grants and\nrevocations, oauth-core for session revocations — and they landed on different\nshapes for reasons worth writing down before a third module guesses.\n\nThe failure this documents is not a missing feature. It is a trail that is\nBELIEVED and wrong: incomplete, invented, or attributable to whoever the caller\nsaid they were. Each rule here comes from something that actually went wrong.\n\n- Ledger for repeating events, provenance columns for terminal ones. Columns for\n  a repeating event silently overwrite history, which looks like an audit trail\n  while destroying evidence. users-roles kept granted_by on the current row and\n  revoked with a DELETE, so its trail was being shredded by design.\n- Provenance is (actor, via), never a lone nullable actor, which cannot tell\n  \"the platform did it\" from \"a human did it and we could not identify them\"\n  from \"we forgot to record it\".\n- The actor comes from the request context only, and better still is derived\n  from the row being modified — unforgeable by construction rather than by\n  validation. Validate it against the column type first: a synthetic non-uuid\n  dev identity written to a uuid column failed with 22P02 and rolled back an\n  enclosing transaction. An unidentifiable actor must never refuse the\n  operation, because authorization was already settled and identity is not\n  authorization.\n- Coverage belongs in the mutating statement, not at call sites. Eleven call\n  sites across five paths mutate one table in users-roles, one of them outside\n  internal/. A data-modifying CTE whose RETURNING feeds the audit insert cannot\n  be forgotten, and gets no-phantom-events for free: an ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING\n  grant returns no rows, so a re-grant appends nothing.\n- A bounded read must say it is bounded, or the newest N reads as the whole\n  history.\n- Never backfill, never FK to the described entity, never gate the read on an\n  Internal route — that scope is actorless, so RequirePermission 401s for the\n  identity ms.Call sends, and a host that degrades a failed fetch to \"no audit\n  section\" turns that into \"this subject has no history\".\n\n* docs: correct section 7 — Internal is not a browser boundary on the dev plane\n\nSection 7 claimed \"Internal scope is itself the boundary; the path is not\nbrowser-reachable\" and prescribed gating a Platform-scope read instead. Both\nhalves are false against api-platform today: the dev-tunnel dispatch mount is\nunauthenticated at the HTTP edge, the handler''s only path-shape rejection\ncovers the __mirrorstack namespace so an /internal/ path is forwarded to the\nmodule, and the handler injects a hardcoded admin app-role. A dev-mounted\nmodule''s Internal route is therefore browser-reachable with a fabricated\nprivileged identity; the 5-condition dev gate protects the plane, not the\ncaller.\n\nKeeps the original correct point — an actorless transport cannot be\npermission-gated, so re-adding the gate is not the fix — and states the\nplatform-side gap plainly instead of a boundary that does not exist.\n\nTwo further claims were re-checked against current code and corrected:\n\n- The intro said two modules \"already follow it\". users-roles'' actingUser\n  still returns an error on an absent or malformed operator UUID, which is\n  exactly the refusal section 3 forbids, so they now \"supply the examples\".\n\n- The checklist required a migration to be advertised in ms.Init''s Versions\n  map \"or it never runs\". api-platform has no consumer of the manifest\n  versions map; the upgrade window''s target counter comes from migration_app,\n  which the SDK derives from Config.SQL via migration.LatestVersion.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: scope the Internal-edge gap to both planes\n\n* docs: state the Internal-edge gap without the dev-only scoping\n\nThe previous commit corrected the \"Internal is not browser-reachable\" claim\nbut closed section 7 by scoping the gap to the dev plane: \"Production modules\nare not dev-mounted, so the dev-tunnel branch described here does not apply\nthere.\" Only the first half of that survives contact with api-platform.\n\nThe dev-tunnel branch indeed does not serve deployed modules, but the same\nunauthenticated /module edge carries a SECOND branch for a module with a\ndeploy row, and that branch skips the dev conditions (app dev-mode, install\nrow, live tunnel) entirely before invoking the deployed function with the same\nfabricated identity — owner user id, app role \"admin\", plus the platform''s own\ninternal secret. Verified with a throwaway test against\ninternal/dispatch/handler: an anonymous GET /module/{id}/internal/audit/roles\nagainst a module with every dev precondition FALSE returned 200, and the\ninvoke envelope carried path=/internal/audit/roles with appRole=\"admin\". The\ndev-tunnel twin behaves identically. So the gap belongs to the /module browser\nedge, not to dev-mounting, and the old closing paragraph read as a reassurance\nthe code does not support.\n\nSection 7 is also de-duplicated: the scope is now stated once rather than\nasserted \"on the dev plane\" in two paragraphs and contradicted in a third.\n\nTwo smaller corrections in the same section:\n\n- \"its only path-shape rejection covers the __mirrorstack namespace\" conflated\n  two different guards. __mirrorstack is the only NAMESPACE refused; the\n  handler does have other path-shape checks (empty/./.. segments, a raw\n  fragment) — they simply do not cover /internal/.\n\n- The checklist''s \"safe to expose to anyone who can reach the dev edge\" is\n  widened to the /module edge on either plane, matching the above.\n\nThe claims kept from the previous commit were each re-verified rather than\nassumed: ms.Call sends app id + the CALLING module''s service secret and no\nactor (dispatch injects the callee''s internal secret); auth.RequireRoles 401s\nonly when the identity is nil or the role empty, so the 401 is conditional on\nno role being fabricated, which is how the text already puts it; and the\nfive-condition dev gate is named exactly as dispatch documents it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: state the Internal-edge mechanism the code actually has\n\nThe review found this branch reintroducing the defect it exists to remove —\nasserting a mechanism the code does not have. Four corrections, all verified\nagainst api-platform and this SDK:\n\n- audit.md §7 claimed RequirePermission returns 401 for an actorless ms.Call.\n  It cannot. internal/core/module.go:521 compiles RequirePermission to\n  auth.RequireRoles(admin, ...declared), and every /module forward stamps\n  X-MS-App-Role: admin (dev_tunnel.go:734 tunnel, :867 lambda,\n  dev_tunnel_relay.go:113 relay), so the gate ADMITS rather than rejects.\n  The advice stands; the reason is silent admission, not a denial.\n- The production-incident narrative was downstream of that unreachable 401.\n  Re-grounded on failures the edge really produces — not_installed 404,\n  route_local_off / tunnel_offline 503, resolver 500 — all of which ms.Call\n  surfaces as an error (call.go:104).\n- scopes.md still carried the deleted invariant on a page audit.md links:\n  \"the SDK rejects anything else with 401\", \"disjoint auth domains\", \"default\n  to Internal ... you can''t put auth back after leaking\". Corrected on both\n  the English and zh-TW pages, with the auth matrix scoped to what it really\n  describes (SDK middleware, secret configured — not reachability).\n- §7 said the deployed branch skips all five dev conditions. It skips four:\n  transport_resolver.go:103 -> catalog.go:327 resolves the deploy through the\n  app''s own module_install row, so a missing install (or un-bootstrapped\n  schema) still yields no transport.\n\nAlso corrects internal-calls.md, audit.md''s other See-also, which justified\ndropping Internal CORS with \"a browser never originates an Internal call\".\nA browser can; dispatch just writes the Allow-Origin itself on that surface\n(dev_tunnel.go:521 writePerAppCORS), so the conclusion survives the reason.\n\nDocs only.\n\n* docs: land the audit advice, cite the truth suites for the mechanism\n\nThis page was rejected twice for asserting platform auth mechanisms the code\ndoes not have. Rather than iterate on the prose a third time, strip the\nmechanism narration and keep the advice it was there to justify.\n\nRemoved from audit.md §7, all unverified or false against current main:\nthe `/module` edge being unauthenticated at the HTTP layer, a fabricated\n`X-MS-App-Role: admin`, dispatch injecting the target module''s internal\nsecret, the deployed branch consulting none of the dev conditions, and the\nenumerated edge error codes. The same claims are removed from scopes.md\n(both locales) and from internal-calls.md §3.\n\nWhat replaces them is a citation. Two characterization suites merged for\nexactly this purpose and are the executable statement of the trust model:\n`auth_scope_truth_test.go` here, and api-platform''s\n`internal/dispatch/handler/module_edge_truth_test.go` +\n`module_edge_router_wiring_test.go`. Facts about the edge are now named by\ntest rather than paraphrased, so CI contradicts a stale document instead of\na reviewer having to remember.\n\nThe advice is unchanged and is the point of the page: no `RequirePermission`\non an `Internal` read, the audit write inside the mutating statement, record\n`(actor, via)` and never a lone actor, actor from ctx only, and never gate\nthe audit read on an actorless call.\n\nAlso corrected against source:\n- scopes.md''s auth matrix was wrong in both directions. Replaced with a\n  measured table taken from the real `m.Router()`, and dropped the\n  \"disjoint auth domains\" claim — one `X-MS-Internal-Secret` authenticates\n  both `InternalAuth` and `PlatformAuth`.\n- §4''s \"five logical paths\" was not verifiable; the eleven `user_roles` call\n  sites span four files, one outside `internal/`.\n- §3''s 22P02 account now separates the 500 from the `ms.Tx` rollback.\n- internal-calls.md §3 keeps its \"today\" antecedent, with the CORS gate\n  stated as `auth.SecretConfigured()` rather than the stale `MS_INTERNAL_SECRET`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqelJJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8aMQAHJ8dTzR3T1dbKbIXbFuxiyr\nl+/pPSEl8c4VX3Q5aYcEHpwrjxmOl7SdsjckeTy66ccC73qbbuNijhZUP8MJwqY+\nQ471EZwqhAo49mFT67TtEL/6o4XL2zKKKZ4Y3dJXQeqAjx4jLCL6Frus5N64yaRw\n2ESk8Dm928Lx+1bmsC8VX3Jo5MgWa+RFQkvLkwlEJCZ4EduUMVxG2Qi7IGoQiEkb\n58XRu9kbt2cBhFPEq1XXs01M9DMQ1Eer7VZHw/CeSSf/khvkmXaJUN2leWoXx9Cn\n06j5Ntt/CIO8Qsm/dqU22VYJwX+nRrGUrFd4+uvINnQNDyBuoSzxewF5gqGb5OaL\n5lKDGSvSkUntjSB8CyvBV5sglsxcItLplcPcrPCIr1b6iVi8J187ycwmq7kg1ETx\nhvCwNB++2JF4T9NWIGifbRJO34WbOyWEDQh7F7E12JSIEzIHLUd64aY3cVo3nKTQ\nEAT81ZDGktmYrKXHQrLdK33dFZA6XHI+VmsOyuPYE5vMbrfHlKnwuQRxs/N56EH8\nbXfoYb66LpQnH/ghSGAN1ZgXWDI7FMVmnhR0BHXPMps6zr1yOciytfnqd8jSXCSj\nf7dgEEeU0INcUP4rFAhrN3vZTD7o0ygiMkkSmUr3BOZaPvoJW0mQFCGSBqHL+dRa\nRTWuHmYBQkp86aCWvMMk\n=y2zz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-10T22:36:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/e49d299510dad9712046d507d0ca8daa1cdd653c","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKGU0OWQyOTk1MTBkYWQ5NzEyMDQ2ZDUwN2QwY2E4ZGFhMWNkZDY1M2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/b6bbfbb7e7cc59f586653a1484cecaac581d721e","sha":"b6bbfbb7e7cc59f586653a1484cecaac581d721e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/b6bbfbb7e7cc59f586653a1484cecaac581d721e"}],"sha":"e49d299510dad9712046d507d0ca8daa1cdd653c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/e49d299510dad9712046d507d0ca8daa1cdd653c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/b6bbfbb7e7cc59f586653a1484cecaac581d721e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T20:50:45Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T20:50:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(auth): pin the real auth-scope model with characterization tests (#175)\n\nThree design documents in one day asserted that the `Internal` scope is a\ntrust boundary and that the Platform/Internal auth scopes are disjoint.\nEach was disproven by a throwaway probe test that was then deleted, so the\nnext author repeated the mistake. This makes those probes permanent, so a\ndoc author or a refactor is contradicted by CI instead of by a reviewer''s\nmemory.\n\nCharacterization tests only — they pin what the code does TODAY, warts\nincluded. No behaviour is changed here. Where the pinned behaviour is\nundesirable the test''s name and comment say so.\n\nPinned:\n\n- One X-MS-Internal-Secret authenticates BOTH PlatformAuth and InternalAuth\n  (same platformSecretReader), so the scopes are not disjoint. On the real\n  Platform surface the secret is honored at two independent points:\n  requireProxy validates it and promotes the forwarded identity, after which\n  platformAuth admits via its upstream-identity branch without ever reaching\n  its own secret check.\n- RequirePermission injects roles.Admin() unconditionally, so AppRole=admin\n  passes a permission declared for \"moderator\" only — a permission can never\n  be admin-excluded.\n- An undeclared permission is lazily registered admin-only.\n- RequireRoles answers 401 only for a nil actor or an empty AppRole (an\n  identity object with no role is still 401), and 403 on a role miss.\n- The deployed envelope is payload-trusted: NewLambdaHandler marks every\n  envelope, internalAuth returns before reading the secret, so an Internal\n  route answers 200 with no secret AND with a wrong secret. The HTTP plane\n  401s on that same wrong secret — the two planes do not share a gate.\n- promoteForwarderIdentity trusts forwarded X-MS-* identity only on the\n  secret-validated path: promoted with a valid secret, nil on the\n  unconfigured local bypass, never reached on rejection.\n\nEvery test verified to bite via a compile-safe behaviour mutation of the\nmiddleware it characterizes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f644b41090c2b4031e3ca896a575f3ac1931b4cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/f644b41090c2b4031e3ca896a575f3ac1931b4cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/b6bbfbb7e7cc59f586653a1484cecaac581d721e","verification":{"payload":"tree f644b41090c2b4031e3ca896a575f3ac1931b4cf\nparent 574d4ed463fe049eeda66525676e8922a863a3df\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1786395045 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786395045 +0800\n\ntest(auth): pin the real auth-scope model with characterization tests (#175)\n\nThree design documents in one day asserted that the `Internal` scope is a\ntrust boundary and that the Platform/Internal auth scopes are disjoint.\nEach was disproven by a throwaway probe test that was then deleted, so the\nnext author repeated the mistake. This makes those probes permanent, so a\ndoc author or a refactor is contradicted by CI instead of by a reviewer''s\nmemory.\n\nCharacterization tests only — they pin what the code does TODAY, warts\nincluded. No behaviour is changed here. Where the pinned behaviour is\nundesirable the test''s name and comment say so.\n\nPinned:\n\n- One X-MS-Internal-Secret authenticates BOTH PlatformAuth and InternalAuth\n  (same platformSecretReader), so the scopes are not disjoint. On the real\n  Platform surface the secret is honored at two independent points:\n  requireProxy validates it and promotes the forwarded identity, after which\n  platformAuth admits via its upstream-identity branch without ever reaching\n  its own secret check.\n- RequirePermission injects roles.Admin() unconditionally, so AppRole=admin\n  passes a permission declared for \"moderator\" only — a permission can never\n  be admin-excluded.\n- An undeclared permission is lazily registered admin-only.\n- RequireRoles answers 401 only for a nil actor or an empty AppRole (an\n  identity object with no role is still 401), and 403 on a role miss.\n- The deployed envelope is payload-trusted: NewLambdaHandler marks every\n  envelope, internalAuth returns before reading the secret, so an Internal\n  route answers 200 with no secret AND with a wrong secret. The HTTP plane\n  401s on that same wrong secret — the two planes do not share a gate.\n- promoteForwarderIdentity trusts forwarded X-MS-* identity only on the\n  secret-validated path: promoted with a valid secret, nil on the\n  unconfigured local bypass, never reached on rejection.\n\nEvery test verified to bite via a compile-safe behaviour mutation of the\nmiddleware it characterizes.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqejmlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABx8QAHhRcMEfSvGYdPwe6XvpynEp\nYyDl8Mmz8lyWinKZUNwdjmTKOMLY5+xnvlJqiflebgCCAWxUnjUHZPMhUM1F9/pT\nerha0eWOCMOQOTaHHIKMrEeml+OwaaM4ACT6QWT6ASmjxLwNgKgu9+ODY4I73jSI\nK1HO/P5OarFCF+O1M9unP7/cKkDkdmK7qC5yaukLi5kNfZRFAToHFcYk/XW6hykb\nOLb8TLhNErJu5DqhXSuax1MVV5K8HK6sbzmNZ1OOp5deB6GGvoKK08IPc8Xu7igR\nSX98AgfvfqMCWa5ily/rCE5Eg3rzyp3OYWBDBgP5LfK/aF6xsAZlb3/jKw7KXOyH\ncAU7yTCdo2GreKyqWk5yA7h1G0Ql9mlPf0uQt0Sw7b7LSrTPyotQKmoMLObC4ff0\n9Cl5YAFqibDQomp6KkjoYkLG9JADbMYeDvrqr/b0MJaa3DfzneNOFBFuVNO4pPm3\n8xDwJO2Gu8P36+Y2Zo8OJt64ItOkiuHuKm8T5DVSCXCz33bpZEcMd0AgIpIn26hk\nL7qGsZIYSACvwW1TE8i5E0aZ2R1JAqMxtkAR2I+JpIiTyNln74j6VRggJI49MV7j\nI99hvoeuf1JljE2VXMG8oNlHreRwdvzkjYFwkfnbkafkQk0wkJbV7uOr4bcfNdGz\n8poq1VSdciD7C5kqvuQT\n=WHuS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-10T20:55:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/b6bbfbb7e7cc59f586653a1484cecaac581d721e","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKGI2YmJmYmI3ZTdjYzU5ZjU4NjY1M2ExNDg0Y2VjYWFjNTgxZDcyMWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/574d4ed463fe049eeda66525676e8922a863a3df","sha":"574d4ed463fe049eeda66525676e8922a863a3df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/574d4ed463fe049eeda66525676e8922a863a3df"}],"sha":"b6bbfbb7e7cc59f586653a1484cecaac581d721e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/b6bbfbb7e7cc59f586653a1484cecaac581d721e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/574d4ed463fe049eeda66525676e8922a863a3df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T20:33:52Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T20:33:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: release v0.4.0 (#168)\n\n* chore: release v0.4.0\n\n* docs: include authenticated module calls in v0.4.0\n\n* docs: state the contribution gap that v0.4.0 does not close\n\nThe v0.4.0 entry claimed the release \"makes contribution slots available on\nboth the dev and deployed request planes\". #166 creates the per-app\ncontribution STORE on the deployed plane, but DELIVERY is still dev-tunnel\nonly: api-platform''s install-time reconcile reads the contributor''s\ncontributesTo and POSTs into the host''s slot through WSSessionModuleEndpoints,\nthe sole ModuleEndpoints implementation, which resolves live\n`mirrorstack dev --tunnel` sessions and nothing else. Either module being\ndeployed makes both hops return ErrModuleEndpointNotFound, and the push is\nswallowed after one platform-side log line.\n\nSo an author reading the old text would deploy a host and its contributor,\nget an empty slot with no error on either side, and have no way to tell that\nfrom \"nobody contributed\" — the silent-failure shape this codebase keeps\nproducing. An auth-provider slot is sign-in, so it is not cosmetic.\n\nDocumentation only: VERSION, the release heading and all code are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"22b64c030ace962c0fd8813c284ef7fa3593fc36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/22b64c030ace962c0fd8813c284ef7fa3593fc36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/574d4ed463fe049eeda66525676e8922a863a3df","verification":{"payload":"tree 22b64c030ace962c0fd8813c284ef7fa3593fc36\nparent 1e133f1217a10a424abf5c0f779685e10b95796d\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1786221232 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786221232 +0800\n\nchore: release v0.4.0 (#168)\n\n* chore: release v0.4.0\n\n* docs: include authenticated module calls in v0.4.0\n\n* docs: state the contribution gap that v0.4.0 does not close\n\nThe v0.4.0 entry claimed the release \"makes contribution slots available on\nboth the dev and deployed request planes\". #166 creates the per-app\ncontribution STORE on the deployed plane, but DELIVERY is still dev-tunnel\nonly: api-platform''s install-time reconcile reads the contributor''s\ncontributesTo and POSTs into the host''s slot through WSSessionModuleEndpoints,\nthe sole ModuleEndpoints implementation, which resolves live\n`mirrorstack dev --tunnel` sessions and nothing else. Either module being\ndeployed makes both hops return ErrModuleEndpointNotFound, and the push is\nswallowed after one platform-side log line.\n\nSo an author reading the old text would deploy a host and its contributor,\nget an empty slot with no error on either side, and have no way to tell that\nfrom \"nobody contributed\" — the silent-failure shape this codebase keeps\nproducing. An auth-provider slot is sign-in, so it is not cosmetic.\n\nDocumentation only: VERSION, the release heading and all code are untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqd5KwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6iUQAI3C7dKPna6sKYAt77uX+s0g\nTx7yPmT3IAnyzwGNsSPG9ghvZcEl8Z3xzm7ostnP2FUzQNuJv7/31kWuAYamxe/Q\nqIg71uBiRKnafYbfmk+KhAolvCpi2CHZEIRmKGt/BkfxGgrdh4uxLtWG5ZqYNHY1\n2WPUnIqU4p2wnLXKNpTX4/AzWKvG8OtXZbiJn0287LluADsTrecAayXpL6nG/y5y\nE+e4pXjgYYDVBZWN474XlX7RS796CLYe9aYN/dM8yna4juCrwmGSUZo9RX3b9c2N\nhIzh8P55TVpx/2r/owEykazBMpjttui/8ePHPRSSsprA5qJiR1sOwO2J43EPGaH3\nItNyN9yJgbBABdeVNZKsDEJe/Uu8M24H1XD95dgdbaca4QOOMWn8rTPfeTliwRNS\ncO5iM/f/iJbIjjhXlQndeKE4eLT/FEJmixoA1/K3FH+8iJFimUPfXGKkiipPZCtL\nWPsjLZEAwe+ovQHKJNLufKOVchbBXFjbAWN79F43KGNWVw9qGJbRSCgect9G3hIC\nBmSHkKF0Kyn01syiDz2FC0TDuCBOPjzeK0tn7Usj7Ab/wW0ToheZcqVTxskHmIW5\nJVmozLxnD0oc29EIa7kukhLxpqHR8FF5Bwt123tmyG9NlXbhRqNzcF8u104Fr9Vj\nMI54VEPjTX8jEsRIQ9wK\n=An4y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-08T20:37:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/574d4ed463fe049eeda66525676e8922a863a3df","node_i