----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-06T14:23:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/16c1a3334ffcdccc8fc154e15052f41ca0de43db","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKDE2YzFhMzMzNGZmY2RjY2M4ZmMxNTRlMTUwNTJmNDFjYTBkZTQzZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/9beb4b93aaad6ae4b2221f55e40a21933c43a0f1","sha":"9beb4b93aaad6ae4b2221f55e40a21933c43a0f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/9beb4b93aaad6ae4b2221f55e40a21933c43a0f1"}],"sha":"16c1a3334ffcdccc8fc154e15052f41ca0de43db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/16c1a3334ffcdccc8fc154e15052f41ca0de43db"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/9beb4b93aaad6ae4b2221f55e40a21933c43a0f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T13:23:49Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T13:23:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: declare and isolate module storage (#167)\n\n* feat(storage): make ms.Storage work on both planes, always prefix-scoped\n\nThe module never learns which plane it is on: both paths now end at\nNewFromCredential with a prefix-scoped storage.Credential. Deployed, the\nplatform vends it (api-platform storagecreds). Dev mints an equivalent one\nlocally against MinIO STS AssumeRole with the SAME inline session policy shape,\nso keys and code path match production and MinIO — not the client — enforces\nthe prefix.\n\nThree bugs fixed:\n\n1. Under Lambda with no vended credential the SDK fell through to Open() and\n   returned \"Open() cannot be used in Lambda\", which reads like a MODULE bug and\n   sends a third-party developer hunting their own code. Now a distinct\n   ErrNotVended that names the PLATFORM and the env vars an operator must wire.\n\n2. Open() defaulted to bucket mirrorstack-dev against REAL AWS with no\n   credentials: presign hung 5s on EC2 IMDS then 502''d. Open() is gone.\n   DevConfigFromEnv fails immediately, naming every missing variable, and never\n   falls back to AWS.\n\n3. Open() set prefix:\"\" — a dev module got an UNSCOPED whole-bucket client even\n   though dev --tunnel serves REAL apps, multiple appIDs through one runner.\n   Both decision docs required killing it (02 sub-decision D, 03 \"Dev / local\n   parity\"). There is now no constructor that can produce an empty prefix.\n\nSecurity: the dev minter interpolates appID/moduleID into the session policy\nResource, and on the dev plane appID arrives in the spoofable X-MS-App-ID\nheader. An unvalidated \"*\" yielded Resource .../apps/*/<mod>/* — confirmed\nagainst minio/minio:latest to grant cross-app writes for that module. Both ids\nnow go through one canonicalizer (appID must be a canonical UUID, moduleID must\nmatch a conservative slug pattern) before they can reach the prefix or the\npolicy, mirroring api-platform''s Canonicalize. Credential.validate() also now\nrequires the trailing slash, because apps/<A>/<M>* would match a sibling whose\nid merely starts with the same bytes.\n\nPresigning is split from server-side calls: PresignPut/PresignGet sign against\nS3_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT while S3 operations use S3_ENDPOINT. Unavoidable in dev — the\nrunner reaches MinIO as s3:9000 while the browser redeeming the URL can only\nresolve localhost:9000. Production passes no endpoints, so both clients keep\nAWS resolution and prod behaviour is unchanged.\n\nCredential lifetime: 3600s with re-mint at ExpiresAt-1200s, the buffer DERIVED\nas maxPresignTTL(900s)+margin(300s) — a presigned URL carries\nX-Amz-Security-Token, so its real validity is min(X-Amz-Expires, remaining token\nlifetime).\n\nAlso corrected three actively misleading comments: the Prefix id-shape example,\nErrNoCredential''s false \"this happens on Public routes\" claim (the platform\nvends for every deployed invocation regardless of route class, and must — all\nthree of video-core''s HLS routes are ms.Public), and validateKey''s implication\nthat it is a security boundary (it runs inside the module''s own process).\n\nCredential''s fields/tags and Storer are unchanged: video-core needs zero\nchanges.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: declare and bound module storage access\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af9a8d8d5cfddfd7234ad899687d92af71512ba4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/af9a8d8d5cfddfd7234ad899687d92af71512ba4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/9beb4b93aaad6ae4b2221f55e40a21933c43a0f1","verification":{"payload":"tree af9a8d8d5cfddfd7234ad899687d92af71512ba4\nparent 93ede9d6bd5a1688cee06889adbc3d598810d4fc\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1786022629 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786022629 +0800\n\nfeat: declare and isolate module storage (#167)\n\n* feat(storage): make ms.Storage work on both planes, always prefix-scoped\n\nThe module never learns which plane it is on: both paths now end at\nNewFromCredential with a prefix-scoped storage.Credential. Deployed, the\nplatform vends it (api-platform storagecreds). Dev mints an equivalent one\nlocally against MinIO STS AssumeRole with the SAME inline session policy shape,\nso keys and code path match production and MinIO — not the client — enforces\nthe prefix.\n\nThree bugs fixed:\n\n1. Under Lambda with no vended credential the SDK fell through to Open() and\n   returned \"Open() cannot be used in Lambda\", which reads like a MODULE bug and\n   sends a third-party developer hunting their own code. Now a distinct\n   ErrNotVended that names the PLATFORM and the env vars an operator must wire.\n\n2. Open() defaulted to bucket mirrorstack-dev against REAL AWS with no\n   credentials: presign hung 5s on EC2 IMDS then 502''d. Open() is gone.\n   DevConfigFromEnv fails immediately, naming every missing variable, and never\n   falls back to AWS.\n\n3. Open() set prefix:\"\" — a dev module got an UNSCOPED whole-bucket client even\n   though dev --tunnel serves REAL apps, multiple appIDs through one runner.\n   Both decision docs required killing it (02 sub-decision D, 03 \"Dev / local\n   parity\"). There is now no constructor that can produce an empty prefix.\n\nSecurity: the dev minter interpolates appID/moduleID into the session policy\nResource, and on the dev plane appID arrives in the spoofable X-MS-App-ID\nheader. An unvalidated \"*\" yielded Resource .../apps/*/<mod>/* — confirmed\nagainst minio/minio:latest to grant cross-app writes for that module. Both ids\nnow go through one canonicalizer (appID must be a canonical UUID, moduleID must\nmatch a conservative slug pattern) before they can reach the prefix or the\npolicy, mirroring api-platform''s Canonicalize. Credential.validate() also now\nrequires the trailing slash, because apps/<A>/<M>* would match a sibling whose\nid merely starts with the same bytes.\n\nPresigning is split from server-side calls: PresignPut/PresignGet sign against\nS3_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT while S3 operations use S3_ENDPOINT. Unavoidable in dev — the\nrunner reaches MinIO as s3:9000 while the browser redeeming the URL can only\nresolve localhost:9000. Production passes no endpoints, so both clients keep\nAWS resolution and prod behaviour is unchanged.\n\nCredential lifetime: 3600s with re-mint at ExpiresAt-1200s, the buffer DERIVED\nas maxPresignTTL(900s)+margin(300s) — a presigned URL carries\nX-Amz-Security-Token, so its real validity is min(X-Amz-Expires, remaining token\nlifetime).\n\nAlso corrected three actively misleading comments: the Prefix id-shape example,\nErrNoCredential''s false \"this happens on Public routes\" claim (the platform\nvends for every deployed invocation regardless of route class, and must — all\nthree of video-core''s HLS routes are ms.Public), and validateKey''s implication\nthat it is a security boundary (it runs inside the module''s own process).\n\nCredential''s fields/tags and Storer are unchanged: video-core needs zero\nchanges.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: declare and bound module storage access\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdIrlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnUIQADFbF5UqVF+jhSzSjc19hWqJ\nQXCv4/tAn/55OFWnBM2rR6oKzcrOlRAofyxdhUKA4Y6J9wwNpC+sa9TsVV1JbyiL\n1ebNdjeEwY36O6xHvbmbG5qaezIdFKjgH7WBORcDTnTf6AxjNizCKoGPFNhQV+FB\nOK5tqBEf/paANBJGVjLoMFRpD6OZJdKmhgURCOCvN68Xvh1dR74OTq4jEjRWaav3\n4M+8qIvX1z273Vj/PU2+QmvwA/e61B/iR1typFYf76T3y3h3mqpoYcClmsjQPx2p\nQ183khwdU3jTMSBGHoOclY2OrqfNC6nyCmHkoUZ+He+ngL6OtkBXObSA7HF8DExs\n0NDqLWYleJqB59KaHxqX45G6WWuLWD10Hx8lpAqGXLIECj61GQwiMae/t5cdsnAp\nmyDDiAthzoAUUdLY/e3v3ZOVquRZfl4GqLlUaJYPqgYZcjvXw9TktLUQy/39w0a2\nsyW6aCWoDv1H/tRIxFDqgZ15dlubLuIJd+5rfihb3T4ZM3OFce07cMdhvVxLFFJb\nDV0J4zSK+oexdHtShshS1MqILijV/Qs5Hd3ffbgfsDXGFvT6761r1dkJUWh6rA2O\nT3Zq9frzeBGhjBl3ZvVX8fCv+eR5INgd4BoB7VirTin8/uRbCf7/OFlC+3RGIvS6\nnvFD0SYc+qfIZWQo1LMr\n=tI75\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-06T13:23:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/9beb4b93aaad6ae4b2221f55e40a21933c43a0f1","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKDliZWI0YjkzYWFhZDZhZTRiMjIyMWY1NWU0MGEyMTkzM2M0M2EwZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/93ede9d6bd5a1688cee06889adbc3d598810d4fc","sha":"93ede9d6bd5a1688cee06889adbc3d598810d4fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/93ede9d6bd5a1688cee06889adbc3d598810d4fc"}],"sha":"9beb4b93aaad6ae4b2221f55e40a21933c43a0f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/9beb4b93aaad6ae4b2221f55e40a21933c43a0f1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/93ede9d6bd5a1688cee06889adbc3d598810d4fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T13:01:04Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T13:01:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(contributions): create the per-app store on the deployed plane (#166)\n\n* fix(contributions): create the per-app store on the deployed plane\n\nThe contributions table was only ever created under `mirrorstack dev`: the\none non-dev call site sat below Start()''s runtime.IsLambda() early return,\nso a deployed module never reached it — and off-Lambda it created the table\nin the connection''s default schema, the wrong place for per-app state.\nEvery deployed host of a contribution slot answered ms.StoredContributions\nwith 42P01 and reported \"no contributions\".\n\nProvisioning moves to the platform''s per-(app, module) lifecycle window:\nsystem.InstallHandler/UpgradeHandler run an SDK-owned Provisioner before the\nauthor''s migrations, inside the install context the platform already sends\n(schema + credential). Per-app by construction; a cold-start hook could not\nbe, since one container serves many apps. A schema-less (tunnel) body stays\na no-op and the dev plane is unchanged.\n\nEnsureTable takes a pg_advisory_xact_lock keyed on current_schema() in the\nsame argument-less Exec (one implicit transaction) and tolerates 42P07/23505,\nso concurrent cold starts for one app cannot fight. Reads and writes heal an\ninstall that predates the hook by creating the store and retrying once on\n42P01 only — the platform sends no lifecycle call at all to an install\nalready at its target counter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(contributions): honor configured database URL\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f4bdba89add87fe2e9495766d26823f68bef4b00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/f4bdba89add87fe2e9495766d26823f68bef4b00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/93ede9d6bd5a1688cee06889adbc3d598810d4fc","verification":{"payload":"tree f4bdba89add87fe2e9495766d26823f68bef4b00\nparent fa19efbac335d19f982c437dbc4fe552f5c3742e\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1786021264 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786021264 +0800\n\nfix(contributions): create the per-app store on the deployed plane (#166)\n\n* fix(contributions): create the per-app store on the deployed plane\n\nThe contributions table was only ever created under `mirrorstack dev`: the\none non-dev call site sat below Start()''s runtime.IsLambda() early return,\nso a deployed module never reached it — and off-Lambda it created the table\nin the connection''s default schema, the wrong place for per-app state.\nEvery deployed host of a contribution slot answered ms.StoredContributions\nwith 42P01 and reported \"no contributions\".\n\nProvisioning moves to the platform''s per-(app, module) lifecycle window:\nsystem.InstallHandler/UpgradeHandler run an SDK-owned Provisioner before the\nauthor''s migrations, inside the install context the platform already sends\n(schema + credential). Per-app by construction; a cold-start hook could not\nbe, since one container serves many apps. A schema-less (tunnel) body stays\na no-op and the dev plane is unchanged.\n\nEnsureTable takes a pg_advisory_xact_lock keyed on current_schema() in the\nsame argument-less Exec (one implicit transaction) and tolerates 42P07/23505,\nso concurrent cold starts for one app cannot fight. Reads and writes heal an\ninstall that predates the hook by creating the store and retrying once on\n42P01 only — the platform sends no lifecycle call at all to an install\nalready at its target counter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(contributions): honor configured database URL\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdIWQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwaoQAEBzn3pp2ZwZsYCpuf5wIyFz\nzdEIumLDN6XrdYTUK9FdCddpNCIo+AsfN8abPx08vOd8VKyEVzxQA/MLopCQSv3Y\nUz9v9Eqooc723DgUxAE+nO2yF/ytj1b6zuG5o3FNpm7ErqlVikcyR3Kd0IDEeHzo\nB8DexlPXbYffXGTggQZjvXDdFU8sNZrbpzLoLsuKrc974BWgcLCnaEuHCRr3B978\nYWgB4c5O1PBl60JxeeWaenGbUuAMYJTI7/A99XhgIVGPv8ACaXYA6MKojSllgmMW\npl0bhXG7MhS5n8uOwwnQdmHm0FDKV+o6AIPvwLDluC6gFBt7IDG7qwWwJVIKew3R\ntntEkWfJkEstkNu3r0dupEzfriWnP5M82MVmgpjJqDwl6FD8QylyXcw5FsxMkDQL\nkyC6VqB8EhAQaH5UtxMoZddMq7W4so9I2vsnkvrVmHAqvch+q/NFW5Wfb0Ud2YWB\ntG4KTh6IPhDvpkVyBGKhCJWMrzfxgxfWRx4MMVSucz2RxqXh8lGxG0H17GhRDWqm\nGTymJ07GK2UTyeCXNo3rxQqqR+VYO9fBpXrxtnFKSwY8L6SYo9czjVNvk3Pxj6Wx\nHFFPaNZLVkgGVUGfN6WyLEkVmXigN9FfxiT/6hjGowJwDLrDyOEoD9SS3b/P36FD\nBRF6CgkUadgfQoKGRsMo\n=9xyt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-06T13:05:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/93ede9d6bd5a1688cee06889adbc3d598810d4fc","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKDkzZWRlOWQ2YmQ1YTE2ODhjZWUwNjg4OWFkYmMzZDU5ODgxMGQ0ZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/fa19efbac335d19f982c437dbc4fe552f5c3742e","sha":"fa19efbac335d19f982c437dbc4fe552f5c3742e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/fa19efbac335d19f982c437dbc4fe552f5c3742e"}],"sha":"93ede9d6bd5a1688cee06889adbc3d598810d4fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/93ede9d6bd5a1688cee06889adbc3d598810d4fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/fa19efbac335d19f982c437dbc4fe552f5c3742e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T17:08:25Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T17:08:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(core): send the service secret on Emit so events are accepted (#165)\n\nThe event bus rejects a sender carrying no X-MS-Service-Secret before it\nlooks anything up, and Emit passed nil headers. Every ms.Emit has been\nfailing 403 unknown_sender (\"event sender is not a live module\") — a\nmessage that points at tunnel liveness rather than the missing credential\nit actually describes, which is why this read as an infrastructure\nproblem for a long time.\n\nms.Notify and the dependency read proxy already send the same secret from\nthe same helper. Emit was the one caller that did not.\n\nNothing caught it. The envelope was correct, the URL was correct, and\ndelivery is deliberately best-effort so a failure never propagates to the\ncaller — the only trace was a line in the emitting module''s own stdout.\nThe new test asserts the credential rather than just the payload.","tree":{"sha":"058cb02b78a8f1593ff114aac283564a8af356dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/058cb02b78a8f1593ff114aac283564a8af356dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/fa19efbac335d19f982c437dbc4fe552f5c3742e","verification":{"payload":"tree 058cb02b78a8f1593ff114aac283564a8af356dc\nparent fe3b8932d05cf2287d884412340bc0b02de9292b\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1785949705 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785949705 +0800\n\nfix(core): send the service secret on Emit so events are accepted (#165)\n\nThe event bus rejects a sender carrying no X-MS-Service-Secret before it\nlooks anything up, and Emit passed nil headers. Every ms.Emit has been\nfailing 403 unknown_sender (\"event sender is not a live module\") — a\nmessage that points at tunnel liveness rather than the missing credential\nit actually describes, which is why this read as an infrastructure\nproblem for a long time.\n\nms.Notify and the dependency read proxy already send the same secret from\nthe same helper. Emit was the one caller that did not.\n\nNothing caught it. The envelope was correct, the URL was correct, and\ndelivery is deliberately best-effort so a failure never propagates to the\ncaller — the only trace was a line in the emitting module''s own stdout.\nThe new test asserts the credential rather than just the payload.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqc24JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4JAQAFj3GrAsRvpz030QtzxpEJGg\niQGsJGK22xG4QXppTvYy5H/JyC4Hr6sJysuyiOKFxG2ACVQJMg+h+uJgXnSfTmgb\n5xY223qtCjuZkJ/NODWr4xUkhiSqWbGaMj2te3ixfhTqA2f34fJyk8cNqvZfDthM\npr9m8rBMk/x5qhjlbVehQRPb5EZHxuMrFd4JVFdkph4r+/2GIgPI+5DqzweyInff\nz/26+EYM1+FOg2b66zCEibhRQocWqys8UddynqExV5IC18Y2rXyRu8s/raIKoRqQ\n21l1mtwKGWIELfGmBUXRWKCI00KXdRFiVVNV6BvqZTmCtmzn9O+B5ve2n81B0KBA\nx62RBoHWQT/JCukdGfY6n7OagNtgbCb1/M7PrQZ+F0TwUKugknEVJTgD0WuB3gGA\nUMKcOEeqsu2tk5Vm3CLT2Z5aGSW2yxtDEi9V5431E5ogK/h/ovWEvJLCXfPDuvSf\nfmXldWhPZN9qM30yNIToyN0PVVBFXH6nLbyCm/npWE6dLvv673KEZFIqwaM7igbp\ndfIXaLmFvlV87zH93T2cLC11ft/n44ZVrFa/IF0DJKr1EFBuYbUmrz88B7iNEsf/\nq3eonYD3K7aeLbb38Vn+KgAktbVNgT6Jk0h4cdk5CgI/7FQl5ZadoNhpmGwiwhYe\ns1kTFfMC8tVkRY714JVv\n=clY9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-05T17:08:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/fa19efbac335d19f982c437dbc4fe552f5c3742e","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKGZhMTllZmJhYzMzNWQxOWY5ODJjNDM3ZGJjNGZlNTUyZjVjMzc0MmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/fe3b8932d05cf2287d884412340bc0b02de9292b","sha":"fe3b8932d05cf2287d884412340bc0b02de9292b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/fe3b8932d05cf2287d884412340bc0b02de9292b"}],"sha":"fa19efbac335d19f982c437dbc4fe552f5c3742e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/fa19efbac335d19f982c437dbc4fe552f5c3742e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/fe3b8932d05cf2287d884412340bc0b02de9292b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T13:45:47Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T13:45:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(system): opt in to local-network access so tunnelled bundles load (#164)\n\nUnder `mirrorstack dev --tunnel` the settings page is served from a public\nhttps origin (apps.mirrorstack.ai) while the module bundle is fetched from\nhttp://localhost. Chrome classes that as a local-network request and\nblocks it unless the target opts in on the preflight.\n\nThe handler set CORS but never the opt-in, so Chrome dropped the request\nbefore it left the browser. Symptom: every module settings page rendered\nas an empty frame under a tunnel — no console error, no entry in the\nmodule''s request log, and the same URL returning 200 to curl. Verified\nagainst Chrome 150: before this change the browser''s request never\nreached the process at all; after it, the preflight arrives and is\nanswered 204.\n\nBoth spellings are answered because the header was renamed: Chrome 138+\nsends Local-Network-Access, earlier versions Private-Network. The opt-in\nis echoed only when the request asks for it, so an ordinary same-origin\nfetch does not advertise access it never requested.\n\nOpting in is safe for this namespace specifically: /__mirrorstack/web/* is\nread-only public static assets carrying no credentials, which is why its\nCORS is already permissive.","tree":{"sha":"4e5c7085d5696ffcc1bdead68a80244b01331436","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/4e5c7085d5696ffcc1bdead68a80244b01331436"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/fe3b8932d05cf2287d884412340bc0b02de9292b","verification":{"payload":"tree 4e5c7085d5696ffcc1bdead68a80244b01331436\nparent 4680bcfd579a4e16f3853ba7c4294b61c5f16d0e\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1785937547 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785937547 +0800\n\nfix(system): opt in to local-network access so tunnelled bundles load (#164)\n\nUnder `mirrorstack dev --tunnel` the settings page is served from a public\nhttps origin (apps.mirrorstack.ai) while the module bundle is fetched from\nhttp://localhost. Chrome classes that as a local-network request and\nblocks it unless the target opts in on the preflight.\n\nThe handler set CORS but never the opt-in, so Chrome dropped the request\nbefore it left the browser. Symptom: every module settings page rendered\nas an empty frame under a tunnel — no console error, no entry in the\nmodule''s request log, and the same URL returning 200 to curl. Verified\nagainst Chrome 150: before this change the browser''s request never\nreached the process at all; after it, the preflight arrives and is\nanswered 204.\n\nBoth spellings are answered because the header was renamed: Chrome 138+\nsends Local-Network-Access, earlier versions Private-Network. The opt-in\nis echoed only when the request asks for it, so an ordinary same-origin\nfetch does not advertise access it never requested.\n\nOpting in is safe for this namespace specifically: /__mirrorstack/web/* is\nread-only public static assets carrying no credentials, which is why its\nCORS is already permissive.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcz6LCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlH8QAJtYwGZxDJRymTzhpLtdULwI\nZag+hWWAiagblWdiD49fD2zXHHUKtsYuC031eswDx3k2qHAh0fbbM15bRq+NXhS7\nBS14EqVDfL/4btqqvoobPYlD3VFvGnwRHXxdIGDacpYv0jV/VmrtJq9hB263/27J\n84AuQpHBz56YLODwcFygyW1MCi7pvsDXrmmg+jBSNTAh8F5DvAMIo5JF/3QrQwsC\ny5lGK4+FIIz93q6TgCmQn8zCg2gx5MasSiQ5of1XuqttxEN3zvheI6649AA/fqWp\n76RkCmoVB+zTxpAgPPDqRF1pcjxW18IjzVLpOx5zwbnM6GQCJnuxocKFsySmsoUe\nFBXO1DbEZ8haty8J3ipJuTVfOyIeZnh1jOZrceOmfn/YAFHR6bqWwijljgEahx59\n4fQ+5O9Vft/Ss7qzHg1V2s934KBbNhqr8IDdZ5WMgFPzzUF2p+EGrd1K7CA1pslx\ntqLgRAl86wMUb7PhFMJEjVfGTl6AYIpO5i9XaP/OPbS4VIX2pZHwJ08B+kGAY386\nLCZ5P3FEchJkFx479jAfw56uM1ecf/qwJaqFDlHHdOgvZFWxi0pXoRrl0/IFjXTK\nRtOXTCTZM3BSZb/vgpHe