//api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/4680bcfd579a4e16f3853ba7c4294b61c5f16d0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T21:50:46Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T21:50:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: fail Start when a declared UI has no bundle to serve (#163)\n\n* feat: fail Start when a declared UI has no bundle to serve\n\nRegisterUI declaring pages while Config.WebDir is empty is always a\nmistake, and nothing catches it today.\n\nms-app-modules#94 shipped a settings page for users-roles with WebDir\nunset. WebDir is what makes Start mount GET /__mirrorstack/web/*\n(module.go:784) — declaring a UIPage does not imply it. The manifest\nadvertised the page, Go built, the bundle built at 389 kB, all ten CI\njobs passed, and an adversarial review found nothing. The admin opened\nthe page and got:\n\n  Couldn''t load module bundle: Failed to fetch dynamically imported\n  module: .../_m/users-roles/__mirrorstack/web/index.js\n\nThe failure lives entirely between a declaration and the runtime meant\nto serve it, so it only ever appears in a browser. This was the third\nbug of that shape in one day.\n\ncheckUIServable runs at Start, after the Lambda and task-worker early\nreturns — a deployed module legitimately serves its bundle from CDN, so\nthe check belongs to the local/dev path where the tunnel runs. The error\nnames the fix rather than the symptom, because it fires on a developer''s\nfirst run of a new surface.\n\nOnly the contradictory combination fails. A module with no UI, a module\nwith both, and a module with WebDir but no UI (it may serve assets\nanother module''s contributed surface renders) all pass, and each is\npinned by a test so the guard cannot start rejecting valid modules.\n\nMutation-tested: forcing checkUIServable to return nil makes both\nfailure tests fail, so they detect the bug rather than passing by\nconstruction. Full suite: 18 packages, 0 failures.\n\n* test: prove Start actually calls the guard\n\nCodex review found the coverage gap: every test called checkUIServable\ndirectly, so deleting the call from Start would have left them all\ngreen — the exact ''passes for the wrong reason'' shape.\n\nStart runs on a goroutine with a deadline rather than inline. Wired, it\nreturns the error immediately; unwired, it falls through to\nListenAndServe and never returns, which inline would surface as a\nten-minute package timeout instead of a failure that names itself.\n\nMutation-tested: removing the call from Start fails this test and no\nother.","tree":{"sha":"8bffb5da89a789df4a4e9f231fa846a8dd292ec0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/8bffb5da89a789df4a4e9f231fa846a8dd292ec0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/4680bcfd579a4e16f3853ba7c4294b61c5f16d0e","verification":{"payload":"tree 8bffb5da89a789df4a4e9f231fa846a8dd292ec0\nparent 9873998b6208ae3a30386837bc11c910ccbdf0ef\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1785880246 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785880246 +0800\n\nfeat: fail Start when a declared UI has no bundle to serve (#163)\n\n* feat: fail Start when a declared UI has no bundle to serve\n\nRegisterUI declaring pages while Config.WebDir is empty is always a\nmistake, and nothing catches it today.\n\nms-app-modules#94 shipped a settings page for users-roles with WebDir\nunset. WebDir is what makes Start mount GET /__mirrorstack/web/*\n(module.go:784) — declaring a UIPage does not imply it. The manifest\nadvertised the page, Go built, the bundle built at 389 kB, all ten CI\njobs passed, and an adversarial review found nothing. The admin opened\nthe page and got:\n\n  Couldn''t load module bundle: Failed to fetch dynamically imported\n  module: .../_m/users-roles/__mirrorstack/web/index.js\n\nThe failure lives entirely between a declaration and the runtime meant\nto serve it, so it only ever appears in a browser. This was the third\nbug of that shape in one day.\n\ncheckUIServable runs at Start, after the Lambda and task-worker early\nreturns — a deployed module legitimately serves its bundle from CDN, so\nthe check belongs to the local/dev path where the tunnel runs. The error\nnames the fix rather than the symptom, because it fires on a developer''s\nfirst run of a new surface.\n\nOnly the contradictory combination fails. A module with no UI, a module\nwith both, and a module with WebDir but no UI (it may serve assets\nanother module''s contributed surface renders) all pass, and each is\npinned by a test so the guard cannot start rejecting valid modules.\n\nMutation-tested: forcing checkUIServable to return nil makes both\nfailure tests fail, so they detect the bug rather than passing by\nconstruction. Full suite: 18 packages, 0 failures.\n\n* test: prove Start actually calls the guard\n\nCodex review found the coverage gap: every test called checkUIServable\ndirectly, so deleting the call from Start would have left them all\ngreen — the exact ''passes for the wrong reason'' shape.\n\nStart runs on a goroutine with a deadline rather than inline. Wired, it\nreturns the error immediately; unwired, it falls through to\nListenAndServe and never returns, which inline would surface as a\nten-minute package timeout instead of a failure that names itself.\n\nMutation-tested: removing the call from Start fails this test and no\nother.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcl62CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMqAQAGh5SrHnPUeRbovF34sXsB/U\nUjySTIWxvgfvfXfWgntDrDhVJcdpr86GCWN6iXq3UCwSrCVeIIVWS6kNdP9fM73G\np/pJbKWy4NqbXbktd2+K1udy14lAIjP5z/2mi2Qlu0Ihsjouik7D2XL+OpWIyIO7\nlvAgFv1wx+Qhz/hDeoE3m6p4AEuaZw13AgaDnffz6eg13EksmfUhmB6Jr5gDB2SS\nwT5aRjssFN7Sfq5CEzv8HXkWCEHtcJVb+azDWG5qHYt47ZSgq2OML72zcTEtpfss\n7q9XjTTXcnPumJ52fL5CvpygESmHqPywCgYVYl4KULgSMDZmxY7xc0eV+c2nV11b\nyvlCrhmlAD3DiG3ogURBMhjsYNM1pK5flw8NtqB/VBxUWc4F/ioKdwx1UiaAW2z3\ndslpqtJgH503YbdRNwPGskv0nehvf8qhMX/+V0hOJCIQpR7rWkwMYrsg3NYAIQgf\n1A219QdetxG0/WjILdd1Z71D4zX0Hnthr29dI3PY+Xbvw37/Cmfhd+1T1GtNE4Pu\nSTmSW0QhRPnWR9bKBWgeNeL/XtZcehTCT5akFU59YTFBMXofFmyq2HvVcdsO2jWb\ntXcqIQSKrd49jDH0XBcljrDlNdcAu1Kjogt6uCUoXzH4zwSvF+zoc/OEpckK8aBw\nkZntv8Ly263MEbhWLRMi\n=bhEU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-04T21:50:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}