37ae6d018e2cb"}],"sha":"d52d1f0cdfb64cfccce3b5ebd9d814ca1a42453a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/d52d1f0cdfb64cfccce3b5ebd9d814ca1a42453a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/54589f95929cbf205fb8e25153f37ae6d018e2cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T15:19:48Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T15:19:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(transport): resolve the #146 module->dispatch seam; pin the deployed-plane credential contract (#161)\n\ncore-v2#338 step 6 is the SENDER side of authenticating a deployed module''s\ncallbacks into dispatch. Investigating it produced an unexpected answer: the\nSDK already satisfies it, and shipping code here would have been wrong.\n\nv0.3.1 already sends the credential on both in-scope legs -- meter/meter.go:483\nand internal/core/notify.go:120 both forward MS_INTERNAL_SECRET as\nX-MS-Service-Secret. The deployed plane differs only in WHO populates that\nvariable: the CLI mints a per-session secret under `mirrorstack dev --tunnel`,\nwhile the deploy provisioner injects a per-module credential. Both are opaque\nstrings the SDK forwards untouched, so no SDK code distinguishes them.\n\nThe SDK also CANNOT derive the credential, so injection is not merely the\ncheaper option -- it is the only workable one. Deriving needs the platform\nsecret, which a third-party module process must never hold (holding it lets one\nmodule mint every other module''s credential, destroying the isolation property\nthe scheme exists for), and the module''s catalog UUID, which nothing in the SDK\nreads: MS_MODULE_ID has zero non-test readers here, only two doc mentions.\n\nSo this is doc + tests, with a provably comment-only source diff.\n\n- meter.go''s \"when #146 lands, swap the body of this function\" instruction is\n  resolved and removed. #146 needed no swap: the deployed leg is the same\n  MS_DISPATCH_URL base, injected into every module Lambda by the provisioner.\n  Replaced with the reason and an explicit warning not to repoint the\n  host.docker.internal fallback at production -- that would make a local stack\n  silently emit usage against the real dispatch. resolveNotifyURL carried the\n  same stale marker.\n- moduleSessionSecret documented as no longer tunnel-only; name kept\n  deliberately, since renaming churns every call site for no behavioral gain.\n- dependency_db''s read-exposed proxy documented as staying tunnel-only BY\n  DECISION, and its \"run under `mirrorstack dev --tunnel`\" error correctly\n  stays: result() routes a trusted-payload invoke to resultDeployed, so the\n  deployed plane cannot reach that string. A deployed consumer reads through\n  the injected Dependencies manifest under the GRANT ceiling, not read-exposed.\n\nTests pin what the platform now depends on. Dispatch constant-time BYTE-compares\nthe credential against a value it recomputes, so verbatim forwarding is a hard\nrequirement -- and because metering is non-fatal by contract, a reshaped\ncredential is a SILENT 403 that stops billing with nothing in the module''s logs.\nBoth legs assert single-valued verbatim forwarding; both assert the credential\nnever reaches an error string, which on the metering path is what a module logs\nstraight into CloudWatch. Verified by mutation: upper-casing the value reddens\nthe verbatim tests, appending it to the non-2xx error reddens the leak test.\n\nNo behavior change, so no module is required to rebuild. Ordering lives entirely\non the platform side: dispatch must accept the per-module credential before the\nprovisioner starts injecting it.\n\nRefs mirrorstack-ai/mirrorstack-core-v2#338\n\nCo-authored-by: Sheng Kun Chang <1sharedaim114@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a10b2ca1799106a44ee15ed19955479643aeafd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/a10b2ca1799106a44ee15ed19955479643aeafd9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/54589f95929cbf205fb8e25153f37ae6d018e2cb","verification":{"payload":"tree a10b2ca1799106a44ee15ed19955479643aeafd9\nparent 1d8b2f7d35963f81edceca78b9938de5986fdef8\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1785683988 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785683988 +0800\n\ndocs(transport): resolve the #146 module->dispatch seam; pin the deployed-plane credential contract (#161)\n\ncore-v2#338 step 6 is the SENDER side of authenticating a deployed module''s\ncallbacks into dispatch. Investigating it produced an unexpected answer: the\nSDK already satisfies it, and shipping code here would have been wrong.\n\nv0.3.1 already sends the credential on both in-scope legs -- meter/meter.go:483\nand internal/core/notify.go:120 both forward MS_INTERNAL_SECRET as\nX-MS-Service-Secret. The deployed plane differs only in WHO populates that\nvariable: the CLI mints a per-session secret under `mirrorstack dev --tunnel`,\nwhile the deploy provisioner injects a per-module credential. Both are opaque\nstrings the SDK forwards untouched, so no SDK code distinguishes them.\n\nThe SDK also CANNOT derive the credential, so injection is not merely the\ncheaper option -- it is the only workable one. Deriving needs the platform\nsecret, which a third-party module process must never hold (holding it lets one\nmodule mint every other module''s credential, destroying the isolation property\nthe scheme exists for), and the module''s catalog UUID, which nothing in the SDK\nreads: MS_MODULE_ID has zero non-test readers here, only two doc mentions.\n\nSo this is doc + tests, with a provably comment-only source diff.\n\n- meter.go''s \"when #146 lands, swap the body of this function\" instruction is\n  resolved and removed. #146 needed no swap: the deployed leg is the same\n  MS_DISPATCH_URL base, injected into every module Lambda by the provisioner.\n  Replaced with the reason and an explicit warning not to repoint the\n  host.docker.internal fallback at production -- that would make a local stack\n  silently emit usage against the real dispatch. resolveNotifyURL carried the\n  same stale marker.\n- moduleSessionSecret documented as no longer tunnel-only; name kept\n  deliberately, since renaming churns every call site for no behavioral gain.\n- dependency_db''s read-exposed proxy documented as staying tunnel-only BY\n  DECISION, and its \"run under `mirrorstack dev --tunnel`\" error correctly\n  stays: result() routes a trusted-payload invoke to resultDeployed, so the\n  deployed plane cannot reach that string. A deployed consumer reads through\n  the injected Dependencies manifest under the GRANT ceiling, not read-exposed.\n\nTests pin what the platform now depends on. Dispatch constant-time BYTE-compares\nthe credential against a value it recomputes, so verbatim forwarding is a hard\nrequirement -- and because metering is non-fatal by contract, a reshaped\ncredential is a SILENT 403 that stops billing with nothing in the module''s logs.\nBoth legs assert single-valued verbatim forwarding; both assert the credential\nnever reaches an error string, which on the metering path is what a module logs\nstraight into CloudWatch. Verified by mutation: upper-casing the value reddens\nthe verbatim tests, appending it to the non-2xx error reddens the leak test.\n\nNo behavior change, so no module is required to rebuild. Ordering lives entirely\non the platform side: dispatch must accept the per-module credential before the\nprovisioner starts injecting it.\n\nRefs mirrorstack-ai/mirrorstack-core-v2#338\n\nCo-authored-by: Sheng Kun Chang <1sharedaim114@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqb2AUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAv0cQAAZLhKv7FIei9hZtxPaQcp2y\nLEQ7fgv4Jr8s9wqxirLVd/XFnGXLl6JY9CJA8dwZOkKmbL8oqElMP2JvJIJwNlRk\n73OWz2+7+2kiJb7HRQN+QxYWPG03xMpcLysEf6oyLcX25Nr/43O6GeGNrKsy/g/1\np+oH1qneGNgBHZZfklUVsHqIadjAQWDPIq+eskYpUSxtPiV3MbZo00P5QatLtlav\nC3cfnjWvICRti8F07llFBOLhYQunb3CUU8/QQnHSQfcaPLmEly88U2sf65GX4RyN\nj/mXZHeQLpeSocnaX0um4T5GGfn/oDry3zebk0yHl11UZDvPGxdUySf3AaAyJP2F\nFrusFDEuzKCFC3GdCh2ZhtLj6l1h5pJbht+lcdMq+tQZ5gptjJNBzrUZ7ZVthPsz\nJwVnH+kJqm6IfHkRJCho5S+vQKmRv0Cf+29SjlPqpXu7xUWD2Jnx6MUgm+n3dNgj\nggDZqQ28+lVYeV0UgBH+/oHUgoYcjoUokmsRgjh2vQVOYR/IE5U+7g5bBu567y5M\n4uoTeMfiKrvciPIiV/684JamaGoWOo2Zqn2yfXvTMoL7G6K6xW+3QzjlA86h5h5K\n8yrgPaYRC8+kuCjPf2ZBB4Kac2kjbXaxe4tM8vJuTNJmWKPysJhW6Wer09Dm9JOf\ndHcN/uxsk0yNVWGWCZ2F\n=7wRe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T15:19:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/54589f95929cbf205fb8e25153f37ae6d018e2cb","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKDU0NTg5Zjk1OTI5Y2JmMjA1ZmI4ZTI1MTUzZjM3YWU2ZDAxOGUyY2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/1d8b2f7d35963f81edceca78b9938de5986fdef8","sha":"1d8b2f7d35963f81edceca78b9938de5986fdef8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/1d8b2f7d35963f81edceca78b9938de5986fdef8"}],"sha":"54589f95929cbf205fb8e25153f37ae6d018e2cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/54589f95929cbf205fb8e25153f37ae6d018e2cb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/1d8b2f7d35963f81edceca78b9938de5986fdef8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-02T08:11:45Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-02T08:11:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: release v0.3.1 (#160)\n\n#158 landed the session-secret header on the meter + Notify ingress but shipped\nwith no version bump and no CHANGELOG entry, so it sits one commit past the\nv0.3.0 tag and no module can pick it up.\n\nThat is a release-ordering hazard, not a hygiene note: api-platform#438 — which\nREQUIRES the header — is already merged, and all three ms-app-modules pin\nv0.3.0. The moment #438 reaches an environment, every dev tunnel 403s on usage\nand notifications until modules rebuild.\n\nOrder: tag v0.3.1 -> bump ms-app-modules -> then promote api-platform.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e0c537655b2954cf9f225b2bf04b4f904b55e557","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/e0c537655b2954cf9f225b2bf04b4f904b55e557"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/1d8b2f7d35963f81edceca78b9938de5986fdef8","verification":{"payload":"tree e0c537655b2954cf9f225b2bf04b4f904b55e557\nparent feccd813bcd4d357eacee91a6f641e90b442ef95\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1785658305 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785658305 +0800\n\nchore: release v0.3.1 (#160)\n\n#158 landed the session-secret header on the meter + Notify ingress but shipped\nwith no version bump and no CHANGELOG entry, so it sits one commit past the\nv0.3.0 tag and no module can pick it up.\n\nThat is a release-ordering hazard, not a hygiene note: api-platform#438 — which\nREQUIRES the header — is already merged, and all three ms-app-modules pin\nv0.3.0. The moment #438 reaches an environment, every dev tunnel 403s on usage\nand notifications until modules rebuild.\n\nOrder: tag v0.3.1 -> bump ms-app-modules -> then promote api-platform.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbvvBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABBoQAHRcOFLCKQ8l93hMVD9WD1wB\nX/Y6oX1VsGEQzSQFdAxZ5/VJahzNM+MBWd+kLhIVqIpBUh+8f7u7ZJ/BmVpfxVOb\nk8owXsyxF8AxHubyDPbQcEhG7y+nM+rQWiYdVf6cEU3i0H3an85XPQtQUd5PJ89u\ncY8Sz/PM1dNdkIMcKEHKrB6LhKj47eP2Se+BDyIYsxYtWHcNLkxf6ld9T53C5Hrw\nbHhm0vyOlqIDas53rfaaGPV6NWNuv0rs7yKMVqD3jt5nIHDC16MTJJTzP3BX8utA\ny1NUAs7SUTL+7WzR8/WDy62BySJbNkezzQfwBBuhLsBdSfDSUIN5ApAowQLTnKy7\nJLd0WvBkuxZZnSS/+7JsMWLg6a/KQ4vzkxstiRUinVMYk5ePK4NNBVXpLecU3Ehx\n+IOLapLB3L/JhswAtQSLxsR0KI3rBOBiLy1sweGb2nirQOn/mVIEe5VGHXWkbtRg\nsHmHtP5Mvte1QP3U83d2W1tSM9ApQpU+rgQdcHOvZ6NlsMzWO29BuZcHinGc+GPL\npUoMG5yTmNzAhcmWDrnJ+OJgmtC+HLcYFK/fKJdGo/V98RZR9hr4xccTSfR4iSpB\n5Bf/gD8jlC+xuqd34YrejB5B0F4rx+8G0xa3k9TpIB+UVEBjyUg11VFy2eim1aec\nHgiTiytwq84uUUHm0BWk\n=XFnm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-02T08:11:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/1d8b2f7d35963f81edceca78b9938de5986fdef8","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKDFkOGIyZjdkMzU5NjNmODFlZGNlY2E3OGI5OTM4ZGU1OTg2ZmRlZjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/feccd813bcd4d357eacee91a6f641e90b442ef95","sha":"feccd813bcd4d357eacee91a6f641e90b442ef95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/feccd813bcd4d357eacee91a6f641e90b442ef95"}],"sha":"1d8b2f7d35963f81edceca78b9938de5986fdef8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/1d8b2f7d35963f81edceca78b9938de5986fdef8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/feccd813bcd4d357eacee91a6f641e90b442ef95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-01T20:42:20Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-01T20:42:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(transport): send the tunnel session secret on the meter + Notify ingress (#158)\n\nDispatch''s POST /apps/{appID}/usage and /apps/{appID}/notifications are mounted\noutside all auth middleware and used to gate the sender on session EXISTENCE\nonly, so an unauthenticated internet caller could POST forged billable usage\nevents for any app with a tunnel-live module. The api-platform side now\nrequires X-MS-Service-Secret to constant-time-match the module''s live\ntunnel-session InternalSecret. This SDK never sent that header on either\nsurface.\n\nBoth transports now send it, reusing the seam dependency_db.go (read-exposed)\nand the CLI''s module-log ingest already ride: MS_INTERNAL_SECRET, the\nper-session value the CLI exports into the module process AND registers with\ndispatch. No new env var, no change to the inbound MS_PLATFORM_TOKEN chain.\n\npostDispatchJSON is shared by ms.Emit and ms.Notify, so the credential is\ncaller-opted-in rather than blanket-applied — a surface can never acquire the\nsession secret by accident. ms.Emit and ms.Call are unchanged.\n\nUnset secret stays best-effort: no header, no early error, request still sent.\nA deployed module legitimately has no tunnel session today, and metering must\nnever break a module''s request path — dispatch is the fail-closed enforcement\npoint. The deployed-module signing seam is core-v2#338 step 7.\n\nMUST LAND WITH api-platform fix/usage-ingest-auth: without that PR this header\nis inert, and without this PR ms.Record/ms.Notify 403 under\n`mirrorstack dev --tunnel`.\n\nPart of mirrorstack-ai/mirrorstack-core-v2#337\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3482100fa4c8b29630696f6b9c0462ee4c429f95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/3482100fa4c8b29630696f6b9c0462ee4c429f95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/feccd813bcd4d357eacee91a6f641e90b442ef95","verification":{"payload":"tree 3482100fa4c8b29630696f6b9c0462ee4c429f95\nparent b1a115bb92d0ba63a0d43740ec627c23af7d85b3\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1785616940 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785616940 +0800\n\nfix(transport): send the tunnel session secret on the meter + Notify ingress (#158)\n\nDispatch''s POST /apps/{appID}/usage and /apps/{appID}/notifications are mounted\noutside all auth middleware and used to gate the sender on session EXISTENCE\nonly, so an unauthenticated internet caller could POST forged billable usage\nevents for any app with a tunnel-live module. The api-platform side now\nrequires X-MS-Service-Secret to constant-time-match the module''s live\ntunnel-session InternalSecret. This SDK never sent that header on either\nsurface.\n\nBoth transports now send it, reusing the seam dependency_db.go (read-exposed)\nand the CLI''s module-log ingest already ride: MS_INTERNAL_SECRET, the\nper-session value the CLI exports into the module process AND registers with\ndispatch. No new env var, no change to the inbound MS_PLATFORM_TOKEN chain.\n\npostDispatchJSON is shared by ms.Emit and ms.Notify, so the credential is\ncaller-opted-in rather than blanket-applied — a surface can never acquire the\nsession secret by accident. ms.Emit and ms.Call are unchanged.\n\nUnset secret stays best-effort: no header, no early error, request still sent.\nA deployed module legitimately has no tunnel session today, and metering must\nnever break a module''s request path — dispatch is the fail-closed enforcement\npoint. The deployed-module signing seam is core-v2#338 step 7.\n\nMUST LAND WITH api-platform fix/usage-ingest-auth: without that PR this header\nis inert, and without this PR ms.Record/ms.Notify 403 under\n`mirrorstack dev --tunnel`.\n\nPart of mirrorstack-ai/mirrorstack-core-v2#337\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqblosCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgukQAD4U6hAeIlahxHqMHtm2KdRP\nMyFsdbFRXH5KIo5i0nxeZsl1xAUHYdG5nTyLKR3PJ6LSxdnHZwSB8Co3gIDLDAEf\nTPGoY78isYdJG2ERm3nQoQ3vCUtOiIwQgv8BoLMqgYlYy5HYEcomdpOr8DV1LC/S\nCEaio5/qkqWHwsoYD0eE94CNLeY/JEzhp+xVJhoBSlbcSlAr1ldcl6CPQo/2ZRj7\nfK0ZLAGJce2w+FV9sSIuXsZoJchgtgVZUipzwf9WpbTFdl9mrgdI39Iweryi9921\nHmX3lTS6FiZiGViy5aEF8pKGXXFz2ITtNGbmddpJa4yOlO4HOpIF6CavgmOfRQa/\nN2VQzZyaxbdHJosLOpPUMpqrMlqG51x7vm/v641ezXj3s78EL38jNv/CQSvVac7r\n/cYFcEMh3wn9gREs4GdoK/yj/Fe+Dpp19yd81sfKMrZuiiAY+IVwLTUctVwa+F98\nitRvQ9Z28yiTW8PdDoUXDYoaQvFuiHCleQtbKaQWZQUuDFrJicOx9bW0XRFC+L8B\nEciRd7JPtPxO812Pe4qY5/gWLP+lt+HQfVMObmDPv2ICy2Wznz+clgViY03QuNOy\ne+b3+MqBWdTgjA4O3nTJkDAYvhV6K1+PhYvmsEmm9d0duut3j+3Ls875jQj15tYG\n6dZ2t3g3fiyrpXJbSegi\n=Ns7p\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-01T20:42:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/feccd813bcd4d357eacee91a6f641e90b442ef95","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKGZlY2NkODEzYmNkNGQzNTdlYWNlZTkxYTZmNjQxZTkwYjQ0MmVmOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/b1a115bb92d0ba63a0d43740ec627c23af7d85b3","sha":"b1a115bb92d0ba63a0d43740ec627c23af7d85b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/b1a115bb92d0ba63a0d43740ec627c23af7d85b3"}],"sha":"feccd813bcd4d357eacee91a6f641e90b442ef95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/feccd813bcd4d357eacee91a6f641e90b442ef95"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/b1a115bb92d0ba63a0d43740ec627c23af7d85b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-30T03:40:24Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-30T03:40:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: release v0.3.0 (#157)\n\n* chore: release v0.3.0\n\nMinor bump, not patch: ms.ContributesTo''s first parameter changed from a bare\nhost id to a versioned spec (id or id@constraint), matching ms.DependsOn. Existing\ncalls keep compiling — an unpinned spec still parses — but the manifest wire shape\ngained contributesTo[].constraint and provides[].payload, so the catalog and any\nmanifest consumer see a new contract. Pre-1.0 that belongs in the minor.\n\nShips the three features accumulated since v0.2.7: co-located dev cross-module\nreads (#152), the dispatch-base fallback warning (#153), and contribution payload\nschemas + versioned ContributesTo (#154).\n\nCutting this unblocks ms-app-modules #72 and #73, which cannot go green while the\nproxy still serves v0.2.7 without the versioned signature.\n\n* docs: complete the v0.3.0 changelog\n\nReview found the section described the co-located dev reads and the contribution\npayload schemas but omitted two shipped fixes: the singleflight refcache race\n(#148) and the dispatch-base fallback warning (#153). Both are user-visible —\none silently orphaned pooled resources, the other left a tunnel session reporting\nan unexplained connection refusal — so neither belongs out of a release note.\n\nRange re-reconciled against git log v0.2.7..main in both directions: nothing\ndescribed that did not ship, nothing shipped that is not described. CI-only\nchanges (#146, #147) and the jsonparser bump (#149) stay omitted, matching how\nearlier released sections treat them.","tree":{"sha":"710d4e4201a412420a61a78ac818291f97d5af7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/710d4e4201a412420a61a78ac818291f97d5af7e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/b1a115bb92d0ba63a0d43740ec627c23af7d85b3","verification":{"payload":"tree 710d4e4201a412420a61a78ac818291f97d5af7e\nparent 8e9aa5ae0f185d7b36b2a6616b1d3b21c1637c20\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1785382824 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785382824 +0800\n\nchore: release v0.3.0 (#157)\n\n* chore: release v0.3.0\n\nMinor bump, not patch: ms.ContributesTo''s first parameter changed from a bare\nhost id to a versioned spec (id or id@constraint), matching ms.DependsOn. Existing\ncalls keep compiling — an unpinned spec still parses — but the manifest wire shape\ngained contributesTo[].constraint and provides[].payload, so the catalog and any\nmanifest consumer see a new contract. Pre-1.0 that belongs in the minor.\n\nShips the three features accumulated since v0.2.7: co-located dev cross-module\nreads (#152), the dispatch-base fallback warning (#153), and contribution payload\nschemas + versioned ContributesTo (#154).\n\nCutting this unblocks ms-app-modules #72 and #73, which cannot go green while the\nproxy still serves v0.2.7 without the versioned signature.\n\n* docs: complete the v0.3.0 changelog\n\nReview found the section described the co-located dev reads and the contribution\npayload schemas but omitted two shipped fixes: the singleflight refcache race\n(#148) and the dispatch-base fallback warning (#153). Both are user-visible —\none silently orphaned pooled resources, the other left a tunnel session reporting\nan unexplained connection refusal — so neither belongs out of a release note.\n\nRange re-reconciled against git log v0.2.7..main in both directions: nothing\ndescribed that did not ship, nothing shipped that is not described. CI-only\nchanges (#146, #147) and the jsonparser bump (#149) stay omitted, matching how\nearlier released sections treat them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaseoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqC4QAKdk0pztR4ZLU65jqalsBsGl\nyKdlPYGuay914UNlB2MYd/hnpQsw2j2dPEhfdOXXF44IQhibNdoIx0rEDWiv9CER\nz064M8gowPceNvC03w+SjohqRp+LwlZqW9UaRMbAlGyN8rrVDhnXzkDR/e6Jy9PC\n9dGKg6v58+Y6qLVjcL2TIPQI0EQotoOGcBwpoY4TxPujvIrFiQaUeo4yoxk/Kij8\nGDUZz5YugCTE2019C5FpeiYY53S4im/63AE308HNGmb54bcfyUGj/cN+qMW+F4WX\n+1eGgX0AizXPGksVtmF3xc0cIACUf1o7BL5bZFwEF2Km45NN2irSHkwuI0t3k+xM\nyrVp5MLUVFgbqTkPwdRlBxLqUqQpLgTUQTAunPGmy/ey3ulKPbRt/rP/wpz8U2r9\nBMWJfvpDZSN0oGX0q9KN+2TaYsGcc5Bfa7zvfnRGLHGhVaw+mjJGM30LOOFx+w1Y\nqvlIDkC1ZoeAOLUbMRoAYVdGefPOWOq8Jx5oA7Gt681kRJvHGdSvgRL4s6jp+sOg\necisLd/TSUkCNwUrkVOEkQPkrRMpbZodsrpyIHs8VgbX/JKXat4N/GJwTEHiDyF0\nqyH3yOlXB3VGvY10Px9IAIJWf0Ztl9kpbIThT2iBpsUOe1PqkKyHGoPzr80qRg0n\n7s9OCE+0pFph1tv/DE5V\n=gx9b\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-30T03:40:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/b1a115bb92d0ba63a0d43740ec627c23af7d85b3","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKGIxYTExNWJiOTJkMGJhNjNhMGQ0Mzc0MGVjNjI3YzIzYWY3ZDg1YjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/8e9aa5ae0f185d7b36b2a6616b1d3b21c1637c20","sha":"8e9aa5ae0f185d7b36b2a6616b1d3b21c1637c20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/8e9aa5ae0f185d7b36b2a6616b1d3b21c1637c20"}],"sha":"b1a115bb92d0ba63a0d43740ec627c23af7d85b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/b1a115bb92d0ba63a0d43740ec627c23af7d85b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/8e9aa5ae0f185d7b36b2a6616b1d3b21c1637c20/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T08:00:16Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T08:00:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: publish contribution payload schemas and version ContributesTo (#154)\n\nA contribution slot shipped a NAME and nothing else. The payload validator is\na closure built by Provide[T] where T is in scope, so it has only ever existed\ninside the host''s process: a contributor could discover that \"user-detail-blocks\"\nexists and still have no way to learn it wants {title, bodyUrl} short of reading\nthe host''s source — which a third-party author cannot do at all. Provide[T] now\nderives the full recursive JSON Schema of T and the manifest carries it at\nprovides[].payload.\n\nCyclic payload types go through $defs rather than being inlined. This is not a\nformatting preference: invopop inlining recurses until the module STACK-OVERFLOWS\nat boot, crashing the process rather than returning an error. ExpandedStruct is\nnot a way back to an inline top level either — it lifts the root out of $defs\nwhile nested self-references still point at it, dangling the $ref for exactly the\ncyclic case. Both behaviours are pinned by tests.\n\nContributesTo was also the one cross-module reference in the SDK carrying no\nversion, while DependsOn has always taken id@constraint. A contribution couples\nyou to the host''s declared slot surface as much as a dependency couples you to\nits API, and a host may reshape or remove a slot on any bump. It now takes the\nsame spec through the same parser, carries the range at contributesTo[].constraint,\nand panics at startup on a host id or SemVer range that does not parse.","tree":{"sha":"5ec13f6938e44608d11f0bf25f5b7b1c8cdec389","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/5ec13f6938e44608d11f0bf25f5b7b1c8cdec389"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/8e9aa5ae0f185d7b36b2a6616b1d3b21c1637c20","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ec13f6938e44608d11f0bf25f5b7b1c8cdec389\nparent 26ee52ae3c9a7834a113522b7925fa63cf159d74\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1785225616 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785225616 +0800\n\nfeat: publish contribution payload schemas and version ContributesTo (#154)\n\nA contribution slot shipped a NAME and nothing else. The payload validator is\na closure built by Provide[T] where T is in scope, so it has only ever existed\ninside the host''s process: a contributor could discover that \"user-detail-blocks\"\nexists and still have no way to learn it wants {title, bodyUrl} short of reading\nthe host''s source — which a third-party author cannot do at all. Provide[T] now\nderives the full recursive JSON Schema of T and the manifest carries it at\nprovides[].payload.\n\nCyclic payload types go through $defs rather than being inlined. This is not a\nformatting preference: invopop inlining recurses until the module STACK-OVERFLOWS\nat boot, crashing the process rather than returning an error. ExpandedStruct is\nnot a way back to an inline top level either — it lifts the root out of $defs\nwhile nested self-references still point at it, dangling the $ref for exactly the\ncyclic case. Both behaviours are pinned by tests.\n\nContributesTo was also the one cross-module reference in the SDK carrying no\nversion, while DependsOn has always taken id@constraint. A contribution couples\nyou to the host''s declared slot surface as much as a dependency couples you to\nits API, and a host may reshape or remove a slot on any bump. It now takes the\nsame spec through the same parser, carries the range at contributesTo[].constraint,\nand panics at startup on a host id or SemVer range that does not parse.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaGGQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1DgQACPd6qkf9BHGW46dorFwr+IA\n90jWZuAd1oQZiE2QYuINwf/2G6A8dsM2aSp8OvAtkTLlasKlqg0ZNJroozbt7nm2\nEkeFdAoiSng4MWsYkpG5xd8c/gIehoobKJ+UIUmd8cvtfJGbtKJbbHcKX7Ew6KrQ\nnirOW4lTeUvvZkZKu25ipAPDRLbAApdKc5LWdmMxBZvrNQ20UPCuaIoyZ40i3e/e\nAp35QdDnDoOuB/Shy7QN4qxaOyUPT/xEeSfmIVfJhLyqacUNOD2F+Lf0x8j/0ZnT\nCsPRFTwd9JvvKjNZOu/6y9EMGsYp+F7MCKIQBgIztzrGlRgXoxpCL/5eqH3LuFV5\nu4W6L301z720gHZTqhm9bJzbEE6HHAT3kACYuFzUTolIFneQ71dvNWe/FAY+yIFB\n3+sJfNMSQJRdQhItTXLBTIo0YO