-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/3dcbabd924a4143ea66144666f299bc5b9063b43/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T18:05:04Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T18:05:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: surface the dispatch-base fallback instead of failing mute (#153)\n\nMS_DISPATCH_URL being unset silently routed every ms.Call/Emit/Notify at\nthe host.docker.internal:8083 dev fallback. A dev-tunnel session runs no\nlocal platform stack, so that address is dead and the caller saw only a\nbare connection error — which oauth-core could only report as a 502 with\nno indication of where the request had been aimed.\n\nWarn once (sync.Once) when the fallback is taken, and wrap the transport\nerror with the method and resolved URL so the dead host names itself.\n\nNo behavior change: the fallback value is untouched, deliberately. Aiming\nit at production would make a genuinely-local platform stack silently talk\nto prod.\n\nRefs mirrorstack-ai/mirrorstack-core-v2#220","tree":{"sha":"919a469bdd3ad21e8f2268766759d4ad49557143","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/919a469bdd3ad21e8f2268766759d4ad49557143"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/3dcbabd924a4143ea66144666f299bc5b9063b43","verification":{"payload":"tree 919a469bdd3ad21e8f2268766759d4ad49557143\nparent e442e9657acd9dfe822f75893d6887152b6fd89c\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1785089104 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785089104 +0800\n\nfix: surface the dispatch-base fallback instead of failing mute (#153)\n\nMS_DISPATCH_URL being unset silently routed every ms.Call/Emit/Notify at\nthe host.docker.internal:8083 dev fallback. A dev-tunnel session runs no\nlocal platform stack, so that address is dead and the caller saw only a\nbare connection error — which oauth-core could only report as a 502 with\nno indication of where the request had been aimed.\n\nWarn once (sync.Once) when the fallback is taken, and wrap the transport\nerror with the method and resolved URL so the dead host names itself.\n\nNo behavior change: the fallback value is untouched, deliberately. Aiming\nit at production would make a genuinely-local platform stack silently talk\nto prod.\n\nRefs mirrorstack-ai/mirrorstack-core-v2#220","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZkxQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkpQQAHHFa5P7EJbDAUUvNZWpVjNb\nsmlEXU98oo0quvPAfUAKGVidzr6M0WHhwpCG/OVpd01Ae8tNSl1NxDF5q+czRNNz\nrVKbmZmpXEtcb+cygZro+iAOFfTciE+3obvOxdoqydhERRqV+gn9jR98trVg/Sd1\nRS5VwuhmWAxObh3SHjYqTLSjpDDKVEW/GAn4T96PMChjRdTECsNrHo/kL0UdoHxo\nBRq4LSqZ5j4y9uMXowaIUnOQyz3/EmXVBDNEcaJnnjdBU7wdHfOSgYAkEklujywy\ntneV3ZINVQqNnZWdR95vtOUQSPqW9ONWf627QN+332HmlED7fCrLHiuK9kf9kVBe\n476AYRsaVmaF0Mgikep086E85pEfYXscbwYz+xgr3fNDYHx0vdCTXD6OqoCGVgze\nNbIWWLngrXeX2NdKstJiohwPXf74YdQ9BNJtI3XE7s4ZBTiZg/MQwHSQEx6fjijh\ndpu6TpIgNB95N5At4AoSOo0xtwKSIfAfeg64nUduced06EXMRM2qj1aTWGTdVSuL\nMMJJZBmB/d7ENkVh3v/lVjz6I3P+s6bHEIuEtE76DEVbpc91C9dNTLEtrYuCBIi+\nXp+BRuXyE0agKqfLadE9FW3Akg6ynCv1zdCS1O+JC4aZ6I04L6N4JjN7SDlLJUqB\nFG+5VZwV2Ypm9AzxEXlK\n=LIgP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-26T18:05:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/3dcbabd924a4143ea66144666f299bc5b9063b43","node_id":"C_kwDOR2zucNoAKDNkY2JhYmQ5MjRhNDE0M2VhNjYxNDQ2NjZmMjk5YmM1YjkwNjNiNDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commit/e442e9657acd9dfe822f75893d6887152b6fd89c","sha":"e442e9657acd9dfe822f75893d6887152b6fd89c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/e442e9657acd9dfe822f75893d6887152b6fd89c"}],"sha":"3dcbabd924a4143ea66144666f299bc5b9063b43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/3dcbabd924a4143ea66144666f299bc5b9063b43"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56163905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/I-am-nothing","id":56163905,"login":"I-am-nothing","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTYzOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/I-am-nothing","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/commits/e442e9657acd9dfe822f75893d6887152b6fd89c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-22T05:17:20Z","email":"56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sheng Kun Chang"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-22T05:17:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: resolve cross-module reads locally when the producer is co-located (#152)\n\nms.DependencyDB sent every dev-plane read to the platform''s read-exposed\nproxy, on the premise that a dev module holds no socket to the platform\nDB. That is true of a remote producer and false of a co-located one:\nunder `mirrorstack dev` the producer and consumer are two processes\nsharing one Postgres and one app schema, so the proxy returned the\nproducer''s PRODUCTION rows to a consumer whose own rows are local.\n\nA co-located read now runs against the local database, authorized by the\nconsumer''s DependsOn and the producer''s ExposeTable, in a READ ONLY\ntransaction over the same sanitized SELECT the deployed plane uses.\nDiscovery rides a dev-only directory table each module publishes itself\ninto — the database is the carrier because the dev runner clears the\nchild environment down to four keys and MS_LOCAL_DB_URL is the only\nguaranteed cross-module channel among them. A row is a lease, not a\nrecord: heartbeated while the process lives and ignored once it ages\nout, so a producer you stopped degrades to the proxy rather than\nsilently serving its abandoned tables.\n\nStrictly additive: a producer absent from the directory keeps the proxy\npath unchanged, and the deployed plane is untouched.\n\nCloses #151\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"adf0bc27cad3438a899a79577c1225788afafb4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/trees/adf0bc27cad3438a899a79577c1225788afafb4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mirrorstack-ai/app-module-sdk/git/commits/e442e9657acd9dfe822f75893d6887152b6fd89c","verification":{"payload":"tree adf0bc27cad3438a899a79577c1225788afafb4a\nparent 4abb7dab6e41a18affbe75340afc65b6290e7baf\nauthor Sheng Kun Chang <56163905+I-am-nothing@users.noreply.github.com> 1784697440 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784697440 +0800\n\nfeat: resolve cross-module reads locally when the producer is co-located (#152)\n\nms.DependencyDB sent every dev-plane read to the platform''s read-exposed\nproxy, on the premise that a dev module holds no socket to the platform\nDB. That is true of a remote producer and false of a co-located one:\nunder `mirrorstack dev` the producer and consumer are two processes\nsharing one Postgres and one app schema, so the proxy returned the\nproducer''s PRODUCTION rows to a consumer whose own rows are local.\n\nA co-located read now runs against the local database, authorized by the\nconsumer''s DependsOn and the producer''s ExposeTable, in a READ ONLY\ntransaction over the same sanitized SELECT the deployed plane uses.\nDiscovery rides a dev-only directory table each module publishes itself\ninto — the database is the carrier because the dev runner clears the\nchild environment down to four keys and MS_LOCAL_DB_URL is the only\nguaranteed cross-module channel among them. A row is a lease, not a\nrecord: heartbeated while the process lives and ignored once it ages\nout, so a producer you stopped degrades to the proxy rather than\nsilently serving its abandoned tables.\n\nStrictly additive: a producer absent from the directory keeps the proxy\npath unchanged, and the deployed plane is untouched.\n\nCloses #151\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYFJhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABIEQABy3MQfB94CGMYpoDq/ZrkSd\nHOArNO16Wlb0uPUaWHot0h9P4Vgv8bt/MZxkBEx9Qe30e3Vb+D+OTwpMmSRwytDF\nS2ura5g4uJwJvv04YuMX6H7vg5KeOnrdDLD0eVxkOBoD2Fk9+y3/Xu7V+UtB1jwc\nhU1OdJGjFdqNCLDxf0BmZZn7p8jXyRZmMWWfGSeZPtmYFeWSW6IUfxbgnsYRFYmu\nJ0UOb/ZNvhEZN+0vL4Gu3cUWTADo27pJCQADME0rkoNYDee+FhVPTuKeBiNJg1QD\n0NKz1hgTCisGx6F9fjhRomp3xPrz+C3H1CFJAKNwiDoNzdziJa1vKuQWeGVXUkBs\nx4H4ah9HMR5CsgVO9XPQ6zGUXUbcEaA194vkXUFQW+N2XSNTcARXUbD2VRs3bZHM\nZL1mr7blF3L/Si8yvzmfapUfDlSGt8gACXJX+PeBR0XD3VCmYX8MhWcWji8EB/zA\n1mYl7gs+Cmgnb29SC2uSFvPVmwD0mL0Py9VjQVlaYYiQ9eTYnSIQiiXq6lgWOFmW\nSj5Np28BDOj9LmaFCBGcIHg2etVm7JWggfmthsUnMGj/Q1I9xjKKBuLt8uGNYKKL\nMUyaslaJlOVeTe8wjafx6hLvHtFb0p6Aw517ywCi6ZmM+ryCr07AK2PcR0Ki3uzv\nEcLMGFvNKWaIdPLugfdL\n=HPXG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-22T05:17:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.c