a/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dirkwa","id":86628605,"login":"dirkwa","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjI4NjA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/app-dock/commits/a693f10b35e2131ea591ea668153b13dc3273dfd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T10:09:27Z","email":"dirkwahrheit@gmail.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T10:14:55Z","email":"dirkwahrheit@gmail.com","name":"Dirk Wahrheit"},"message":"ci: label a pull request from its title\n\n.github/release.yml sorts the release notes by PR label, and a PR\nopened from the command line carries none, so every entry landed\nunder Other.\n\nlabel-by-title.yml labels a PR when it is opened, reopened or its\ntitle edited: feat and perf get enhancement, fix gets bug, docs gets\ndocumentation, and build, ci, test, chore, refactor and style get\nskip-changelog, which leaves them out of the notes. It keeps one of\nthose labels at a time, so a retitled PR swaps its label. A body\nedit leaves the labels alone, so a label set by hand stays until the\ntitle changes. It reads only the title and checks nothing out, which\nis what makes pull_request_target safe here.","tree":{"sha":"72976370ae55cf6ccef22603cded87f134c5a11b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/app-dock/git/trees/72976370ae55cf6ccef22603cded87f134c5a11b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/app-dock/git/commits/a693f10b35e2131ea591ea668153b13dc3273dfd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"ve