,{"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/app-dock/commit/f4f614c1f5b09c78853931397c245d64b3530d6b","sha":"f4f614c1f5b09c78853931397c245d64b3530d6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/app-dock/commits/f4f614c1f5b09c78853931397c245d64b3530d6b"}],"sha":"896a3210ea189076a3892f862cc60a07057a0eb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/app-dock/commits/896a3210ea189076a3892f862cc60a07057a0eb8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/app-dock/commits/f4f614c1f5b09c78853931397c245d64b3530d6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-27T18:37:37Z","email":"dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com","name":"dirkwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-27T18:37:37Z","email":"dirkwahrtheit@gmail.com","name":"dirkwa"},"message":"feat: add optional fullscreen toggle button to dock (#21)\n\nAdds a showFullscreenButton config (off by default) that places a\nsquare-four-corners button in the utility-button row of the dock. Tap\ntoggles native browser fullscreen on document.documentElement. Targets\ndocumentElement (not body or the iframe) so the active webapp goes\nfullscreen with the dock and the iframe is not the fullscreen element,\npreserving double-tap gesture passthrough.\n\nThe button is feature-detected via document.fullscreenEnabled and hidden\nwhen the Fullscreen API is unavailable (notably iPadOS Safari, where\n\"Add to Home Screen\" remains the equivalent path). A fullscreenchange\nlistener keeps the icon and label in sync when the user presses Esc.\n\nCloses #21.","tree":{"sha":"1fbc74405293abb419f060e223aebf32d49e55c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/app-dock/git/trees/1fbc74405293abb419f060e223aebf32d49e55c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/app-dock/git/commits/f4f614c1f5b09c78853931397c245d64b3530d6b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/SignalK/app-dock/commit/f4f614c1f5b09c78853931397c2