A1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/app-dock/commits/dfe6cc89a96075feaa6a00633fd8b5bf8d2b1ef9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-18T22:53:13Z","email":"dirkwahrheit@gmail.com","name":"dirkwa"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-18T22:53:13Z","email":"dirkwahrheit@gmail.com","name":"dirkwa"},"message":"ci: generate release notes from merged PRs\n\nReplaces the mikepenz changelog step with softprops'' built-in\ngenerate_release_notes, which calls GitHub''s native release-notes API.\nUses PR titles directly — no categorization config, no reliance on\ncommit-message discipline, one less third-party action to keep pinned.\n\nOur last two releases came out with body \"- no changes\" because\nmikepenz''s default config filters by PR labels we don''t apply.","tree":{"sha":"78a0ded97720c1d777357631af978cbd43d065d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/app-dock/git/trees/78a0ded97720c1d777357631af978cbd43d065d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SignalK/app-dock/git/commits/dfe6cc89a96075feaa6a00633fd8b5bf8d2b1ef9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86628605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dirkwa/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"",