rl":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commit/5a25981e27c54ccad9e1515cb304947b01a10213","node_id":"C_kwDOR3zpP9oAKDVhMjU5ODFlMjdjNTRjY2FkOWUxNTE1Y2IzMDQ5NDdiMDFhMTAyMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commit/c7306a9a31791db00202665775dc236b3bb7f329","sha":"c7306a9a31791db00202665775dc236b3bb7f329","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commits/c7306a9a31791db00202665775dc236b3bb7f329"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commit/90f7376aac2899c39b578d99f23dc9457cea3afe","sha":"90f7376aac2899c39b578d99f23dc9457cea3afe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commits/90f7376aac2899c39b578d99f23dc9457cea3afe"}],"sha":"5a25981e27c54ccad9e1515cb304947b01a10213","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commits/5a25981e27c54ccad9e1515cb304947b01a10213"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4515317?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kyjin","id":4515317,"login":"kyjin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MTUzMTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commits/c7306a9a31791db00202665775dc236b3bb7f329/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T02:48:18Z","email":"yours012@gmail.com","name":"kyjin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T02:48:18Z","email":"yours012@gmail.com","name":"kyjin"},"message":"fix(practices): P3-142 — sweep TMPDIR trap + prover''s remaining fold-dependent cases\n\nax-case-sensitive-sweep.sh built its attack topology under ${TMPDIR:-/tmp} without ever\npointing TMPDIR at the case-sensitive volume it attaches, so run-all-guards.sh''s\n--include-fixtures sweep of ax-prove-hermetic-runtime.sh silently tested the BOOT volume''s\n(case-insensitive) semantics instead — every prior 357/0 green was partially vacuous for\nTMPDIR-based probes. TMPDIR is now forced onto the attached volume and the forced directory\nis itself probed case-sensitive before the guard suite runs; a new exit 6 covers failure to\nforce or probe it (documented in the header, --probe-only now exercises it too).\n\nax-prove-hermetic-runtime.sh''s casefold/dircase/nacase/symcase/symjump/symmidfinal cases all\nassume $WORK folds the axis under test (their SECOND spelling is either never materialized on\ndisk — casefold/dircase/nacase register it via index plumbing alone — or the alias census in\ntree_fingerprint.py groups strictly by OBSERVED (st_dev, st_ino), so it can only ever observe\nthe alias on a folding filesystem). On a non-folding filesystem the premise cannot be built and\nr9_premise''s own checks call violation(), a genuine harness FAIL rather than an honest skip.\n\nReused the existing ax_fold_probe/WORK_FOLDS_CASE/WORK_FOLDS_NORM machinery from yesterday''s\nP3-139 fix (symmidslash/symmidsub/symmidnfd) — moved it earlier in the file (before ANY case\nthat needs it) rather than reinventing it, and added one axis-specific probe (WORK_FOLDS_NACASE,\nusing the case''s own É/é bytes) for nacase''s non-ASCII-case premise. Each of the six cases is now\ngated on the correct axis and reports SKIPPED-N with probe evidence when the premise cannot be\nbuilt; nfcnfd/symnfcnfd/symmidnfd (normalization) and symloop/symlegit (no alias at all) are\nleft ungated, per direct measurement on a real case-sensitive APFS volume showing normalization\nstill folds there while case does not.\n\nVerified: Arm 1 (default case-insensitive APFS) — prover exit 0, SKIPPED 0, byte-identical to\nthe pre-fix baseline modulo the random tmp path. Arm 2 (case-sensitive APFS volume, TMPDIR\nforced onto it) — prover exit 0, VIOLATION 0, SKIPPED 29 (23 new + 6 from P3-139), with\nnfcnfd/symnfcnfd/symmidnfd correctly still running (this volume folds normalization even while\ncase-sensitive) and the Z5 false-positive control correctly selecting the REAL distinct-inode\narm now that $WORK itself sits on the case-sensitive volume.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c2dff14983cbd5126f23aa014823d35b9a1f273","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/git/trees/2c2dff14983cbd5126f23aa014823d35b9a1f273"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/git/commits/c7306a9a31791db00202665775dc236b3bb7f329","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4515317?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kyjin","id":4515317,"login":"kyjin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MTUzMTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commit/c7306a9a31791db00202665775dc236b3bb7f329","node_id":"C_kwDOR3zpP9oAKGM3MzA2YTlhMzE3OTFkYjAwMjAyNjY1Nzc1ZGMyMzZiM2JiN2YzMjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commit/e16601090b4309e452ba0acb752f3e9624730e93","sha":"e16601090b4309e452ba0acb752f3e9624730e93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commits/e16601090b4309e452ba0acb752f3e9624730e93"}],"sha":"c7306a9a31791db00202665775dc236b3bb7f329","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commits/c7306a9a31791db00202665775dc236b3bb7f329"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4515317?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kyjin","id":4515317,"login":"kyjin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MTUzMTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commits/90f7376aac2899c39b578d99f23dc9457cea3afe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T02:35:12Z","email":"yours012@gmail.com","name":"kyjin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T02:35:12Z","email":"yours012@gmail.com","name":"kyjin"},"message":"fix(hooks+generator): D-5 unique tmp naming + D-6 complete hook templates & probe\n\nD-5 — practices/generate_index.sh: replace the fixed \"$OUT.tmp\" write target\nwith a unique per-invocation mktemp path (+ EXIT trap cleanup). Two concurrent\nruns against the same catalog previously truncated each other''s in-flight\nwrite. Verified byte-identical INDEX.md for both practices and practices-react\nafter regeneration, plus zero tmp residue on a real corrupted-catalog failure\n(pre-existing OUT untouched). Updated generate_index_selftest.sh''s residue\nassertions from a literal \".tmp\" check to a glob, matching the new naming.\n\nD-6 — skills/ax-install-hooks/SKILL.md: the java line in Branch A/B was a\nbash comment (never executed) regardless of ax.config.json''s stacks — made it\na real, uncommented command (still parameterized: swap module path/task name).\nAdded a \"Non-vacuous verification (mandatory)\" probe section modeled on\nax-install-react-enforcement/ax-install-java-enforcement: reuse the\nstack-specific gate''s own probe if one is installed (proves the full chain),\nelse plant a temporary `exit 1` in the hook file to prove the wiring itself,\nattempt a real git commit, require BLOCK, clean up, confirm a clean commit\npasses. Includes the vacuous-wiring diagnostic order (hooksPath → executable\nbit → stack detection → underlying script). Updated the self-check checklist\naccordingly, and resolved docs/USAGE-GUIDE.md §5 + docs/START-PROMPTS.md\n경로 B [5]''s \"hooks has no probe, test manually\" language to match.\n\nMechanically verified (headless): both the react-branch and java-branch\nBranch A (core.hooksPath) templates, in throwaway git repos, both directions\n(violating commit BLOCKED / clean commit PASSED). React used a minimal fake\npackage.json lint script; java used a gradle-free stand-in script — both test\nthe HOOK''s plumbing only, not the real ESLint/ArchUnit rule detection, which\nremains untested outside a live interactive skill run. Husky/lefthook\n(Branch B/C) share the same command lines but were not separately wired and\ntested.","tree":{"sha":"b3fc7e6faa09a241f0d4377b56abb86172d647ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/git/trees/b3fc7e6faa09a241f0d4377b56abb86172d647ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/git/commits/90f7376aac2899c39b578d99f23dc9457cea3afe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4515317?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kyjin","id":4515317,"login":"kyjin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MTUzMTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commit/90f7376aac2899c39b578d99f23dc9457cea3afe","node_id":"C_kwDOR3zpP9oAKDkwZjczNz