ions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commit/995d72450923749f72d25db7cdcf61cf87516442","node_id":"C_kwDOR3zpP9oAKDk5NWQ3MjQ1MDkyMzc0OWY3MmQyNWRiN2NkY2Y2MWNmODc1MTY0NDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commit/95dfaa78fa8d60b46ef7ed94b9975966c130a488","sha":"95dfaa78fa8d60b46ef7ed94b9975966c130a488","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commits/95dfaa78fa8d60b46ef7ed94b9975966c130a488"}],"sha":"995d72450923749f72d25db7cdcf61cf87516442","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commits/995d72450923749f72d25db7cdcf61cf87516442"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4515317?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kyjin","id":4515317,"login":"kyjin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MTUzMTc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kyjin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/commits/63272eb46aa3559d9e65a9e1db60b26040f5f605/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T00:48:08Z","email":"yours012@gmail.com","name":"kyjin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T00:48:08Z","email":"yours012@gmail.com","name":"kyjin"},"message":"fix(p3-139): symmidslash/symmidsub/symmidnfd → explicit SKIP on non-folding FS\n\nax-prove-hermetic-runtime.sh''s symmidslash/symmidsub cases construct their alias\nthrough CASE folding (dirlink ≡ DIRLINK); symmidnfd through NORMALIZATION folding\n(NFC é-link ≡ NFD e+combining-acute-link). On a filesystem that does not fold the\naxis under test, the premise cannot be built at all, and r9_premise''s generic\n\"this filesystem does not fold the axis under test\" branch was reporting that as\na VIOLATION — the wrong verdict for a premise mismatch (BACKLOG P3-139).\n\nAdd ax_fold_probe (mirrors cs_probe''s own shape: write one spelling, ask for the\nother) and gate the six symmidslash/symmidsub r9_case calls behind a CASE-fold\nprobe and the two symmidnfd calls behind a NORMALIZATION-fold probe, both against\n$WORK — the same directory those cases build their sandboxes in. When the axis\ndoes not fold, print an explicit SKIPPED note naming the case tags, the missing\npremise, and the probed (dev,ino) evidence, and track it in a SKIPPED counter\nsurfaced in the final banner. Never absorbed into the pass/fail verdict: the\noverall exit code is still governed by FAIL alone.\n\nVerified both arms:\n  - default (case+normalization-folding) APFS: all cases run exactly as before,\n    exit 0, no SKIPPED, no VIOLATION.\n  - case-sensitive APFS volume (hdiutil create -fs \"Case-sensitive APFS\"): the\n    six CASE cases SKIP with reason; symmidnfd still RUNS (this volume, like the\n    default one, still folds normalization) and still refuses as designed.","tree":{"sha":"a84b55f48f018f6d2d010401c3321658b903a5ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/git/trees/a84b55f48f018f6d2d010401c3321658b903a5ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dev-methodologies/ax-template/git/commits/63272eb46aa3559d9e65a9e1db60b26040f5f605","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avat